tRPC","en":"tdd"},"description":{"zh":"tdd AI智能代理提供更好的Auth、tRPC、Drizzle和TanStack Query集成，简化开发流程，提升效率。","ja":"AIエージェントtddは、Better Auth、tRPC、Drizzle、TanStack Queryを統合し、開発をより効率的にします。","ko":"tdd AI 에이전트는 Better Auth, tRPC, Drizzle, TanStack Query를 통합하여 개발 효율성을 높여줍니다.","es":"Mejora tu desarrollo de software con tdd, combinando Better Auth, tRPC, Drizzle y TanStack Query para una autenticación más segura","fr":"Améliorez votre développement de logiciels avec tdd, en combinant Better Auth, tRPC, Drizzle et TanStack Query pour une authentification plus sécurisée","de":"Verbessern Sie Ihre Softwareentwicklung mit tdd, indem Sie Better Auth, tRPC, Drizzle und TanStack Query für eine sicherere Authentifizierung kombinieren","pt":"TDD com Better Auth, tRPC, Drizzle e TanStack Query é uma combinação poderosa para desenvolvedores","ru":"TDD с Better Auth, tRPC, Drizzle и TanStack Query - это мощная комбинация для разработчиков","ar":"TDD مع Better Auth و tRPC و Drizzle و TanStack Query هي مزيج قوي لمطورين","en":"Better Auth + tRPC + Drizzle + TanStack Query"},"definition":{"en":"Better Auth + tRPC + Drizzle + TanStack Query"},"features":{"zh":["更好的Auth集成","tRPC支持","Drizzle集成","TanStack Query支持","简化开发流程","提升开发效率"],"ja":["Better Authの統合","tRPCのサポート","Drizzleの統合","TanStack Queryのサポート","開発プロセスの簡素化","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["Better Auth 통합","tRPC 지원","Drizzle 통합","TanStack Query 지원","개발 프로세스簡素化","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Autenticación mejorada con Better Auth","Combinación de tRPC, Drizzle y TanStack Query","Desarrollo de software más seguro y eficiente","Pruebas y desarrollo combinados","Mejora de la calidad del código"],"fr":["Authentification améliorée avec Better Auth","Combinaison de tRPC, Drizzle et TanStack Query","Développement de logiciels plus sécurisé et efficace","Tests et développement combinés","Amélioration de la qualité du code"],"de":["Verbesserte Authentifizierung mit Better Auth","Kombination von tRPC, Drizzle und TanStack Query","Sicherere und effizientere Softwareentwicklung","Kombination von Tests und Entwicklung","Verbesserung der Code-Qualität"],"pt":["Melhor autenticação com Better Auth","Integração com tRPC para comunicação eficiente","Gerenciamento de estado com Drizzle","Otimização de consultas com TanStack Query"],"ru":["Улучшенная аутентификация с Better Auth","Интеграция с tRPC для эффективного общения","Управление состоянием с Drizzle","Оптимизация запросов с TanStack Query"],"ar":["تحسين المصادقة مع Better Auth","التكامل مع tRPC للاتصال الفعال","إدارة الحالة مع Drizzle","تحسين الاستفسارات مع TanStack Query"]},"keywords":{"zh":["tdd AI智能代理","AI智能代理工具","Better Auth","tRPC","Drizzle","TanStack Query","开发效率","开发工具","如何使用tdd","tdd安装指南"],"ja":["AIエージェントtdd","AIエージェントツール","Better Auth","tRPC","Drizzle","TanStack Query","開発効率","開発ツール","tddの使い方","tddのインストールガイド"],"ko":["tdd AI 에이전트","AI 에이전트 도구","Better Auth","tRPC","Drizzle","TanStack Query","개발 효율성","개발 도구","tdd 사용법","tdd 설치 가이드"],"es":["tdd","Better Auth","tRPC","Drizzle","TanStack Query","desarrollo de software","pruebas y desarrollo","autenticación segura","código de calidad","herramientas de tdd"],"fr":["tdd","Better Auth","tRPC","Drizzle","TanStack Query","développement de logiciels","tests et développement","authentification sécurisée","code de qualité","outils tdd"],"de":["tdd","Better Auth","tRPC","Drizzle","TanStack Query","Softwareentwicklung","Tests und Entwicklung","sichere Authentifizierung","Code-Qualität","tdd-Tools"],"pt":["tdd","better auth","trpc","drizzle","tanstack query","como usar tdd","o que é tdd","tdd vs bdd","instalar tdd","guia de configuração tdd"],"ru":["tdd","better auth","trpc","drizzle","tanstack query","как использовать tdd","что такое tdd","tdd vs bdd","установить tdd","руководство по настройке tdd"],"ar":["tdd","better auth","trpc","drizzle","tanstack query","كيفية استخدام tdd","ما هو tdd","tdd vs bdd","تثبيت tdd","دليل إعداد tdd"]}},"owner":"udecode","repo":"better-convex","repoPath":"udecode/better-convex","stars":364,"forks":25,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T12:18:42Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tdd","description":"Use when implementing complex logic that needs test coverage - write the test first, watch it fail, write minimal code to pass; ensures tests actually verify behavior by requiring failure first; NOT for UI components, simple CRUD, or straightforward code","bodyPreview":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**When to use:** Only for complex logic where bugs are likely, or when user explicitly requests tests.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Use TDD when:**\n\n1. **User explicitly requests tests**\n2. **Complex logic where bugs are likely:**\n   - Complex algorithms\n   - Business logic with edge cases\n   - Da","body":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**When to use:** Only for complex logic where bugs are likely, or when user explicitly requests tests.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Use TDD when:**\n\n1. **User explicitly requests tests**\n2. **Complex logic where bugs are likely:**\n   - Complex algorithms\n   - Business logic with edge cases\n   - Data transformations\n   - Critical paths that could break silently\n\n**Skip TDD for:**\n\n- ❌ UI components (React components, hooks)\n- ❌ Simple CRUD operations\n- ❌ Straightforward mappings\n- ❌ Anything you''re 100% certain is correct\n- ❌ Throwaway prototypes\n- ❌ Configuration files\n\n**Verification alternatives when skipping:**\n\n- Typecheck with `npm run typecheck`\n- Lint with `npm run lint`\n- Manual testing for UI changes\n- Code review confidence\n\n## The Rule (When Using TDD)\n\n```\nWHEN WRITING TESTS: NO CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\n**When you''ve decided to use TDD** (complex logic, user request):\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions when using TDD:**\n\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n**When NOT using TDD** (UI, simple code):\n\n- Write code directly\n- Verify with typecheck/lint\n- Skip the test\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_red -> red [label=\"wrong\\nfailure\"];\n    green -> verify_green;\n    verify_green -> refactor [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_green -> green [label=\"no\"];\n    refactor -> verify_green [label=\"stay\\ngreen\"];\n    verify_green -> next;\n    next -> red;\n}\n```\n\n### RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\ntest(''retries failed operations 3 times'', async () => {\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const operation = () => {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts < 3) throw new Error(''fail'');\n    return ''success'';\n  };\n\nconst result = await retryOperation(operation);\n\nexpect(result).toBe(''success'');\nexpect(attempts).toBe(3);\n});\n\n````\nClear name, tests real behavior, one thing\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\ntest(''retry works'', async () => {\n  const mock = jest.fn()\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(''success'');\n  await retryOperation(mock);\n  expect(mock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);\n});\n````\n\nVague name, tests mock not code\n</Bad>\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n### Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n**Test errors?** Fix error, re-run until it fails correctly.\n\n### GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      if (i === 2) throw e;\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(''unreachable'');\n}\n```\nJust enough to pass\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options?: {\n    maxRetries?: number;\n    backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n    onRetry?: (attempt: number) => void;\n  }\n): Promise<T> {\n  // YAGNI\n}\n```\nOver-engineered\n</Bad>\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n### Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n**Other tests fail?** Fix now.\n\n### REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n### Repeat\n\nNext failing test for next feature.\n\n## Good Tests\n\n| Quality          | Good                                | Bad                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Minimal**      | One thing. \"and\" in name? Split it. | `test(''validates email and domain and whitespace'')` |\n| **Clear**        | Name describes behavior             | `test(''test1'')`                                     |\n| **Shows intent** | Demonstrates desired API            | Obscures what code should do                        |\n\n## Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n- You never saw it catch the bug\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:\n\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n- \"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive\n\nAutomated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:\n\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust. Working code without real tests is technical debt.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower.\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required. You verify remembered edge cases, not discovered ones.\n\nTests-first force edge case discovery before implementing. Tests-after verify you remembered everything (you didn''t).\n\n30 minutes of tests after ≠ TDD. You get coverage, lose proof tests work.\n\n## Common Rationalizations (When TDD Applies)\n\n**Valid reasons to skip TDD:**\n| Reason | Reality |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| \"This is a UI component\" | ✅ Correct! Verify with typecheck/manual testing, skip tests. |\n| \"Simple CRUD, 100% confident\" | ✅ Correct! Verify with typecheck/lint, skip tests. |\n| \"Straightforward mapping\" | ✅ Correct! If truly simple, skip tests. |\n\n**Invalid rationalizations (for complex logic):**\n| Excuse | Reality |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| \"Too simple to test\" | If it''s complex logic, test it. If truly simple, skip is fine. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference, write tests first\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n| \"TDD will slow me down\" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |\n| \"Manual test faster\" | Manual doesn''t prove edge cases. You''ll re-test every change. |\n\n## Red Flags - When Using TDD\n\n**These only apply when you''ve decided to use TDD** (complex logic, user request):\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n**Valid decision to skip TDD:**\n\n- ✅ \"This is a UI component\" - Skip TDD, verify with typecheck\n- ✅ \"Simple CRUD, 100% confident\" - Skip TDD, verify with lint\n- ✅ \"Straightforward code\" - Skip TDD if truly simple\n\n## Example: Bug Fix\n\n**Bug:** Empty email accepted\n\n**RED**\n\n```typescript\ntest(\"rejects empty email\", async () => {\n  const result = await submitForm({ email: \"\" });\n  expect(result.error).toBe(\"Email required\");\n});\n```\n\n**Verify RED**\n\n```bash\n$ npm test\nFAIL: expected ''Email required'', got undefined\n```\n\n**GREEN**\n\n```typescript\nfunction submitForm(data: FormData) {\n  if (!data.email?.trim()) {\n    return { error: \"Email required\" };\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Verify GREEN**\n\n```bash\n$ npm test\nPASS\n```\n\n**REFACTOR**\nExtract validation for multiple fields if needed.\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n**If using TDD** (complex logic, user request):\n\n- [ ] Every new complex function has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n**If NOT using TDD** (UI, simple code):\n\n- [ ] Code is straightforward and you''re 100% confident\n- [ ] `npm run typecheck` passes\n- [ ] `npm run lint` passes\n- [ ] Manual testing confirms UI works as expected\n- [ ] No complex business logic that needs test coverage\n\n## When Stuck\n\n| Problem                | Solution                                                             |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Don''t know how to test | Write wished-for API. Write assertion first. Ask your human partner. |\n| Test too complicated   | Design too complicated. Simplify interface.                          |\n| Must mock everything   | Code too coupled. Use dependency injection.                          |\n| Test setup huge        | Extract helpers. Still complex? Simplify design.                     |\n\n## Debugging Integration\n\n**Bug in complex logic?**\nWrite failing test reproducing it. Follow TDD cycle. Test proves fix and prevents regression.\n\n**Bug in UI component or simple code?**\nFix directly. Verify with typecheck/lint/manual testing.\n\n**Decision criteria:**\n\n- Complex algorithm/business logic → Write test\n- UI component/straightforward fix → Skip test\n\n## Final Rules\n\n**When to use TDD:**\n\n1. **User explicitly requests tests**\n2. **Complex logic where bugs are likely** (algorithms, business logic, data transformations)\n\n**When to skip TDD:**\n\n- UI components (React components, hooks)\n- Simple CRUD operations\n- Straightforward mappings\n- Anything you''re 100% certain is correct\n\n**If using TDD:**\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\n**If skipping TDD:**\n\n```\nProduction code → typecheck + lint pass\nManual verification for UI changes\nCode review confidence\n```\n\n**Only deterministic unit tests** - no integration tests, no complex mocking, no async complexity.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-28T12:47:57.234Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Coding Agents requiring rigorous testing of complex logic, such as those utilizing tRPC, Drizzle, or TanStack Query","zh":"适用于高级编码代理，需要对复杂逻辑进行严格测试，例如那些使用 tRPC、Drizzle 或 TanStack Query 的代理","ja":"Advanced Coding Agents に適しています。tRPC、Drizzle、または TanStack Query を使用するような複雑なロジックの徹底的なテストを必要とする場合に最適です","ko":"고급 코딩 에이전트에 적합합니다. tRPC, Drizzle 또는 TanStack Query를 사용하는 것과 같은 복잡한 로직에 대한 철저한 테스트가 필요한 경우에 최적입니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Codificación Avanzada que requieren pruebas rigurosas de lógica compleja, como aquellos que utilizan tRPC, Drizzle o TanStack Query","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Codage Avancé nécessitant des tests rigoureux de logique complexe, tels que ceux utilisant tRPC, Drizzle ou TanStack Query","de":"Ideal für Advanced Coding Agents, die strenge Tests von komplexer Logik erfordern, wie z.B. solche, die tRPC, Drizzle oder TanStack Query verwenden","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Codificação Avançados que exigem testes rigorosos de lógica complexa, como aqueles que utilizam tRPC, Drizzle ou TanStack Query","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов кодирования, требующих тщательного тестирования сложной логики, такой как те, которые используют tRPC, Drizzle или TanStack Query","ar":"مثالي لعميل الترميز المتقدم الذي يتطلب اختبارًا قاسيًا للمنطق المعقد ، مثل تلك التي تستخدم tRPC و Drizzle أو TanStack Query"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ensure code reliability by writing tests first, utilizing Test-Driven Development principles to validate complex algorithms and business logic with edge cases, particularly in scenarios where users explicitly request tests","zh":"赋予代理确保代码可靠性的能力，通过写测试来实现，利用测试驱动开发原则来验证复杂算法和业务逻辑中的边缘情况，特别是在用户明确请求测试的情景中","ja":"テスト駆動開発の原則を使用して、エッジケースやビジネスロジックを含む複雑なアルゴリズムを検証し、コードの信頼性を確保するために、テストを先に書くことでエージェントに力を与えます。特に、ユーザーがテストを明示的に要求するシナリオで","ko":"테스트 주도 개발 원리를 사용하여 복잡한 알고리즘과 비즈니스 논리 및 에지 케이스를 검증하여 코드의 신뢰성을 보장하기 위해 테스트를 먼저 작성함으로써 에이전트에게 힘을 부여합니다. 특히 사용자가 테스트를 명시적으로 요청하는 시나리오에서","es":"Habilita a los agentes a garantizar la confiabilidad del código escribiendo pruebas primero, utilizando principios de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas para validar algoritmos complejos y lógica de negocio con casos límite, particularmente en escenarios donde los usuarios solicitan explícitamente pruebas","fr":"Permet aux agents de garantir la fiabilité du code en écrivant des tests en premier, en utilisant les principes de Développement Piloté par les Tests pour valider les algorithmes complexes et la logique métier avec des cas limites, en particulier dans les scénarios où les utilisateurs demandent explicitement des tests","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Zuverlässigkeit des Codes sicherzustellen, indem sie zuerst Tests schreiben, Prinzipien des testgetriebenen Developments verwenden, um komplexe Algorithmen und Geschäftlogik mit Randfällen zu validieren, insbesondere in Szenarien, in denen die Benutzer explizit Tests anfordern","pt":"Habilita os agentes a garantir a confiabilidade do código, escrevendo testes primeiro, utilizando princípios de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes para validar algoritmos complexos e lógica de negócios com casos de bordo, particularmente em cenários onde os usuários solicitam explicitamente testes","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить надежность кода, написавая тесты первыми, используя принципы разработки, управляемой тестами, для проверки сложных алгоритмов и бизнес-логики с граничными случаями, особенно в сценариях, когда пользователи явно запрашивают тесты","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على ضمان موثوقية الشفرة من خلال كتابة الاختبارات أولاً ، باستخدام مبادئ التطوير القائم على الاختبار للتحقق من الخوارزميات المعقدة ومنطق الأعمال مع الحالات الحدية ، خاصة في السيناريوهات التي يطلب فيها المستخدمون اختبارات صريحة"},"useCases":{"en":["Validating complex algorithms with edge cases","Testing business logic to prevent bugs","Ensuring code reliability in high-stakes applications"],"zh":["验证复杂算法中的边缘情况","测试业务逻辑以防止错误","确保高风险应用中的代码可靠性"],"ja":["エッジケースを含む複雑なアルゴリズムの検証","バグを防ぐためのビジネスロジックのテスト","高リスクアプリケーションにおけるコードの信頼性の確保"],"ko":["에지 케이스를 포함한 복잡한 알고리즘의 검증","버그를 방지하기 위한 비즈니스 논리의 테스트","고위험 애플리케이션에서 코드의 신뢰성 보장"],"es":["Validar algoritmos complejos con casos límite","Probar lógica de negocio para prevenir errores","Garantizar la confiabilidad del código en aplicaciones de alto riesgo"],"fr":["Valider des algorithmes complexes avec des cas limites","Tester la logique métier pour prévenir les bogues","Assurer la fiabilité du code dans les applications à haut enjeu"],"de":["Komplexe Algorithmen mit Randfällen validieren","Geschäftlogik testen, um Fehler zu vermeiden","Code-Zuverlässigkeit in High-Stakes-Anwendungen sicherstellen"],"pt":["Validar algoritmos complexos com casos de bordo","Testar lógica de negócios para prevenir bugs","Garantir confiabilidade do código em aplicações de alto risco"],"ru":["Проверка сложных алгоритмов с граничными случаями","Тестирование бизнес-логики для предотвращения ошибок","Обеспечение надежности кода в приложениях высокого риска"],"ar":["التحقق من الخوارزميات المعقدة مع الحالات الحدية","اختبار منطق الأعمال لتجنب الأخطاء","ضمان موثوقية الشفرة في التطبيقات عالية المخاطر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Only suitable for complex logic where bugs are likely","Requires user explicit request for tests in some cases"],"zh":["仅适用于复杂逻辑，可能出现错误","在某些情况下需要用户明确请求测试"],"ja":["バグが発生しやすい複雑なロジックのみに適しています","一部のシナリオではユーザーからの明示的なテスト要求が必要です"],"ko":["버그가 발생하기 쉬운 복잡한 로직에만 적합합니다","일부 시나리오에서는 사용자의 명시적인 테스트 요청이 필요합니다"],"es":["Solo es adecuado para lógica compleja donde es probable que aparezcan errores","Requiere una solicitud explícita del usuario para pruebas en algunos casos"],"fr":["N''est adapté que pour une logique complexe où les bogues sont susceptibles de survenir","Nécessite une demande explicite de l''utilisateur pour des tests dans certains cas"],"de":["Nur für komplexe Logik geeignet, bei der Fehler wahrscheinlich sind","Benötigt eine explizite Anforderung des Benutzers für Tests in einigen Fällen"],"pt":["Apenas adequado para lógica complexa onde bugs são prováveis","Exige solicitação explícita do usuário para testes em alguns casos"],"ru":["Подходит только для сложной логики, где ошибки вероятны","Требует явной просьбы пользователя о тестах в некоторых случаях"],"ar":["يناسب فقط المنطق المعقد حيث من المحتمل وجود أخطاء","يتطلب طلبًا صريحًا من المستخدم للاختبارات في بعض الحالات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"276f585a2ae98c6b06889583e27cfff49f0852a25c440418cf7bd6d178b35f97","qualityScore":56}');
