ter un Point de Fin d''Événement d...","de":"AI-Agent-Tools: Hinzufügen eines Outbound-Ereignis-Endpunkts","pt":"Agentes de IA: Adicionar Endpoint de Evento de Saída","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Добавление Конечной Точки Исходящего События","ar":"وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي: إضافة نهاية خارجية للنقطة الناتجة","en":"Adding an Outbound Event Endpoint"},"description":{"zh":"Microbus 教育您的 AI 代理掌握分布式系统，包括架构、模式和操作学科，实现企业级微服务开发","ja":"Microbus を使用して AI エージェントが分散システムをマスターし、エンタープライズ グレードのマイクロサービスを開発","ko":"Microbus로 AI 에이전트가 분산 시스템을 마스터하고 엔터프라이즈급 마이크로 서비스를 개발","es":"Microbus enseña a tu agente de codificación a dominar los sistemas distribuidos y producir microservicios de nivel empresarial","fr":"Microbus enseigne à votre agent de codage à maîtriser les systèmes distribués et à produire des microservices de niveau entreprise","de":"Microbus lehrt Ihren Codieragenten, verteilte Systeme zu beherrschen und Microservices im Unternehmensumfeld zu produzieren","pt":"O Microbus ensina seu agente de codificação a dominar a complexa área de sistemas distribuídos e produzir microserviços de nível empresarial","ru":"Microbus учит вашего кодирующего агента осваивать сложную область распределенных систем и производить корпоративные микросервисы","ar":"Microbus يعلم وكيل الترميز الخاص بك التألق في مجال الأنظمة الموزعة وإنتاج микروسيرفيسات من الدرجة الأولى","en":"Your coding agent can already code. Microbus teaches it to master the complex domain of distributed systems — the architecture, the patterns, the operational..."},"definition":{"en":"Your coding agent can already code. Microbus teaches it to master the complex domain of distributed systems — the architecture, the patterns, the operational discipline — and produce enterprise-grade microservices, every time."},"features":{"zh":["分布式系统架构","微服务开发","操作学科","企业级微服务","AI 代理开发","Microbus 框架"],"ja":["分散システムアーキテクチャ","マイクロサービス開発","オペレーショナルディシプリン","エンタープライズグレードマイクロサービス","AI エージェント開発","Microbus フレームワーク"],"ko":["분산 시스템 아키텍처","마이크로 서비스 개발","운영학","엔터프라이즈급 마이크로 서비스","AI 에이전트 개발","Microbus 프레임워크"],"es":["Arquitectura de sistemas distribuidos","Patrones de diseño de microservicios","Disciplina operativa para microservicios","Integración con Microbus","Soporte para frameworks de mensajería","Implementación de microservicios de nivel empresarial"],"fr":["Architecture de systèmes distribués","Modèles de conception de microservices","Discipline opérationnelle pour les microservices","Intégration avec Microbus","Prise en charge des frameworks de messagerie","Mise en œuvre de microservices de niveau entreprise"],"de":["Architektur von verteilten Systemen","Entwurfsmuster für Microservices","Betriebsdisziplin für Microservices","Integration mit Microbus","Unterstützung von Messaging-Frameworks","Implementierung von Microservices im Unternehmensumfeld"],"pt":["Domínio de sistemas distribuídos","Criação de microserviços de nível empresarial","Integração com o Microbus","Padrões de arquitetura","Disciplina operacional"],"ru":["Освоение распределенных систем","Создание корпоративных микросервисов","Интеграция с Microbus","Архитектурные паттерны","Операционная дисциплина"],"ar":["التألق في الأنظمة الموزعة","إنشاء микروسيرفيسات من الدرجة الأولى","التكامل مع Microbus","أنماط الهندسة المعمارية","التأديب التشغيلي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","分布式系统","微服务开发","Microbus 框架","如何使用 Microbus","什么是分布式系统","Microbus 安装","Microbus 教程"],"ja":["AIエージェント","分散システム","マイクロサービス開発","Microbus フレームワーク","Microbus の使い方","分散システムとは","Microbus インストール","Microbus チュートリアル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","분산 시스템","마이크로 서비스 개발","Microbus 프레임워크","Microbus 사용법","분산 시스템이란","Microbus 설치","Microbus 튜토리얼"],"es":["Herramientas de agente de IA","Cómo usar Microbus","Qué es un punto de fin de evento de salida","Alternativas a Microbus","Microbus vs otros frameworks de mensajería","Instalación de Microbus","Guía de configuración de Microbus","Desarrollo de microservicios con Microbus"],"fr":["Outils d''agent IA","Comment utiliser Microbus","Qu''est-ce qu''un point de fin d''événement de sortie","Alternatives à Microbus","Microbus vs d''autres frameworks de messagerie","Installation de Microbus","Guide de configuration de Microbus","Développement de microservices avec Microbus"],"de":["AI-Agent-Tools","Wie man Microbus verwendet","Was ist ein Outbound-Ereignis-Endpunkt","Alternativen zu Microbus","Microbus vs andere Messaging-Frameworks","Installation von Microbus","Konfigurationsanleitung für Microbus","Entwicklung von Microservices mit Microbus"],"pt":["como usar o Microbus","o que é um agente de IA","microserviços vs monolito","instalar o Microbus","guias de configuração do Microbus","alternativas ao Microbus","framework de microserviços","messagebus"],"ru":["как использовать Microbus","что такое ИИ агент","микросервисы vs монолит","установить Microbus","руководства по настройке Microbus","альтернативы Microbus","фреймворк микросервисов","messagebus"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Microbus","ما هو وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي","ميكروسيرفيسات مقابل مونوليت","تثبيت Microbus","دليل إعداد Microbus","بديل Microbus","إطار عمل ميكروسيرفيس","messagebus"]}},"owner":"microbus-io","repo":"fabric","repoPath":"microbus-io/fabric","stars":170,"forks":5,"updatedAt":"2026-02-22T16:02:26Z","topics":["framework","messagebus","microservices","opensource"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Adding an Outbound Event Endpoint","description":"Creates or modify an outbound event endpoint of a microservice. Use when explicitly asked by the user to create or modify an outbound event endpoint of a microservice.","bodyPreview":"**CRITICAL**: Do NOT explore or analyze existing microservices before starting. The templates in this skill are self-contained.\n\n**CRITICAL**: Do not omit the `MARKER` comments when generating the code. They are intended as waypoints for future edits.\n\n**CRITICAL**: Do NOT register outbound events in `doOpenAPI`. Only functional endpoints and web handlers are exposed via OpenAPI.                        \n\n## Workflow\n\nCopy this checklist and track your progress:\n\n```\nCreating or modifying an even","body":"**CRITICAL**: Do NOT explore or analyze existing microservices before starting. The templates in this skill are self-contained.\n\n**CRITICAL**: Do not omit the `MARKER` comments when generating the code. They are intended as waypoints for future edits.\n\n**CRITICAL**: Do NOT register outbound events in `doOpenAPI`. Only functional endpoints and web handlers are exposed via OpenAPI.                        \n\n## Workflow\n\nCopy this checklist and track your progress:\n\n```\nCreating or modifying an event endpoint:\n- [ ] Step 1: Read local AGENTS.md file\n- [ ] Step 2: Determine signature\n- [ ] Step 3: Determine the method and route\n- [ ] Step 4: Determine a description\n- [ ] Step 5: Define complex types\n- [ ] Step 6: Define the payload structs\n- [ ] Step 7: Extend the trigger and hook\n- [ ] Step 8: Trigger the event\n- [ ] Step 9: Test the outgoing event\n- [ ] Step 10: Update manifest\n- [ ] Step 11: Document the microservice\n- [ ] Step 12: Versioning\n```\n\n#### Step 1: Read Local `AGENTS.md` File\n\nRead the local `AGENTS.md` file in the microservice''s directory. It contains microservice-specific instructions that should take precedence over global instructions.\n\n#### Step 2: Determine Signature\n\nDetermine the Go signature of the outgoing event endpoint.\n\n```go\nfunc OnMyEvent(ctx context.Context, inArg1 string, inArg2 ThirdPartyStruct) (outArg1 map[string]MyStruct, err error)\n```\n\nConstraints:\n- The first input argument must be `ctx context.Context`\n- The function must return an `err error`\n- Maps must be keyed by string, e.g. `map[string]any`\n- Complex types (structs) are allowed by value or by reference, e.g. `MyStruct` or `*MyStruct`\n- All input or output arguments must be serializable into JSON, including complex types\n- Arguments must not be named `t` or `svc`\n- Argument names must start with a lowercase letter\n- The function name must start with `On` followed by an uppercase letter\n- A return argument named `httpStatusCode` must be of type `int`\n- If the return argument `httpResponseBody` is present, no other return argument other than `httpStatusCode` and `error` can be present\n\nThere are three magic variable names that are useful when constructing a REST API.\n\n- An input argument `httpRequestBody` has the request''s body read directly into it. Other input arguments, if present, are read from the query arguments of the request. Use this pattern when an endpoint accepts a single object that is defined elsewhere. Handling a `PUT` request is an example\n- Similarly, an output argument `httpResponseBody` has the request''s body read directly into it. No other output arguments other than `httpStatusCode` can be returned if `httpResponseBody` is present. Use this pattern when an endpoint returns a single object that is defined elsewhere. Handling a `GET` request is an example\n- An output argument named `httpStatusCode` of type `int` will allow the function to set the request''s status code. Returning `http.StatusCreated` after a `POST` request is an example\n\n#### Step 3: Determine the Method and Route\n\nThe method of the endpoint determines the HTTP method with which it will be addressable. The most common approach is to use `POST`.\n\nThe route of the endpoint is resolved relative to the hostname of the microservice to determine how it is addressed. The common approach is to use the name of the endpoint in kebab-case as its route, e.g. `/my-event`.\n\nEvents should be set on a dedicated port to allow blocking external requests from reaching them. The recommended port to use for events is 417. Prefix the route with the port, e.g. `:417/my-event`.\n\nDo not use path arguments in events.\n\nPrefix the route with `//` to set a hostname other than that of this microservice, e.g. `//another.host.name:417/on-something`\n\n#### Step 4: Determine a Description\n\nDescribe the endpoint starting with its name, in Go doc style: `OnMyEvent is triggered when X`. Embed this description in followup steps where appropriate.\n\n#### Step 5: Define Complex Types\n\nIdentify the struct types in the signature. These complex types must be defined in the `myserviceapi` directory because they are part of the public API of the microservice. Skip this step if there are no complex types.\n\nPlace each definition in a separate file named after the type, e.g. `myserviceapi/mystruct.go`.\n\nIf the complex type is owned by this microservice, define its struct explicitly. Be sure to include `json` tags with camelCase names and the `omitzero` option.\n\n```go\npackage myserviceapi\n\n// MyStruct is X.\ntype MyStruct struct {\n\tFooField string `json:\"fooField,omitzero\"`\n\tBarField int    `json:\"barField,omitzero\"`\n}\n```\n\nIf the complex type is owned by another microservice, define an alias to it instead.\n\n```go\npackage myserviceapi\n\nimport (\n\t\"github.com/path/to/thirdparty\"\n)\n\n// ThirdPartyStruct is X.\ntype ThirdPartyStruct = thirdparty.ThirdPartyStruct\n```\n\n#### Step 6: Define the Payload Structs\n\nIn `myserviceapi/client.go`, define a struct `OnMyEventIn` to hold the input arguments of the function, excluding `ctx context.Context`. Use PascalCase for the field names and camelCase for the `json` tag names. If an argument is named `httpRequestBody`, set its `json` tag value to `-`.\n\n```go\n// OnMyEventIn are the input arguments of OnMyEvent.\ntype OnMyEventIn struct { // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n\tInArg1 string           `json:\"inArg1,omitzero\"`\n\tInArg2 ThirdPartyStruct `json:\"inArg2,omitzero\"`\n}\n```\n\nAlso in `myserviceapi/client.go`, define a struct `OnMyEventOut` to hold the output arguments of the function, excluding `err error`. Use PascalCase for the field names and camelCase for the `json` tag names. If an argument is named `httpStatusCode`, set its `json` tag value to `-`. Append the definition at the end of the file.\n\n```go\n// OnMyEventOut are the output arguments of OnMyEvent.\ntype OnMyEventOut struct { // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n\tOutArg1 map[string]MyStruct `json:\"outArg1,omitzero\"`\n}\n```\n\nAlso in `myserviceapi/client.go`, define a struct `OnMyEventResponse` to hold the response of the request. The struct provides a single method `Get` that returns the functions return arguments. Append the definition at the end of the file.\n\n```go\n// OnMyEventResponse is the response to OnMyEvent.\ntype OnMyEventResponse struct { // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n\tdata OnMyEventOut\n\tHTTPResponse *http.Response\n\terr error\n}\n\n// Get retrieves the return values.\nfunc (_res *OnMyEventResponse) Get() (argOut1 map[string]MyStruct, err error) { // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n\treturn _res.data.ArgOut1, _res.err\n}\n```\n\n#### Step 7: Extend the Trigger and Hook\n\nExtend the trigger and hook in `myserviceapi/client.go`.\n\nDefine the route and URL of the endpoint at the top of the file in the respective `const` and `var` blocks. \n\n```go\n// Endpoint routes.\nconst (\n\t// ...\n\tRouteOfOnMyEvent = `/on-my-event` // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n)\n\n// Endpoint URLs.\nvar (\n\t// ...\n\tURLOfOnMyEvent = httpx.JoinHostAndPath(Hostname, RouteOfOnMyEvent) // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n)\n```\n\nAppend the methods at the bottom of the file.\n\n- In the comments, replace `OnMyEvent is triggered when X` with the description of the endpoint\n- Set the value of `method` and `_method` to the method of the endpoint\n\n```go\n/*\nOnMyEvent is triggered when X.\n*/\nfunc (_c MulticastTrigger) OnMyEvent(ctx context.Context, argIn1 string, argIn2 ThirdPartyStruct) <-chan *OnMyEventResponse { // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n\t_method := \"POST\"\n\t_url := httpx.JoinHostAndPath(_c.host, RouteOfOnMyEvent)\n\t_in := OnMyEventIn{\n\t\tArgIn1: argIn1,\n\t\tArgIn2: argIn2,\n\t}\n\t_query, _body, _err := httpx.WriteInputPayload(_method, _in)\n\tif _err != nil {\n\t\t_res := make(chan *OnMyEventResponse, 1)\n\t\t_res <- &OnMyEventResponse{err: _err} // No trace\n\t\tclose(_res)\n\t\treturn _res\n\t}\n\t_ch := _c.svc.Publish(\n\t\tctx,\n\t\tpub.Method(_method),\n\t\tpub.URL(_url),\n\t\tpub.Query(_query),\n\t\tpub.Body(_body),\n\t\tpub.Options(_c.opts...),\n\t)\n\t_res := make(chan *OnMyEventResponse, cap(_ch))\n\tfor _i := range _ch {\n\t\tvar _r OnMyEventResponse\n\t\t_httpRes, _err := _i.Get()\n\t\t_r.HTTPResponse = _httpRes\n\t\tif _err != nil {\n\t\t\t_r.err = _err // No trace\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t_err = httpx.ReadOutputPayload(_httpRes, &_r.data)\n\t\t\tif _err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t_r.err = errors.Trace(_err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\t_res <- &_r\n\t}\n\tclose(_res)\n\treturn _res\n}\n\n/*\nOnMyEvent is triggered when X.\n*/\nfunc (c Hook) OnMyEvent(handler func(ctx context.Context, argIn1 string, argIn2 ThirdPartyStruct) (argOut1 map[string]myserviceapi.MyStruct, err error)) (func unsub() (err error), err error) {\n\tdoOnMyEvent := func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) error {\n\t\tvar i OnMyEventIn\n\t\tvar o OnMyEventOut\n        err = httpx.ReadInputPayload(r, RouteOfOnMyEvent, &i)\n        if err != nil {\n            return errors.Trace(err)\n        }\n        o.ArgOut1, err = handler(r.Context(), i.ArgIn1, i.ArgIn2)\n        if err != nil {\n            return err // No trace\n        }\n        err = httpx.WriteOutputPayload(w, o)\n        if err != nil {\n            return errors.Trace(err)\n        }\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n    method := \"POST\"\n\tpath := httpx.JoinHostAndPath(c.host, RouteOfOnMyEvent)\n\tunsub, err = _c.svc.Subscribe(method, path, doOnMyEvent)\n\treturn unsub, errors.Trace(err)\n}\n```\n\n#### Step 8: Trigger the Event\n\nThe event itself does not have an implementation. Rather, trigger the event from within other endpoints using its trigger.\n\nTo fire an event and wait for zero or more responses, loop over the response channel.\n\n```go\nfor r := range myserviceapi.NewMulticastTrigger(svc).OnMyEvent(ctx, argIn1, argIn2) {\n    argOut1, err := r.Get()\n    if err != nil {\n        return errors.Trace(err)\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nTo fire and forget, call the trigger inside a Go routine.\n\n```go\nsvc.Go(ctx, func(ctx context.Context) (err error) {\n    myserviceapi.NewMulticastTrigger(svc).OnMyEvent(ctx, argIn1, argIn2)\n    return nil\n})\n```\n\n#### Step 9: Test the Outgoing Event\n\nSkip this step if instructed to be \"quick\" or to skip tests.\n\nAppend the following code block to the end of `service_test.go`.\n\n- Do not remove comments with `HINT`s. They are there to guide you in the future.\n- Insert test cases at the bottom of the test function using the recommended pattern.\n- Enter distinct queue names in `sub.Queue` when hooking multiple times to the event to simulate multiple clients\n\n```go\nfunc TestMyService_OnMyEvent(t *testing.T) { // MARKER: OnMyEvent\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tctx := t.Context()\n\n\t// Initialize the microservice under test\n\tsvc := NewService()\n\n\t// Initialize the testers\n\ttester := connector.New(\"tester.client\")\n\tclient := myserviceapi.NewClient(tester)\n\ttrigger := myserviceapi.NewMulticastTrigger(tester)\n\thook := myserviceapi.NewHook(tester)\n\n\t// Run the testing app\n\tapp := application.New()\n\tapp.Add(\n\t\t// HINT: Add microservices or mocks required for this test\n\t\tsvc,\n\t\ttester,\n\t)\n\tapp.RunInTest(t)\n\n\t/*\n\t\tHINT: Use the following pattern for each test case\n\n\t\tt.Run(\"test_case_name\", func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tassert := testarossa.For(t)\n\n\t\t\tunsub, err := hook.WithOptions(sub.Queue(\"queue1\")).OnMyEvent(\n\t\t\t\tfunc(ctx context.Context, argIn1 string, argIn2 ThirdPartyStruct) (argOut1 map[string]myserviceapi.MyStruct, err error) {\n\t\t\t\t\tassert.Expect(\n\t\t\t\t\t\targIn1, expectedArgIn1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\targIn2, expectedArgIn2,\n\t\t\t\t\t)\n\t\t\t\t\t// Implement event sink here...\n\t\t\t\t\treturn argOut1, err\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t)\n\t\t\tif assert.NoError(err) {\n\t\t\t\tdefer unsub()\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tfor e := range trigger.OnMyEvent(ctx, argIn1, argIn2) {\n\t\t\t\tif frame.Of(e.HTTPResponse).FromHost() == tester.Hostname() {\n\t\t\t\t\targOut1, err := e.Get()\n\t\t\t\t\tassert.Expect(\n                        argOut1, expectedArgOut1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\terr, nil,\n\t\t\t\t\t)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t*/\n}\n```\n\n#### Step 10: Update Manifest\n\nUpdate the `outboundEvents` and `downstream` sections of `manifest.yaml`.\n\n#### Step 11: Document the Microservice\n\nSkip this step if instructed to be \"quick\" or to skip documentation.\n\nUpdate the microservice''s local `AGENTS.md` file to reflect the changes. Capture purpose, context, and design rationale. Focus on the reasons behind decisions rather than describing what the code does. Explain design choices, tradeoffs, and the context needed for someone to safely evolve this microservice in the future.\n\n#### Step 12: Versioning\n\nIf this is the first edit to the microservice in this session, increment the `Version` const in `intermediate.go`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:28:35.613Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents specializing in enterprise microservices development that need to implement event-driven architectures.","zh":"非常适合专门从事企业微服务开发的AI代理，需要实施事件驱动的架构。","ja":"エンタープライズ マイクロサービス開発に特化した AI エージェントに最適で、イベント駆動型アーキテクチャを実装する必要があります。","ko":"엔터프라이즈 마이크로서비스 개발에 전문적인 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 이벤트 驅動 型 아키텍처를 구현해야 합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que se especializan en el desarrollo de microservicios empresariales que necesitan implementar arquitecturas orientadas a eventos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA spécialisés dans le développement de microservices d''entreprise qui doivent mettre en œuvre des architectures orientées vers les événements.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die auf die Entwicklung von Unternehmensmicroservices spezialisiert sind, die Ereignisorientierte Architekturen implementieren müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA especializados em desenvolvimento de microserviços empresariais que precisam implementar arquiteturas orientadas a eventos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-агентов, специализирующихся на разработке корпоративных микросервисов, которым необходимо реализовывать событийно-ориентированные архитектуры.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتخصصين في تطوير خدمات مصغرة للمؤسسات والتي تحتاج إلى تنفيذ هياكل معمارية قائمة على الأحداث."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to implement outbound event endpoints using Microbus patterns, ensuring proper event routing and payload structure without exposing events through OpenAPI. This provides foundational infrastructure for event-driven communication between microservices.","zh":"使代理能够使用 Microbus 模式实现出站事件端点，确保正确的事件路由和有效载荷结构，而不通过 OpenAPI 公开事件。这为微服务之间的事件驱动通信提供了基础设施。","ja":"エージェントが Microbus パターンを使用してアウトバウンド イベント エンドポイントを実装できるようにし、OpenAPI 経由でイベントを公開せずに、適切なイベント ルーティングとペイロード構造を確保します。これにより、マイクロサービス間のイベント駆動型通信の基盤インフラストラクチャが提供されます。","ko":"에이전트가 마이크로버스 패턴을 사용하여 아웃바운드 이벤트 엔드포인트를 구현할 수 있도록 하며, 오픈 API를 통해 이벤트를 공개하지 않고 적절한 이벤트 라우팅과 페이로드 구조를 보장합니다. 이는 마이크로서비스 간의 이벤트 驱動 型 통신을 위한 기반 인프라를 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar puntos finales de eventos salientes utilizando patrones de Microbus, asegurando una ruta de eventos y una estructura de carga útil adecuadas sin exponer eventos a través de OpenAPI. Esto proporciona una infraestructura fundamental para la comunicación orientada a eventos entre microservicios.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des points de terminaison d''événements sortants en utilisant des modèles de Microbus, garantissant une routage d''événements et une structure de charge utile appropriées sans exposer les événements via OpenAPI. Cela fournit une infrastructure fondamentale pour la communication orientée vers les événements entre les microservices.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, ausgehende Ereignisendpunkte mit Microbus-Mustern zu implementieren, um eine ordnungsgemäße Ereignisroute und eine Nutzlaststruktur bereitzustellen, ohne Ereignisse über OpenAPI offenzulegen. Dies bietet eine grundlegende Infrastruktur für ereignisorientierte Kommunikation zwischen Microservices.","pt":"Permite que os agentes implementem endpoints de eventos de saída usando os padrões do Microbus, garantindo o roteamento adequado de eventos e a estrutura da carga útil sem expor os eventos através do OpenAPI. Isso fornece uma infraestrutura fundamental para comunicação orientada a eventos entre microserviços.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать исходящие конечные точки событий с использованием шаблонов Microbus, обеспечивая правильную маршрутизацию событий и структуру полезной нагрузки без раскрытия событий через OpenAPI. Это обеспечивает базовую инфраструктуру для событийно-ориентированного взаимодействия между микросервисами.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تنفيذ نقاط نهاية الأحداث الصادرة باستخدام أنماط Microbus، مما يضمن توجيه الأحداث بشكل صحيح وهيكل الحمولة دون كشف الأحداث عبر OpenAPI. يوفر هذا البنية التحتية الأساسية للاتصال القائم على الأحداث بين الخدمات المصغرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing event-driven microservice communication","Adding publish-subscribe capabilities to services","Creating decoupled system architectures","Generating enterprise-grade event payloads"],"zh":["实现事件驱动的微服务通信","向服务添加发布-订阅功能","创建解耦的系统架构","生成企业级事件有效载荷"],"ja":["イベント駆動型マイクロサービス通信の実装","サービスにパブリッシュ-サブスクライブ機能を追加する","疎結合システムアーキテクチャの作成","エンタープライズグレード イベント ペイロードの生成"],"ko":["이벤트 驱動 型 마이크로서비스 통신의 구현","서비스에 발행-구독 기능을 추가하는 것","疎結合 시스템 아키텍처의 생성","엔터프라이즈 급 이벤트 페이로드의 생성"],"es":["Implementación de la comunicación entre microservicios orientada a eventos","Agregar capacidades de publicación-suscripción a los servicios","Creación de arquitecturas de sistemas desconectados","Generación de cargas de eventos de nivel empresarial"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de la communication entre microservices orientée vers les événements","Ajout de capacités de publication-abonnement aux services","Création d''architectures de systèmes déconnectés","Génération de charges d''événements de niveau entreprise"],"de":["Implementierung der ereignisorientierten Kommunikation zwischen Microservices","Hinzufügen von Publikations-Abonnementsfunktionen zu Diensten","Erstellung von Systemarchitekturen ohne Verbindung","Generierung von Unternehmensebenen-Ereignisnutzlasten"],"pt":["Implementação de comunicação por eventos entre microserviços","Adição de capacidades de publicação-assinatura aos serviços","Criação de arquiteturas de sistema desacopladas","Geração de cargas úteis de eventos de nível empresarial"],"ru":["Реализация событийно-ориентированного взаимодействия между микросервисами","Добавление возможностей публикации-подписки в сервисы","Создание несвязанных системных архитектур","Генерация корпоративных полезных нагрузок событий"],"ar":["تنفيذ الاتصال القائم على الأحداث بين الخدمات المصغرة","إضافة قدرات النشر والاشتراك إلى الخدمات","إنشاء هياكل نظام منفصلة","إنشاء حمولات أحداث على مستوى المؤسسة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Microbus framework integration","Events excluded from OpenAPI documentation","Dependent on template structure compliance"],"zh":["需要 Microbus 框架集成","事件从 OpenAPI 文档中排除","依赖于模板结构的遵守"],"ja":["Microbus フレームワークの統合が必要","イベントは OpenAPI ドキュメントから除外される","テンプレート構造の準拠に依存する"],"ko":["마이크로버스 프레임워크 통합이 필요","이벤트는 오픈 API 문서에서 제외","템플릿 구조의 준수를 의존"],"es":["Requiere integración con el framework Microbus","Los eventos están excluidos de la documentación de OpenAPI","Dependiente del cumplimiento de la estructura de plantilla"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec le framework Microbus","Les événements sont exclus de la documentation OpenAPI","Dépend de la conformité de la structure de modèle"],"de":["Benötigt eine Integration mit dem Microbus-Framework","Ereignisse sind von der OpenAPI-Dokumentation ausgeschlossen","Hängt von der Einhaltung der Vorlagenstruktur ab"],"pt":["Requer integração com o framework Microbus","Eventos excluídos da documentação do OpenAPI","Dependente da conformidade com a estrutura do modelo"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с фреймворком Microbus","События исключены из документации OpenAPI","Зависит от соответствия структуре шаблона"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملاً مع إطار عمل Microbus","استبعاد الأحداث من وثائق OpenAPI","يعتمد على الامتثال لهيكل القالب"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"b78468d54b773a4fed463440f08a3fef4c4be6e88b9177aa3a52330a4902a1b2","qualityScore":55}');
