s de desarrollo","Toma de decisiones basada en datos","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo como React y Node.js"],"fr":["Système de gestion de produits modulaire","Assisté par des outils d''IA","Optimisation des processus de développement","Prise de décision basée sur les données","Intégration avec des outils de développement tels que React et Node.js"],"de":["Modulares Produktmanagementsystem","Unterstützt durch KI-Tools","Optimierung von Entwicklungsprozessen","Datenbasierte Entscheidungsfindung","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React und Node.js"],"pt":["Sistema de gestão de produtos modulares","Integração com Ferramentas de IA","Otimização da gestão de produtos","Identificação de oportunidades","Desenvolvimento de produtos personalizados"],"ru":["Модульная система управления продуктом","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами","Оптимизация управления продуктом","Выявление возможностей","Разработка индивидуальных продуктов"],"ar":["نظام إدارة منتجات قابل للتوسيع","التكامل مع أنظمة الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين إدارة المنتجات","تحديد الفرص","تطوير منتجات مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","机会框架","模块化产品管理","如何使用AI智能代理","机会框架安装指南","AI智能代理与传统产品管理的比较"],"ja":["AIエージェント","オポチュニティフレーミング","モジュラー製品管理","AIエージェントの使い方","オポチュニティフレーミングの設定ガイド","AIエージェントと伝統的な製品管理の比較"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","기회 프레임워크","모듈형 제품 관리","AI 에이전트 사용법","기회 프레임워크 설정 가이드","AI 에이전트와 전통적인 제품 관리의 비교"],"es":["herramientas de IA para gestión de productos","cómo utilizar opportunity-framing","qué es la gestión de productos asistida por IA","opportunity-framing vs herramientas de gestión de productos tradicionales","instalación de opportunity-framing","guía de configuración de opportunity-framing"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour la gestion de produits","comment utiliser opportunity-framing","qu''est-ce que la gestion de produits assistée par l''IA","opportunity-framing vs outils de gestion de produits traditionnels","installation d''opportunity-framing","guide de configuration d''opportunity-framing"],"de":["KI-Tools für das Produktmanagement","wie man opportunity-framing verwendet","was ist das KI-gestützte Produktmanagement","opportunity-framing vs traditionelle Produktmanagement-Tools","installation von opportunity-framing","konfigurationsanleitung für opportunity-framing"],"pt":["como usar opportunity-framing","o que é opportunity-framing","opportunity-framing vs jira","opportunity-framing alternative","instalar opportunity-framing","guia de configuração do opportunity-framing"],"ru":["как использовать opportunity-framing","что такое opportunity-framing","opportunity-framing vs jira","опportunity-framing альтернатива","установить opportunity-framing","руководство по настройке opportunity-framing"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام opportunity-framing","ما هو opportunity-framing","opportunity-framing مقابل jira","بديل opportunity-framing","تثبيت opportunity-framing","دليل إعداد opportunity-framing"]}},"owner":"samarv","repo":"Shanon","repoPath":"samarv/Shanon","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-27T01:51:08.479Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"opportunity-framing","description":"Frame customer opportunities as unmet needs, pain points, and desires rather than solutions. Use when writing opportunities for an Opportunity Solution Tree, validating opportunity statements, or training teams to distinguish problems from solutions. CRITICAL for avoiding the #1 OST failure - 98% of people write opportunities as solutions (Teresa Torres). Triggers when user asks to frame opportunities, write opportunities, validate opportunity statements, or check if this is a need vs solution.","bodyPreview":"# Opportunity Framing\n\nTransform feature requests and customer feedback into actionable, specific opportunities that represent true customer needs.\n\n## Core Principle\n\n**Opportunities are needs, not solutions.**\n\nThe #1 failure mode: \"98% of people that write opportunities write them as solutions.\" - Teresa Torres\n\n## Good vs Bad Opportunities\n\n### Bad (Solutions Disguised as Needs)\n- \"We need a better login experience\"\n- \"We need voice input for passwords\"\n- \"I wish this was easier to use\"\n- \"A","body":"# Opportunity Framing\n\nTransform feature requests and customer feedback into actionable, specific opportunities that represent true customer needs.\n\n## Core Principle\n\n**Opportunities are needs, not solutions.**\n\nThe #1 failure mode: \"98% of people that write opportunities write them as solutions.\" - Teresa Torres\n\n## Good vs Bad Opportunities\n\n### Bad (Solutions Disguised as Needs)\n- \"We need a better login experience\"\n- \"We need voice input for passwords\"\n- \"I wish this was easier to use\"\n- \"Add a calendar view\"\n- \"Implement dark mode\"\n\n### Good (Specific Customer Needs)\n- \"It''s hard to enter my password - selecting specific letters on the screen with the Apple TV remote\"\n- \"I can''t see who''s in the cast before I start watching\"\n- \"I don''t know if this show is good without watching 3 episodes first\"\n- \"I lose track of where I was when switching between devices\"\n- \"I can''t tell if I''ve already watched this episode\"\n\n## Quality Tests\n\nApply ALL three tests to validate an opportunity:\n\n### Test 1: Is it specific and actionable?\n- Bad: \"Navigation is confusing\" (too vague)\n- Good: \"I can''t find the search button on the main screen\" (specific)\n\n### Test 2: Does it describe the problem, not the solution?\n- Bad: \"We need better filters\" (solution)\n- Good: \"I can''t narrow down results by release date\" (problem)\n\n### Test 3: Is it grounded in a real customer story?\n- Bad: \"Users want faster load times\" (assumption)\n- Good: \"I gave up waiting for the page to load and closed the app\" (story-based)\n\n## Framing Process\n\n### Step 1: Listen for the raw input\nCustomer says: \"I wish there was a way to skip the intro automatically.\"\n\n### Step 2: Strip away the solution language\nSolution words to remove: \"add\", \"implement\", \"build\", \"create\", \"should have\", \"I wish there was\"\n\n### Step 3: Find the underlying need\nAsk: \"What problem would that solution solve?\"\nAnswer: \"I waste time clicking ''skip intro'' for every episode when binge-watching\"\n\n### Step 4: Make it specific\nGeneric: \"Binge-watching is tedious\"\nSpecific: \"I have to click ''skip intro'' 6+ times per hour when binge-watching a series\"\n\n### Step 5: Validate with the story\nCan you trace this back to a real customer moment?\nYes: \"Tell me about the last time you binge-watched something...\"\n\n## Vertical Depth Pattern\n\nOpportunities should get smaller and more actionable as you move down the tree:\n\n**Level 1 (Big)**: \"I can''t decide what to watch\"\n\n**Level 2 (Smaller)**: \"I don''t know if this show is good\"\n\n**Level 3 (Actionable)**: \"I can''t see who''s in the cast\"\n\nEach level down should:\n- Be more specific than the level above\n- Be a contributing factor to the parent opportunity\n- Be actionable enough to generate multiple solution ideas\n\n## Red Flags\n\nWatch for these indicators that you''ve written a solution, not an opportunity:\n\n- Contains implementation language (\"add\", \"build\", \"implement\", \"create\")\n- Describes a feature name or UI pattern (\"dashboard\", \"calendar view\", \"notifications\")\n- Uses \"should/could/would have\" phrasing\n- Lacks specificity (could apply to any product)\n- Not traceable to a specific customer story\n- Describes HOW rather than WHY or WHAT\n\n## Transformation Examples\n\n### Example 1: E-commerce\n**Raw input**: \"We need product recommendations\"\n**Bad opportunity**: \"Users want personalized recommendations\"\n**Good opportunity**: \"I don''t know what else to buy after adding one item to my cart\"\n\n### Example 2: SaaS Tool\n**Raw input**: \"Add keyboard shortcuts\"\n**Bad opportunity**: \"Power users need keyboard shortcuts\"\n**Good opportunity**: \"I waste 5+ seconds per action reaching for my mouse when I''m in flow state\"\n\n### Example 3: Mobile App\n**Raw input**: \"Implement offline mode\"\n**Bad opportunity**: \"Users need offline access\"\n**Good opportunity**: \"I lose my work when I go through a tunnel on my commute\"\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Pattern: \"I wish there was...\"\nThis is ALWAYS a solution in disguise.\n1. Ask: \"What problem does that solve?\"\n2. Ask: \"Tell me about the last time you experienced that problem\"\n3. Write the opportunity from the story\n\n### Pattern: Stakeholder feature requests\n\"Build feature X\" → \"Why?\" → \"To solve Y\" → \"Tell me about Y\"\n\nExample:\n- Request: \"Build a calendar view\"\n- Why?: \"To help users see their schedule\"\n- Problem: \"I can''t tell if I''m double-booked without checking 3 different places\"\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing an opportunity, confirm:\n\n- [ ] Written as a customer need, not a solution\n- [ ] Specific and concrete (mentions actual UI, steps, or context)\n- [ ] Traceable to a real customer story/interview\n- [ ] Actionable (could generate 3+ different solution ideas)\n- [ ] At appropriate depth (not too broad, not too narrow)\n- [ ] No implementation language (add/build/implement/create)\n- [ ] Passes all 3 quality tests above\n\n## Working with Experience Maps\n\nOpportunities should be organized by the customer''s journey phases:\n\n**Netflix Example:**\n1. Trigger (deciding to watch something)\n   - \"I don''t know what I''m in the mood for\"\n   - \"I don''t have much time and need something short\"\n2. Choosing what to watch\n   - \"I can''t see who''s in the cast\"\n   - \"I don''t know if this matches my mood\"\n3. Evaluating if it''s good\n   - \"I can''t tell if it''s good without watching 3 episodes\"\n4. The viewing experience\n   - \"I have to click skip intro 6+ times per hour\"\n5. Post-viewing experience\n   - \"I forget what happened in previous seasons\"\n\nEach phase contains specific needs and pain points.\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### \"I want\" vs \"I can''t\"\n- Bad: \"I want to customize my dashboard\" (expresses desire)\n- Good: \"I can''t see my most important metrics without scrolling\" (expresses problem)\n\n### Generic vs Specific\n- Bad: \"The app is slow\" (generic)\n- Good: \"The search results take 8+ seconds to load on my phone\" (specific)\n\n### Feature vs Need\n- Bad: \"Users need a dark mode\" (feature)\n- Good: \"The bright screen hurts my eyes when using the app at night\" (need)\n\n## Coaching Prompts\n\nWhen helping others frame opportunities, use these prompts:\n\n1. \"Can you tell me about a specific time when you experienced that?\"\n2. \"What happened? Walk me through it step by step.\"\n3. \"What were you trying to do?\"\n4. \"What made that difficult/frustrating?\"\n5. \"What did you do next?\"\n6. \"How did that feel?\"\n\n## Reference: Teresa Torres'' Quality Standard\n\n> \"I''ve seen blog posts written about how they''re using the opportunity solution tree, and I cry a little bit because their opportunity space is all solutions. I don''t want to knock down somebody''s blog post, but I also don''t want this bad example out there in the world.\"\n\nThe bar is high. When in doubt:\n1. Read the opportunity statement out loud\n2. Ask: \"Is this describing WHAT the customer is trying to do or HOW we might solve it?\"\n3. If there''s any trace of HOW, rewrite it\n\n## Output Format\n\nWhen framing opportunities, use this format:\n\n```\nOpportunity: [Customer need statement in first person]\nEvidence: [Quote or story from customer interview]\nContext: [Journey phase this belongs to]\nParent opportunity: [If this is a sub-opportunity]\nConfidence: [High/Medium/Low based on # of customer stories]\n```\n\nExample:\n```\nOpportunity: \"I can''t tell if I''m double-booked without checking 3 different places\"\nEvidence: \"Last week I showed up to two meetings at the same time because my work calendar, personal calendar, and the team''s shared calendar weren''t synced.\" - User Interview #7\nContext: Schedule management / Planning phase\nParent opportunity: \"I can''t manage my time effectively across multiple calendars\"\nConfidence: High (heard from 8/10 interview participants)\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T02:16:20.522Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Product Management Agents needing to transform customer feedback into actionable opportunities.","zh":"非常适合需要将客户反馈转化为可操作机会的产品管理Agent。","ja":"顧客のフィードバックを実行可能な機会に変換する必要があるプロダクトマネジメントエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고객 피드백을 실행 가능한 기회로 전환해야 하는 제품 관리 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de Gestión de Producto que necesitan transformar los comentarios de los clientes en oportunidades accionables.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de Gestion de Produit ayant besoin de transformer les retours clients en opportunités actionnables.","de":"Ideal für Produktmanagement-Agenten, die Kundenfeedback in umsetzbare Chancen verwandeln müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gestão de Produtos que precisam transformar feedback de clientes em oportunidades concretas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по управлению продуктами, которым необходимо преобразовывать отзывы клиентов в действенные возможности.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إدارة المنتجات التي تحتاج إلى تحويل ملاحظات العملاء إلى فرص قابلة للتنفيذ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to distinguish between true customer needs and solution-disguised opportunities, leveraging core principles like Teresa Torres'' insights to prioritize features effectively, and utilizing techniques such as modular PM systems for AI-assisted product management.","zh":"使Agent能够区分真实的客户需求与伪装成解决方案的机会，利用Teresa Torres的核心见解等原则来有效确定功能优先级，并利用模块化PM系统等技术进行AI辅助的产品管理。","ja":"エージェントが真の顧客ニーズと解決策として偽装された機会を区別できるようにし、Teresa Torresの洞察のような核心原則を活用して機能の優先順位を効果的に設定し、モジュラー式PMシステムなどの技術を利用してAI支援によるプロダクトマネジメントを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 진정한 고객 요구와 솔루션으로 위장된 기회를 구별할 수 있도록 하여, Teresa Torres의 통찰력과 같은 핵심 원칙을 활용해 기능 우선순위를 효과적으로 지정하고, 모듈식 PM 시스템과 같은 기술을 사용하여 AI 지원 제품 관리를 수행합니다.","es":"Empodera a los agentes para distinguir entre las verdaderas necesidades del cliente y las oportunidades disfrazadas de soluciones, aprovechando principios fundamentales como las ideas de Teresa Torres para priorizar características de manera efectiva, y utilizando técnicas como sistemas modulares de PM para la gestión de productos asistida por IA.","fr":"Permet aux agents de distinguer les véritables besoins des clients des opportunités déguisées en solutions, en tirant parti de principes fondamentaux tels que les insights de Teresa Torres pour prioriser efficacement les fonctionnalités, et en utilisant des techniques telles que les systèmes modulaires de PM pour la gestion de produits assistée par IA.","de":"Befähigt Agenten, zwischen echten Kundenbedürfnissen und als Lösungen getarnten Chancen zu unterscheiden, indem sie Kernprinzipien wie die Einsichten von Teresa Torres nutzen, um Funktionen effektiv zu priorisieren, und Techniken wie modulare PM-Systeme für KI-unterstütztes Produktmanagement einsetzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a distinguir entre as necessidades reais dos clientes e oportunidades disfarçadas de soluções, utilizando princípios fundamentais como as ideias de Teresa Torres para priorizar recursos de forma eficaz, e utilizando técnicas como sistemas de gestão de produtos modulares para gestão de produtos assistida por AI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью различать истинные потребности клиентов и возможности, замаскированные под решения, используя основополагающие принципы, такие как идеи Терезы Торрес, для эффективной приоритизации функций, и используя такие техники, как модульные системы управления продуктами для управления продуктами с помощью ИИ.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التمييز بين احتياجات العملاء الحقيقية والفرص المخفية تحت ستار الحلول، مستفيدًا من المبادئ الأساسية مثل أفكار تيريزا توريس لتحديد أولويات الميزات بفعالية، واستخدام تقنيات مثل أنظمة إدارة المنتجات القابلة للتحديث لتدبير منتجات مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي."},"useCases":{"en":["Transforming feature requests into specific customer needs","Prioritizing product backlogs based on actionable opportunities","Differentiating between solutions and true customer needs in feedback analysis"],"zh":["将功能请求转化为具体的客户需求","基于可操作的机会确定产品待办列表的优先级","在反馈分析中区分解决方案和真实的客户需求"],"ja":["機能リクエストを具体的な顧客ニーズに変換する","実行可能な機会に基づいてプロダクトバックログの優先順位を設定する","フィードバック分析において解決策と真の顧客ニーズを区別する"],"ko":["기능 요청을 특정 고객 요구사항으로 전환","실행 가능한 기회를 기반으로 제품 백로그 우선순위 지정","피드백 분석에서 솔루션과 진정한 고객 요구 사항 구별"],"es":["Transformar solicitudes de características en necesidades específicas del cliente","Priorizar carteras de productos basándose en oportunidades accionables","Diferenciar entre soluciones y verdaderas necesidades del cliente en el análisis de comentarios"],"fr":["Transformer les demandes de fonctionnalités en besoins clients spécifiques","Prioriser les backlogs produits sur la base d''opportunités actionnables","Différencier les solutions des véritables besoins clients dans l''analyse des retours"],"de":["Umwandeln von Funktionsanfragen in spezifische Kundenbedürfnisse","Priorisieren von Produkt-Backlogs basierend auf umsetzbaren Chancen","Unterscheiden zwischen Lösungen und echten Kundenbedürfnissen in der Feedbackanalyse"],"pt":["Transformar solicitações de recursos em necessidades específicas dos clientes","Priorizar backlogs de produtos com base em oportunidades concretas","Diferenciar entre soluções e necessidades reais dos clientes na análise de feedback"],"ru":["Преобразование запросов на функции в конкретные потребности клиентов","Приоритизация очередей продуктов на основе действенных возможностей","Различение между решениями и истинными потребностями клиентов при анализе отзывов"],"ar":["تحويل طلبات الميزات إلى احتياجات محددة للعملاء","تحديد أولويات قائمة منتجات معطلة بناءً على فرص قابلة للتنفيذ","تمييز الحلول عن احتياجات العملاء الحقيقية في تحليل الملاحظات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of customer feedback and feature requests","Dependent on the quality of input data for effective opportunity framing"],"zh":["需要理解客户反馈和功能请求","依赖输入数据的质量以进行有效的机会框架构建"],"ja":["顧客のフィードバックと機能リクエストの理解が必要","効果的な機会の枠組み構築には入力データの品質に依存"],"ko":["고객 피드백 및 기능 요청에 대한 이해 필요","효과적인 기회 프레임 구성을 위해 입력 데이터의 품질에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los comentarios de los clientes y las solicitudes de características","Depende de la calidad de los datos de entrada para un encuadre efectivo de oportunidades"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des retours clients et des demandes de fonctionnalités","Dépend de la qualité des données d''entrée pour un cadrage efficace des opportunités"],"de":["Erfordert ein Verständnis von Kundenfeedback und Funktionsanfragen","Abhängig von der Qualität der Eingabedaten für eine effektive Chancenformulierung"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de feedback de clientes e solicitações de recursos","Depende da qualidade dos dados de entrada para um enquadramento eficaz de oportunidades"],"ru":["Требует понимания отзывов клиентов и запросов на функции","Зависит от качества входных данных для эффективного определения возможностей"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لتعليقات العملاء وطلبات الميزات","يعتمد على جودة بيانات الإدخال لتحديد فرص فعال"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"30f866c77a17935b9e64c04fe725c8af9835e779af598193ef0e762c7f028120","qualityScore":55}');
