"ko":"cli는 AI 에이전트를 사용한 멀티 에이전트 파이프라인 개발 도구로써 높은 효율의 개발을 가능하게 합니다","es":"cli ofrece pipelines multiagente para desarrollo asistido por AI, mejorando la eficiencia y productividad","fr":"cli propose des pipelines multi-agents pour le développement assisté par l''IA, améliorant l''efficacité et la productivité","de":"cli bietet Multi-Agent-Pipelines für die künstlich intelligente Entwicklung, die Effizienz und Produktivität verbessern","pt":"A cli é uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento assistido por IA que utiliza pipelines de multiagentes para melhorar a eficiência","ru":"ИИ Агенты и cli представляют собой инструменты для разработки, использующие многоагентные конвейеры для повышения эффективности","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي و cli هي أدوات تنمية مدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي التي تستخدم خطوط أنابيب متعددة الوكلاء لتحسين الكفاءة","en":"Multi-agent pipelines for AI-assisted development"},"definition":{"en":"Multi-agent pipelines for AI-assisted development"},"features":{"zh":["支持多代理管道开发","实现AI-assisted开发","提高开发效率","支持多种开发语言","提供灵活的开发工作流"],"ja":["マルチエージェントパイプライン開発をサポート","AIエージェントを使用した開発を実現","開発効率を向上させる","複数の開発言語をサポート","柔軟な開発ワークフローを提供"],"ko":["멀티 에이전트 파이프라인 개발을 지원","AI 에이전트를 사용한 개발을 구현","개발 효율성을 향상시키는","複数의 개발 언어를 지원","유연한 개발 워크플ロー를 제공"],"es":["Pipelines multiagente para desarrollo asistido","Integración con AI como código","Mejora de la eficiencia y productividad","Compatibilidad con múltiples plataformas","Facilidad de uso y configuración"],"fr":["Pipelines multi-agents pour développement assisté","Intégration avec l''IA comme code","Amélioration de l''efficacité et de la productivité","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes","Facilité d''utilisation et de configuration"],"de":["Multi-Agent-Pipelines für die künstlich intelligente Entwicklung","Integration mit KI-Code","Verbesserung der Effizienz und Produktivität","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen","Einfachheit bei der Verwendung und Konfiguration"],"pt":["Pipelines de multiagentes para desenvolvimento","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento populares","Suporte a linguagens de programação como Python e Node.js","Interface de linha de comando (CLI) para facilitar o uso","Melhoria da eficiência e produtividade do desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Многоагентные конвейеры для разработки","Интеграция с популярными инструментами разработки","Поддержка языков программирования, таких как Python и Node.js","Интерфейс командной строки (CLI) для упрощения использования","Повышение эффективности и производительности разработки"],"ar":["خطوط أنابيب متعددة الوكلاء للتنمية","التكامل مع أدوات التنمية الشهيرة","دعم لغات البرمجة مثل Python و Node.js","واجهة سطر الأوامر (CLI) لتسهيل الاستخدام","تحسين الكفاءة والإنتاجية التنموية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用cli开发","什么是AI智能代理","cli与其他开发工具的比较","cli安装指南","cli开发教程","AI-assisted开发最佳实践"],"ja":["cliを使用した開発方法","AIエージェントとは","cliと他の開発ツールの比較","cliのインストール方法","cli開発ガイド","AIエージェントを使用した開発ベストプラクティス"],"ko":["cli를 사용한 개발 방법","AI 에이전트란","cli와 다른 개발 도구의 비교","cli 설치 가이드","cli 개발 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트를 사용한 개발 베스트 프랙티스"],"es":["herramientas de AI para desarrollo","cómo usar cli","qué es el desarrollo asistido por AI","cli vs otros herramientas de AI","instalación de cli","guía de configuración de cli","desarrollo de software con AI","mejores prácticas para el desarrollo asistido por AI"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour le développement","comment utiliser cli","quoi est le développement assisté par l''IA","cli vs autres outils d''IA","installation de cli","guide de configuration de cli","développement de logiciels avec l''IA","meilleures pratiques pour le développement assisté par l''IA"],"de":["KI-Tools für die Entwicklung","wie man cli verwendet","was ist die künstlich intelligente Entwicklung","cli vs andere KI-Tools","installation von cli","konfigurationsanleitung für cli","softwareentwicklung mit KI","beste praxis für die künstlich intelligente Entwicklung"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","desenvolvimento assistido por ia","pipelines de multiagentes","cli para desenvolvimento","como usar cli","o que é cli","alternativas ao cli","cli vs outras ferramentas"],"ru":["ИИ агенты","усиление разработки","многоагентные конвейеры","cli для разработки","как использовать cli","что такое cli","альтернативы cli","cli vs другие инструменты"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","التنمية المدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي","خطوط أنابيب متعددة الوكلاء","cli للتنمية","كيفية استخدام cli","ما هي أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديلات cli","cli مقابل أدوات أخرى"]}},"owner":"re-cinq","repo":"wave","repoPath":"re-cinq/wave","stars":6,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T21:34:14Z","topics":["agentic-workflow","ai-as-code","multi-agent-systems"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cli","description":"Expert command-line interface development including argument parsing, subcommands, interactive prompts, and CLI best practices","bodyPreview":"## User Input\n\n```text\n$ARGUMENTS\n```\n\nYou **MUST** consider the user input before proceeding (if not empty).\n\n## Outline\n\nYou are a Command Line Interface (CLI) expert specializing in argument parsing, subcommands, interactive prompts, and CLI best practices. Use this skill when the user needs help with:\n\n- Creating command-line tools and utilities\n- Implementing argument parsing and validation\n- Building interactive CLI applications\n- Designing CLI help systems and documentation\n- CLI testing","body":"## User Input\n\n```text\n$ARGUMENTS\n```\n\nYou **MUST** consider the user input before proceeding (if not empty).\n\n## Outline\n\nYou are a Command Line Interface (CLI) expert specializing in argument parsing, subcommands, interactive prompts, and CLI best practices. Use this skill when the user needs help with:\n\n- Creating command-line tools and utilities\n- Implementing argument parsing and validation\n- Building interactive CLI applications\n- Designing CLI help systems and documentation\n- CLI testing and distribution\n- Cross-platform CLI development\n\n## CLI Libraries and Frameworks\n\n### 1. Go CLI Libraries\n- **Cobra**: Powerful CLI framework for Go applications\n- **urfave/cli**: Simple, fast, and fun CLI applications\n- **flag**: Standard library flag package\n- **pflag**: POSIX-compliant flag package\n- **kingpin**: Deprioritized but still useful\n\n### 2. Python CLI Libraries\n- **Click**: Composable command interface creation\n- **argparse**: Standard library argument parser\n- **docopt**: Command-line interface descriptions\n- **typer**: Modern CLI library with type hints\n- **fire**: Automatic CLI generation\n\n### 3. Node.js CLI Libraries\n- **Commander.js**: Complete solution for Node.js command-line programs\n- **yargs**: Command-line argument parser\n- **oclif**: CLI framework for Node.js\n- **meow**: Helper for CLI apps\n- **minimist**: Argument parser\n\n### 4. Rust CLI Libraries\n- **clap**: Command Line Argument Parser\n- **structopt**: Derive-based argument parser (deprecated, use clap)\n- **argh**: Fast and simple argument parser\n- **lexopt**: Minimalist argument parser\n\n## Core CLI Concepts\n\n### 1. Argument Parsing\n- **Positional arguments**: Required arguments in specific positions\n- **Optional flags**: Optional parameters with single/double dashes\n- **Subcommands**: Nested command structures\n- **Environment variables**: Configuration via environment\n- **Config files**: Persistent configuration storage\n- **Validation**: Type checking and value validation\n\n### 2. Interactive Elements\n- **Prompts**: User input with validation\n- **Confirmations**: Yes/no confirmations\n- **Selection menus**: Choose from predefined options\n- **Progress bars**: Show operation progress\n- **Spinners**: Indicate ongoing work\n\n### 3. User Experience\n- **Help systems**: Auto-generated help text\n- **Error messages**: Clear, actionable error reporting\n- **Auto-completion**: Tab completion for commands\n- **Colors and formatting**: Readable output formatting\n- **Consistency**: Follow CLI conventions\n\n## CLI Development Patterns\n\n### Go with Cobra Example\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"github.com/spf13/cobra\"\n    \"github.com/spf13/viper\"\n)\n\nvar rootCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"myapp [command]\",\n    Short: \"My application does awesome things\",\n    Long: `My application is a CLI tool that demonstrates \nbest practices for command-line interface development.`,\n}\n\nvar configCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"config [key] [value]\",\n    Short: \"Get or set configuration values\",\n    Long:  `Get or set configuration values. If only key is provided,\ngets the value. If both key and value are provided, sets the value.`,\n    Args:  cobra.MinimumNArgs(1),\n    Run:   runConfig,\n}\n\nvar (\n    configFile string\n    verbose    bool\n    output     string\n)\n\nfunc init() {\n    cobra.OnInitialize(initConfig)\n    \n    rootCmd.PersistentFlags().StringVarP(&configFile, \"config\", \"c\", \"\", \"config file (default is $HOME/.myapp.yaml)\")\n    rootCmd.PersistentFlags().BoolVarP(&verbose, \"verbose\", \"v\", false, \"verbose output\")\n    rootCmd.PersistentFlags().StringVarP(&output, \"output\", \"o\", \"json\", \"output format (json|yaml|text)\")\n    \n    rootCmd.AddCommand(configCmd)\n}\n\nfunc initConfig() {\n    if configFile != \"\" {\n        viper.SetConfigFile(configFile)\n    } else {\n        home, err := os.UserHomeDir()\n        if err != nil {\n            fmt.Println(err)\n            os.Exit(1)\n        }\n        \n        viper.AddConfigPath(home)\n        viper.SetConfigType(\"yaml\")\n        viper.SetConfigName(\".myapp\")\n    }\n    \n    viper.AutomaticEnv()\n    \n    if err := viper.ReadInConfig(); err == nil {\n        fmt.Println(\"Using config file:\", viper.ConfigFileUsed())\n    }\n}\n\nfunc runConfig(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) {\n    switch len(args) {\n    case 1:\n        // Get value\n        value := viper.GetString(args[0])\n        if value == \"\" {\n            fmt.Printf(\"Config key ''%s'' not found\\n\", args[0])\n            os.Exit(1)\n        }\n        fmt.Printf(\"%s: %s\\n\", args[0], value)\n    case 2:\n        // Set value\n        viper.Set(args[0], args[1])\n        fmt.Printf(\"Set %s = %s\\n\", args[0], args[1])\n    default:\n        fmt.Println(\"Usage: myapp config [key] [value]\")\n        os.Exit(1)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n    if err := rootCmd.Execute(); err != nil {\n        fmt.Println(err)\n        os.Exit(1)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Python with Click Example\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport click\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n@click.group()\n@click.option(''--config'', ''-c'', type=click.Path(), help=''Configuration file path'')\n@click.option(''--verbose'', ''-v'', is_flag=True, help=''Enable verbose output'')\n@click.pass_context\ndef cli(ctx, config, verbose):\n    \"\"\"My application does awesome things.\"\"\"\n    ctx.ensure_object(dict)\n    ctx.obj[''config''] = config\n    ctx.obj[''verbose''] = verbose\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.argument(''filename'', type=click.Path(exists=True))\n@click.option(''--format'', ''-f'', \n              type=click.Choice([''json'', ''yaml'', ''text'']), \n              default=''text'', \n              help=''Output format'')\n@click.pass_context\ndef process(ctx, filename, format):\n    \"\"\"Process a file and output results.\"\"\"\n    verbose = ctx.obj.get(''verbose'', False)\n    \n    if verbose:\n        click.echo(f\"Processing file: {filename}\")\n    \n    try:\n        with open(filename, ''r'') as f:\n            content = f.read()\n        \n        # Process the content\n        result = process_content(content)\n        \n        # Output in requested format\n        if format == ''json'':\n            click.echo(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n        elif format == ''yaml'':\n            import yaml\n            click.echo(yaml.dump(result))\n        else:\n            click.echo(str(result))\n            \n    except Exception as e:\n        click.echo(f\"Error: {e}\", err=True)\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n@cli.command()\n@click.argument(''key'')\n@click.argument(''value'', required=False)\n@click.pass_context\ndef config(ctx, key, value):\n    \"\"\"Get or set configuration values.\"\"\"\n    config_file = ctx.obj.get(''config'') or get_default_config_path()\n    \n    if value:\n        set_config_value(config_file, key, value)\n        click.echo(f\"Set {key} = {value}\")\n    else:\n        value = get_config_value(config_file, key)\n        if value:\n            click.echo(f\"{key} = {value}\")\n        else:\n            click.echo(f\"Config key ''{key}'' not found\")\n            sys.exit(1)\n\ndef process_content(content):\n    \"\"\"Example content processing function.\"\"\"\n    lines = content.split(''\\n'')\n    return {\n        ''lines'': len(lines),\n        ''chars'': len(content),\n        ''words'': len(content.split())\n    }\n\nif __name__ == ''__main__'':\n    cli()\n```\n\n### Rust with Clap Example\n```rust\nuse clap::{Parser, Subcommand};\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse std::fs;\nuse std::io;\n\n#[derive(Parser)]\n#[command(author, version, about, long_about = None)]\nstruct Cli {\n    #[arg(short, long, default_value = \"config.yaml\")]\n    config: String,\n    \n    #[arg(short, long, action = clap::ArgAction::Count)]\n    verbose: u8,\n    \n    #[command(subcommand)]\n    command: Commands,\n}\n\n#[derive(Subcommand)]\nenum Commands {\n    Process(ProcessCommand),\n    Config(ConfigCommand),\n}\n\n#[derive(Parser)]\nstruct ProcessCommand {\n    /// Input file to process\n    #[arg(value_name = \"FILE\")]\n    file: String,\n    \n    /// Output format\n    #[arg(short, long, default_value = \"text\")]\n    format: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Parser)]\nstruct ConfigCommand {\n    /// Configuration key to get/set\n    key: String,\n    \n    /// Configuration value to set\n    value: Option<String>,\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let cli = Cli::parse();\n    \n    match cli.command {\n        Commands::Process(cmd) => process_file(cmd, &cli),\n        Commands::Config(cmd) => handle_config(cmd, &cli),\n    }\n}\n\nfn process_file(cmd: ProcessCommand, cli: &Cli) {\n    if cli.verbose > 0 {\n        println!(\"Processing file: {}\", cmd.file);\n    }\n    \n    match fs::read_to_string(&cmd.file) {\n        Ok(content) => {\n            let result = analyze_content(&content);\n            \n            match cmd.format.as_str() {\n                \"json\" => println!(\"{}\", serde_json::to_string_pretty(&result).unwrap()),\n                \"yaml\" => println!(\"{}\", serde_yaml::to_string(&result).unwrap()),\n                _ => println!(\"{:?}\", result),\n            }\n        }\n        Err(e) => {\n            eprintln!(\"Error reading file: {}\", e);\n            std::process::exit(1);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn handle_config(cmd: ConfigCommand, cli: &Cli) {\n    match cmd.value {\n        Some(value) => set_config_value(&cli.config, &cmd.key, &value),\n        None => {\n            match get_config_value(&cli.config, &cmd.key) {\n                Some(value) => println!(\"{} = {}\", cmd.key, value),\n                None => {\n                    eprintln!(\"Config key ''{}'' not found\", cmd.key);\n                    std::process::exit(1);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]\nstruct ContentAnalysis {\n    lines: usize,\n    chars: usize,\n    words: usize,\n}\n\nfn analyze_content(content: &str) -> ContentAnalysis {\n    ContentAnalysis {\n        lines: content.lines().count(),\n        chars: content.chars().count(),\n        words: content.split_whitespace().count(),\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Interactive CLI Patterns\n\n### Confirmation Prompts (Python with Click)\n```python\nimport click\n\n@click.command()\ndef deploy():\n    \"\"\"Deploy the application.\"\"\"\n    \n    if not click.confirm(''This will deploy to production. Continue?''):\n        click.echo(''Deployment cancelled.'')\n        return\n    \n    with click.progressbar(length=100, label=''Deploying'') as bar:\n        for i in range(100):\n            time.sleep(0.1)\n            bar.update(1)\n    \n    click.echo(''Deployment complete!'')\n\n@click.command()\n@click.option(''--force'', is_flag=True, help=''Skip confirmation'')\ndef delete(force):\n    \"\"\"Delete resources.\"\"\"\n    \n    if not force:\n        if not click.confirm(''This will delete all resources. Continue?''):\n            click.echo(''Deletion cancelled.'')\n            return\n    \n    # Perform deletion\n    click.echo(''Resources deleted.'')\n```\n\n### Interactive Selection (Node.js with Inquirer)\n```javascript\nconst inquirer = require(''inquirer'');\nconst program = require(''commander'');\n\nprogram\n    .version(''1.0.0'')\n    .command(''setup'')\n    .description(''Interactive setup wizard'')\n    .action(async () => {\n        const answers = await inquirer.prompt([\n            {\n                type: ''input'',\n                name: ''name'',\n                message: ''What is your project name?'',\n                validate: input => input.length > 0 || ''Project name is required''\n            },\n            {\n                type: ''list'',\n                name: ''template'',\n                message: ''Choose a template:'',\n                choices: [''basic'', ''advanced'', ''minimal'']\n            },\n            {\n                type: ''checkbox'',\n                name: ''features'',\n                message: ''Select features:'',\n                choices: [''database'', ''auth'', ''logging'', ''testing'']\n            }\n        ]);\n        \n        console.log(''Setup complete with:'', answers);\n        // Continue setup...\n    });\n\nprogram.parse(process.argv);\n```\n\n## CLI Testing Patterns\n\n### Go CLI Testing\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"bytes\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"strings\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"github.com/spf13/cobra\"\n)\n\nfunc TestRootCommand(t *testing.T) {\n    tests := []struct {\n        name     string\n        args     []string\n        expected string\n        error    bool\n    }{\n        {\n            name:     \"help flag\",\n            args:     []string{\"--help\"},\n            expected: \"myapp does awesome things\",\n            error:    false,\n        },\n        {\n            name:     \"invalid command\",\n            args:     []string{\"invalid\"},\n            expected: \"\",\n            error:    true,\n        },\n    }\n    \n    for _, tt := range tests {\n        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n            // Capture output\n            buf := new(bytes.Buffer)\n            rootCmd.SetOut(buf)\n            rootCmd.SetErr(buf)\n            \n            // Set arguments\n            rootCmd.SetArgs(tt.args)\n            \n            // Execute command\n            err := rootCmd.Execute()\n            \n            output := buf.String()\n            \n            if tt.error && err == nil {\n                t.Errorf(\"expected error but got none\")\n            }\n            if !tt.error && err != nil {\n                t.Errorf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n            }\n            if !strings.Contains(output, tt.expected) {\n                t.Errorf(\"expected output to contain %q, got %q\", tt.expected, output)\n            }\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Python CLI Testing\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom click.testing import CliRunner\nfrom myapp import cli\n\ndef test_process_command(tmp_path):\n    \"\"\"Test the process command.\"\"\"\n    runner = CliRunner()\n    \n    # Create test file\n    test_file = tmp_path / \"test.txt\"\n    test_file.write_text(\"test content\\n\")\n    \n    # Run command\n    result = runner.invoke(cli.process, [str(test_file)])\n    \n    assert result.exit_code == 0\n    assert \"lines: 1\" in result.output\n    assert \"chars: 12\" in result.output\n\ndef test_config_command():\n    \"\"\"Test the config command.\"\"\"\n    runner = CliRunner()\n    \n    # Test getting value\n    result = runner.invoke(cli.config, [''test.key''])\n    assert result.exit_code == 0\n    \n    # Test setting value\n    result = runner.invoke(cli.config, [''test.key'', ''test.value''])\n    assert result.exit_code == 0\n    assert \"Set test.key = test.value\" in result.output\n```\n\n## CLI Best Practices\n\n### 1. Command Design\n- Use descriptive command names (verbs are good)\n- Follow Unix conventions (short options, long options)\n- Provide help text and examples\n- Support configuration files and environment variables\n- Handle errors gracefully\n\n### 2. Output Formatting\n- Support multiple output formats (JSON, YAML, plain text)\n- Use colors sparingly and respect NO_COLOR environment\n- Provide progress indicators for long operations\n- Format numbers with appropriate units\n\n### 3. User Experience\n- Implement auto-completion where possible\n- Provide clear error messages with suggestions\n- Use confirmation prompts for destructive operations\n- Support verbose and quiet modes\n\n### 4. Distribution\n- Create single-binary executables where possible\n- Provide installation instructions\n- Include man pages or help documentation\n- Consider packaging for different platforms\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Build command-line tools and utilities\n- Create CLI interfaces for existing applications\n- Design interactive command-line applications\n- Implement argument parsing and validation\n- Add help systems and documentation to CLI tools\n- Test CLI applications\n- Package and distribute CLI tools\n\nAlways prioritize:\n- Clear, intuitive command structures\n- Comprehensive error handling\n- Cross-platform compatibility\n- Rich user experience when appropriate\n- Comprehensive testing coverage"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T01:55:04.525Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Developer Agents requiring advanced command-line interface capabilities for argument parsing and validation","zh":"适用于需要高级命令行接口能力的开发者代理，特别是参数解析和验证","ja":"開発者エージェントが高度なコマンドラインインターフェイス機能を必要とする場合に最適です。特に引数の解析と検証","ko":"고급 명령줄 인터페이스 기능이 필요한 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 특히 인수 파싱 및 유효성 검사","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollador que requieren capacidades de interfaz de línea de comandos avanzadas para el análisis y validación de argumentos","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Développeur nécessitant des capacités d''interface de ligne de commande avancées pour l''analyse et la validation des arguments","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsagenten, die erweiterte Befehlszeilen-Schnittstellenfunktionen für Argumentanalyse und -validierung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvedor que exigem capacidades avançadas de interface de linha de comando para análise e validação de argumentos","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработчиков, требующих расширенных возможностей командной строки для парсинга и проверки аргументов","ar":"مثالي لعميل المطور الذي يتطلب إمكانيات متقدمة لواجهة سطر الأوامر لتحليل وتنفيذ حجة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create interactive command-line tools and utilities using subcommands, implementing argument parsing and validation with libraries, and designing CLI help systems and documentation for seamless user interaction, all while following CLI best practices and utilizing protocols like stdin/stdout for efficient data exchange","zh":"赋予代理创建交互式命令行工具和实用程序的能力，使用子命令实现参数解析和验证，使用库，并设计CLI帮助系统和文档以实现无缝的用户交互，同时遵循CLI最佳实践并利用stdin/stdout等协议进行高效的数据交换","ja":"サブコマンドを使用して引数の解析と検証を実装し、ライブラリを使用し、CLIヘルプシステムとドキュメントを設計して無駄のないユーザーインタラクションを実現し、CLIのベストプラクティスに従い、stdin/stdoutなどのプロトコルを利用して効率的なデータ交換を行うことで、エージェントが対話型のコマンドラインツールとユーティリティを作成できるようにします","ko":"에이전트가 서브 명령을 사용하여 인수 파싱 및 유효성 검사를 구현하고 라이브러리를 사용하고 CLI 도움말 시스템 및 문서를 설계하여 무결점의 사용자 상호 작용을 가능하게 하고 CLI 최적화 관행을 따르고 stdin/stdout 등 프로토콜을 활용하여 효율적인 데이터 교환을 하면서 대화형 명령줄 도구 및 유틸리티를 만들 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear herramientas y utilidades de línea de comandos interactivas utilizando subcomandos, implementando el análisis y la validación de argumentos con bibliotecas, y diseñando sistemas de ayuda de CLI y documentación para una interacción del usuario fluida, siguiendo las mejores prácticas de CLI y utilizando protocolos como stdin/stdout para un intercambio de datos eficiente","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des outils et des utilitaires de ligne de commande interactifs en utilisant des sous-commandes, en implémentant l''analyse et la validation des arguments avec des bibliothèques, et en concevant des systèmes d''aide CLI et de documentation pour une interaction utilisateur fluide, en suivant les meilleures pratiques de CLI et en utilisant des protocoles comme stdin/stdout pour un échange de données efficace","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, interaktive Befehlszeilen-Tools und -Utilities mit Unterbefehlen zu erstellen, das Parsen und die Validierung von Argumenten mit Bibliotheken zu implementieren und Befehlszeilen-Hilfesysteme und Dokumentationen für eine nahtlose Benutzerinteraktion zu entwerfen, während sie den besten Praktiken für Befehlszeilen und den Protokollen wie stdin/stdout für einen effizienten Datenaustausch folgen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar ferramentas e utilitários de linha de comando interativos usando subcomandos, implementando a análise e validação de argumentos com bibliotecas e projetando sistemas de ajuda CLI e documentação para interação de usuário sem problemas, seguindo as melhores práticas de CLI e utilizando protocolos como stdin/stdout para troca de dados eficiente","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать интерактивные инструменты и утилиты командной строки, используя подкоманды, реализуя парсинг и проверку аргументов с помощью библиотек, и проектируя системы помощи CLI и документацию для бесперебойного взаимодействия с пользователем, при этом следуя лучшим практикам CLI и используя протоколы, такие как stdin/stdout, для эффективного обмена данными","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية إنشاء أدوات وبرامج سطر الأوامر التفاعلية باستخدام أوامر فرعية وتنفيذ