t Entwicklungstools","Detaillierte Berichte über Fehler und Schwachstellen","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Programmiersprachen","Benutzerfreundliche Oberfläche"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de projetos com React","Integração com Python e Node.js","Ferramentas de visão de AI para desenvolvedores","CLI para facilidade de uso","Agent para automação de tarefas"],"ru":["Разработка проектов с помощью React","Интеграция с Python и Node.js","ИИ Агент для разработчиков","CLI для удобства использования","Автоматизация задач с помощью Агента"],"ar":["تطوير المشاريع باستخدام React","التكامل مع Python و Node.js","أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي للرؤية للمطورين","CLI لسهولة الاستخدام","وكيل لتحسين المهام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用Vision Audit","什么是AI智能审计","Vision Audit替代品","Vision Audit与其他工具的比较","Vision Audit安装指南","Vision Audit设置教程","AI智能审计工具","开发者工具","项目优化"],"ja":["ビジョン監査の使い方","AIエージェントの監査とは","ビジョン監査の代替品","ビジョン監査と他のツールの比較","ビジョン監査のインストールガイド","ビジョン監査の設定チュートリアル","AIエージェントの監査ツール","開発者ツール","プロジェクトの最適化"],"ko":["비전 감사를 사용하는 방법","AI 에이전트의 감사는 무엇인가","비전 감사의 대체품","비전 감사와 다른 도구의 비교","비전 감사의 설치 가이드","비전 감사의 설정 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트의 감사 도구","개발자 도구","프로젝트 최적화"],"es":["herramientas de visión de código","análisis de código","desarrollo de software","vision-audit alternativa","cómo usar vision-audit","instalación de vision-audit","guias de configuración de vision-audit"],"fr":["outils de vision de code","analyse de code","développement de logiciels","alternative à vision-audit","comment utiliser vision-audit","installation de vision-audit","guides de configuration de vision-audit"],"de":["Code-Review-Tools","Code-Analyse","Software-Entwicklung","Alternative zu vision-audit","wie man vision-audit verwendet","Installation von vision-audit","Konfigurationsanleitungen für vision-audit"],"pt":["como usar vision-audit","o que é vision-audit","alternativas para vision-audit","vision-audit vs outros ferramentas","instalar vision-audit","guia de configuração do vision-audit"],"ru":["как использовать vision-audit","что такое vision-audit","альтернативы vision-audit","vision-audit vs другие инструменты","установить vision-audit","руководство по настройке vision-audit"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة vision-audit","ما هي أداة vision-audit","بديل لأداة vision-audit","أداة vision-audit مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت أداة vision-audit","دليل إعداد أداة vision-audit"]}},"owner":"benjaminshoemaker","repo":"benshoemaker-us","repoPath":"benjaminshoemaker/benshoemaker-us","stars":2,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T05:10:46Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vision-audit","description":"Audit project alignment with VISION.md, identify SDLC gaps, and generate feature proposals. Use when reviewing strategic direction or planning new features.","bodyPreview":"# Vision Audit\n\nA comprehensive audit that evaluates the toolkit against its vision, compares to SDLC outcomes, researches the landscape, and **generates feature proposals** with rationale.\n\nThis is both an audit tool and a **roadmap generator**.\n\n**Key principle:** Focus on *outcomes*, not practices or tools. Proposals should achieve outcomes in ways that align with our principles and differentiate from competitors.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis skill is **toolkit-specific**. It reads the toolkit''s direction","body":"# Vision Audit\n\nA comprehensive audit that evaluates the toolkit against its vision, compares to SDLC outcomes, researches the landscape, and **generates feature proposals** with rationale.\n\nThis is both an audit tool and a **roadmap generator**.\n\n**Key principle:** Focus on *outcomes*, not practices or tools. Proposals should achieve outcomes in ways that align with our principles and differentiate from competitors.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis skill is **toolkit-specific**. It reads the toolkit''s direction documents and generates proposals for improvement. Not synced to target projects.\n\n## Trigger\n\nManual only. Run `/vision-audit` when you want to:\n- Check alignment with vision and SDLC outcomes\n- Get researched feature proposals\n- Understand competitive positioning\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nThe following documents should exist in the repository root:\n\n| Document | Purpose | Required? |\n|----------|---------|-----------|\n| **VISION.md** | Principles, scope, success criteria | Yes |\n| **SDLC_REFERENCE.md** | Outcomes to achieve | Yes |\n| **COMPETITORS.md** | Landscape analysis, differentiation | Recommended |\n\nIf COMPETITORS.md is missing, proposals will lack competitive context but audit will still run.\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n```\nVision Audit Progress:\n- [ ] Phase 1: Parse direction documents\n- [ ] Phase 2: Gather evidence from codebase\n- [ ] Phase 3: Evaluate vision alignment (R/Y/G scoring)\n- [ ] Phase 4: Classify SDLC outcomes (ACHIEVED / AVOIDED / OPPORTUNITY)\n- [ ] Phase 5: Research opportunities (web search + competitor check)\n- [ ] Phase 6: Generate proposals with rationale\n- [ ] Phase 7: Output combined report\n```\n\n---\n\n## Part A: Vision Alignment Audit\n\n### Phase 1: Parse Direction Documents\n\nRead and extract from each document:\n\n**VISION.md:**\n| Section | Extract |\n|---------|---------|\n| Problem | Context (not scored) |\n| Aspiration | Core goal |\n| Principles | Numbered principles (priority order) |\n| AI Strengths | What to leverage |\n| AI Weaknesses | What to guard against |\n| Scope In/Out | Boundaries for classification |\n| Success | Measurable criteria |\n\n**SDLC_REFERENCE.md:**\n- All outcomes by phase (1.1, 1.2, 2.1, etc.)\n- \"Why it matters\" for each\n\n**COMPETITORS.md:**\n- Competitor list and philosophies\n- Feature matrix (what they have vs us)\n- Strengths to learn from\n- Our unique differentiation\n- Gaps & opportunities already identified\n\n### Phase 2: Gather Evidence\n\nScan the codebase:\n\n| Source | What to Look For |\n|--------|------------------|\n| `.claude/skills/` | Skill count, complexity, patterns |\n| `.claude/commands/` | Legacy commands |\n| `README.md` | Feature claims, workflow |\n| `AGENTS.md` | Workflow rules |\n| `docs/` | Documentation coverage |\n| Prompt files | Spec/plan generation patterns |\n\n### Phase 3: Evaluate Vision Alignment\n\nScore each vision item:\n\n| Score | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| 🟢 Green | Aligned — clear evidence |\n| 🟡 Yellow | Partial — mixed signals |\n| 🔴 Red | Misaligned — contradiction |\n\n---\n\n## Part B: SDLC Gap Analysis\n\n### Phase 4: Classify SDLC Outcomes\n\nFor each outcome in SDLC_REFERENCE.md:\n\n```\nACHIEVED     → Toolkit achieves this outcome\nAVOIDED      → Out of scope per VISION.md (with citation)\nOPPORTUNITY  → In scope but not yet achieved\n```\n\n**Decision Tree:**\n```\nDoes toolkit achieve this outcome?\n├─ YES → ACHIEVED\n├─ NO → Is it out of scope per VISION.md?\n│       ├─ YES → AVOIDED (cite the scope exclusion)\n│       └─ NO → OPPORTUNITY (proceed to research)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Part C: Research & Proposals (NEW)\n\n### Phase 5: Research Opportunities\n\nFor each OPPORTUNITY identified, conduct research:\n\n#### 5a. Web Research (Live)\n\nUse WebSearch to find current information:\n\n```\nSearch: \"{outcome} best practices 2026\"\nSearch: \"AI coding tools {outcome}\"\nSearch: \"{specific capability} implementation patterns\"\n```\n\nExtract:\n- Current industry trends\n- How leading tools approach this\n- Emerging patterns or technologies\n\n#### 5b. Competitor Analysis\n\nCheck COMPETITORS.md for each opportunity:\n\n- Do any competitors address this? How?\n- What works well in their approach?\n- What can we do differently/better?\n- Does addressing this strengthen our differentiation?\n\n#### 5c. Principles Filter\n\nFor each opportunity, check against VISION.md principles:\n\n```\n□ Simplicity: Does this add too much complexity?\n□ Flexibility: Does this force a workflow?\n□ 90% Rule: Do most solo developers want this?\n```\n\nIf an opportunity fails the principles filter, mark it as **SKIP** with reasoning.\n\n### Phase 6: Generate Proposals\n\nFor each researched opportunity that passes the principles filter, generate a proposal:\n\n```\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nPROPOSAL: {Short Title}\n─────────────────────────\n\nOutcome Addressed: {SDLC outcome ID and name}\n\nGap: {What''s missing today}\n\nResearch Findings:\n  • Trend: {What current best practices say}\n  • Competitors: {How others handle this}\n  • Differentiation: {How we can do it uniquely}\n\nProposal: {What to build/change}\n\nRationale:\n  • Vision fit: {How this advances our aspiration}\n  • Principle alignment: {Which principles it respects}\n  • Competitive angle: {Why our approach is better}\n\nImplementation Sketch:\n  • Approach: {High-level how}\n  • Files affected: {Which skills/prompts to modify}\n  • Effort: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n\nPriority: HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW\n  {Brief justification for priority}\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Combined Report Structure\n\n```\n╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n║                       VISION ALIGNMENT AUDIT                      ║\n╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n\nSUMMARY\n───────\nVision Alignment:  X of Y items (🟢 N / 🟡 N / 🔴 N)\nSDLC Outcomes:     X achieved, Y avoided, Z opportunities\nProposals:         N proposals generated (H high, M medium, L low)\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nPART A: VISION ALIGNMENT\n────────────────────────\n[R/Y/G scoring for aspiration, principles, AI strengths/weaknesses,\nscope, success criteria]\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nPART B: SDLC OUTCOME COVERAGE\n─────────────────────────────\n[By-phase listing of ACHIEVED / AVOIDED / OPPORTUNITY]\n\n[Coverage summary table]\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nPART C: PROPOSALS\n─────────────────\n\n[For each proposal, full detail as shown in Phase 6]\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nSKIPPED OPPORTUNITIES\n─────────────────────\n[Opportunities that failed principles filter, with reasoning]\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nCOMPETITIVE POSITIONING\n───────────────────────\nSummary of how proposals strengthen differentiation:\n• {Proposal 1} reinforces {unique angle}\n• {Proposal 2} addresses gap vs {competitor}\n• etc.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nRECOMMENDED ROADMAP\n───────────────────\nBased on this audit, suggested implementation order:\n\n1. {HIGH priority proposal} - {one-line rationale}\n2. {HIGH priority proposal} - {one-line rationale}\n3. {MEDIUM priority proposal} - {one-line rationale}\n...\n```\n\n---\n\n## Research Guidelines\n\n### What to Search For\n\n| Opportunity Type | Search Queries |\n|-----------------|----------------|\n| Security | \"shift-left security AI coding 2026\", \"SAST tools modern development\" |\n| Testing | \"AI-assisted testing best practices\", \"test generation tools 2026\" |\n| Context management | \"LLM context management techniques\", \"AI coding context rot solutions\" |\n| Workflow | \"AI coding workflow automation\", \"spec-driven development tools\" |\n\n### Competitive Questions to Answer\n\nFor each opportunity, answer:\n1. Which competitors address this? (check COMPETITORS.md feature matrix)\n2. What''s their approach? (philosophy, not just features)\n3. What works well? What doesn''t?\n4. Can we achieve the outcome with less complexity?\n5. Can we leverage our unique angles (verification-first, cross-model, simplicity)?\n\n### Principles Filter Details\n\n**Simplicity over capability:**\n- Would this add a new skill? (caution)\n- Would this add significant lines to existing skills? (caution)\n- Could this be documentation instead of tooling? (prefer docs)\n\n**Flexibility over guardrails:**\n- Does this force users into a specific workflow?\n- Can users opt-out or skip this?\n- Is this additive rather than mandatory?\n\n**90% rule:**\n- Is this a common need for solo developers?\n- Is this enterprise/team-specific? (skip)\n- Is this niche technology-specific? (skip)\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n### COMPETITORS.md Missing\n\n```\nNOTE: COMPETITORS.md not found.\n\nProposals will be generated without competitive analysis.\nConsider creating COMPETITORS.md for richer proposals.\n```\n\n### No Opportunities Found\n\n```\nAll SDLC outcomes are either ACHIEVED or correctly AVOIDED.\n\nNo proposals generated. The toolkit is well-aligned with its vision\nand SDLC best practices.\n\nConsider:\n- Reviewing COMPETITORS.md for differentiation opportunities\n- Checking if new SDLC trends have emerged (run with fresh research)\n```\n\n### Too Many Opportunities\n\nIf more than 10 opportunities are identified:\n- Prioritize ruthlessly using principles filter\n- Generate full proposals only for HIGH priority items\n- Summarize MEDIUM/LOW in a list without full research\n\n### Research Rate Limits\n\nIf web search is rate-limited:\n- Fall back to COMPETITORS.md analysis only\n- Note that proposals lack current trend research\n- Suggest re-running later for full analysis\n\n---\n\n## Review Your Output\n\nAfter generating proposals, verify:\n- Each proposal was cross-checked against the design principles filter\n- No SDLC outcomes from VISION.md were missed\n- Proposals are actionable and scoped (not vague aspirations)\n\n## Output Principles\n\n1. **Actionable** — Each proposal should be implementable\n2. **Justified** — Every recommendation tied to vision/outcomes/competition\n3. **Honest** — If something doesn''t fit our principles, say so and skip it\n4. **Prioritized** — Don''t overwhelm; rank by impact and effort\n5. **Differentiated** — Proposals should strengthen our unique positioning\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:41:39.481Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Strategic AI Agents needing comprehensive toolkit evaluation and roadmap generation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要综合评估工具包和生成技术路线图能力的战略 AI 代理。","ja":"戦略的 AI エージェントが包括的なツールキット評価とロードマップ生成機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"전략적 AI 에이전트가 포괄적인 툴킷 평가 및 로드맵 생성 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA Estratégicos que necesitan una evaluación completa de la herramienta y capacidades de generación de hojas de ruta.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''IA Stratégiques ayant besoin d''une évaluation complète de l''outil et de capacités de génération de feuille de route.","de":"Perfekt für Strategische KI-Agents, die eine umfassende Toolkit-Bewertung und Roadmap-Generierungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Estratégicos que necessitam de uma avaliação abrangente de ferramentas e capacidades de geração de roadmap.","ru":"Идеально подходит для стратегических агентов ИИ, которым необходима комплексная оценка инструментария и возможности генерации дорожной карты.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الاستراتيجيين الذين يحتاجون إلى تقييم شامل لأدوات وأمكانيات توليد خارطة الطريق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate feature proposals with rationale, comparing toolkit outcomes against SDLC results and researching the landscape, utilizing principles-focused analysis and competitor differentiation.","zh":"赋予代理生成具有合理依据的功能提案的能力，比较工具包结果与 SDLC 结果，并利用以原则为重点的分析和竞争对手区分进行研究。","ja":"エージェントが理由付きの機能提案を生成する能力を備え、ツールキットの結果を SDLC の結果と比較し、原則に焦点を当てた分析と競合他社の差別化を使用して調査します。","ko":"에이전트가 이유가 있는 기능 제안을 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 툴킷 결과를 SDLC 결과와 비교하고 원칙에 중점을 둔 분석 및 경쟁사 차별화를 사용하여 조사합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar propuestas de características con razonamiento, comparando los resultados de las herramientas con los resultados del SDLC y investigando el panorama, utilizando un análisis centrado en principios y diferenciación de competidores.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des propositions de fonctionnalités avec une raison, en comparant les résultats des outils avec les résultats du SDLC et en recherchant le paysage, en utilisant une analyse axée sur les principes et une différenciation des concurrents.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Vorschläge für Funktionen mit Begründung zu generieren, indem sie die Ergebnisse der Toolkit mit den Ergebnissen des SDLC vergleichen und die Landschaft erforschen, unter Verwendung einer prinzipiellen Analyse und Wettbewerbsunterscheidung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar propostas de recursos com justificativa, comparando os resultados do toolkit com os resultados do SDLC e pesquisando o cenário, utilizando análise focada em princípios e diferenciação de concorrentes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать предложения функций с обоснованием, сравнивая результаты инструментария с результатами SDLC и исследуя ландшафт, используя принципно-ориентированный анализ и дифференциацию конкурентов.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من生成 مقترحات الميزات مع مبرر، مقارنة نتائج الأدوات مع نتائج SDLC والبحث في المناظر الطبيعية، باستخدام تحليل مركز على المبادئ والتمييز بين المنافسين."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating feature proposals aligned with project vision","Evaluating toolkit effectiveness against SDLC outcomes","Researching competitor landscapes for differentiation"],"zh":["生成与项目愿景一致的功能提案","评估工具包的有效性与 SDLC 结果","研究竞争对手的格局以实现差异化"],"ja":["プロジェクトのビジョンに沿った機能提案を生成する","ツールキットの有効性を SDLC の結果と比較する","競合他社の状況を調査して差別化する"],"ko":["프로젝트 비전과 일치하는 기능 제안을 생성하는 것","툴킷의 효과를 SDLC 결과와 비교하는 것","경쟁사의 상황을 조사하여 차별화하는 것"],"es":["Generar propuestas de características alineadas con la visión del proyecto","Evaluar la eficacia de la herramienta frente a los resultados del SDLC","Investigar los paisajes de los competidores para la diferenciación"],"fr":["Générer des propositions de fonctionnalités alignées sur la vision du projet","Évaluer l''efficacité de l''outil par rapport aux résultats du SDLC","Rechercher les paysages des concurrents pour la différenciation"],"de":["Generieren von Funktionsvorschlägen, die mit der Projektvision übereinstimmen","Bewerten der Toolkit-Effektivität gegenüber den SDLC-Ergebnissen","Erforschen der Wettbewerberlandschaft für die Differenzierung"],"pt":["Geração de propostas de recursos alinhadas com a visão do projeto","Avaliação da eficácia do toolkit contra os resultados do SDLC","Pesquisa de paisagens de concorrentes para diferenciação"],"ru":["Генерация предложений функций, согласованных с видением проекта","Оценка эффективности инструментария по сравнению с результатами SDLC","Исследование ландшафта конкурентов для дифференциации"],"ar":["توليد مقترحات الميزات المتوافقة مع رؤية المشروع","تقييم فعالية أدوات ضد نتائج SDLC","البحث في مناظر المنافسين للتمييز"]},"limitations":{"en":["Toolkit-specific, requiring access to the toolkit''s direction and principles"],"zh":["工具包特定，需要访问工具包的方向和原则"],"ja":["ツールキット固有のもので、ツールキットの方向と原則へのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["툴킷 특정 사항으로 툴킷의 방향 및 원칙에 대한 액세스가 필요"],"es":["Específico de la herramienta, que requiere acceso a la dirección y principios de la herramienta"],"fr":["Spécifique à l''outil, nécessitant un accès à la direction et aux principes de l''outil"],"de":["Toolkit-spezifisch, erfordert Zugriff auf die Richtlinie und Grundsätze der Toolkit"],"pt":["Específico do toolkit, exigindo acesso à direção e princípios do toolkit"],"ru":["Специфичен для инструментария, требующий доступа к направлению и принципам инструментария"],"ar":["خاص بالأدوات، يتطلب الوصول إلى اتجاه ومبادئ الأداة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3e21098391c73bdabd21181761649779d0d85f5f9142a7e1d4354cd6d9f23041","qualityScore":55}');
