":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: babysit-pr ل Android/Termux","en":"babysit-pr"},"description":{"zh":"babysit-pr 是一个用于 Codex CLI 的调整工具，用于 Android/Termux 的自更新和版本构建","ja":"babysit-pr は Codex CLI のカスタマイズツールで、Android/Termux の自更新とバージョンビルドを実現する","ko":"babysit-pr은 Codex CLI의 설정 도구로서 Android/Termux의 자기 업데이트와 버전 빌드를 실현한다","es":"babysit-pr es una herramienta de AI que mejora la experiencia de Codex CLI en Android/Termux con actualizaciones y construcción de versiones","fr":"babysit-pr est un outil d''IA qui améliore l''expérience de Codex CLI sur Android/Termux avec des mises à jour et une construction de versions","de":"babysit-pr ist ein KI-Tool, das die Codex-CLI-Erfahrung auf Android/Termux mit Updates und Versionserstellung verbessert","pt":"O babysit-pr é um conjunto de tweaks para o Codex CLI no Android/Termux, permitindo atualizações e compilação de versões","ru":"babysit-pr - это набор настроек для Codex CLI в Android/Termux, позволяющий обновлять и собирать версии","ar":"babysit-pr هو مجموعة من التعديلات لتطبيق Codex CLI على Android/Termux، مما يسمح بالتحديث وإنشاء الإصدارات","en":"Codex CLI tweaks for Android/Termux (self-update + build version)"},"definition":{"en":"Codex CLI tweaks for Android/Termux (self-update + build version)"},"features":{"zh":["Codex CLI 调整","Android/Termux 自更新","版本构建","CLI 命令集","Termux 集成"],"ja":["Codex CLI カスタマイズ","Android/Termux の自更新","バージョンビルド","CLI コマンドセット","Termux 統合"],"ko":["Codex CLI 설정","Android/Termux의 자기 업데이트","버전 빌드","CLI 명령어 세트","Termux 통합"],"es":["Actualización automática de Codex CLI","Construcción de versiones personalizadas","Compatibilidad con Android/Termux","Integración con OpenAI","Interfaz de línea de comandos (CLI) intuitiva"],"fr":["Mise à jour automatique de Codex CLI","Construction de versions personnalisées","Compatibilité avec Android/Termux","Intégration avec OpenAI","Interface de ligne de commande (CLI) intuitive"],"de":["Automatische Aktualisierung von Codex CLI","Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Versionen","Kompatibilität mit Android/Termux","Integration mit OpenAI","Intuitive Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle (CLI)"],"pt":["Atualização automática do Codex CLI","Compilação de versões personalizadas","Integração com o Android/Termux","Melhoria da eficiência do desenvolvimento","Suporte a comandos CLI personalizados"],"ru":["Автоматическое обновление Codex CLI","Сборка пользовательских версий","Интеграция с Android/Termux","Повышение эффективности разработки","Поддержка пользовательских команд CLI"],"ar":["التحديث التلقائي لتطبيق Codex CLI","إنشاء إصدارات مخصصة","التكامل مع Android/Termux","تحسين كفاءة التطوير","دعم الأوامر المخصصة CLI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 工具","Codex CLI","Android/Termux","自更新","版本构建","CLI 命令集","Termux 集成","babysit-pr 教程","Codex CLI 使用指南"],"ja":["AI エージェント","Codex CLI","Android/Termux","自更新","バージョンビルド","CLI コマンドセット","Termux 統合","babysit-pr チュートリアル","Codex CLI 使用方法"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Codex CLI","Android/Termux","자기 업데이트","버전 빌드","CLI 명령어 세트","Termux 통합","babysit-pr 가이드","Codex CLI 사용법"],"es":["herramientas de AI para Android","cómo usar Codex CLI","qué es OpenAI","alternativas a Codex CLI","guía de instalación de babysit-pr","configuración de Termux para AI"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour Android","comment utiliser Codex CLI","qu''est-ce que OpenAI","alternatives à Codex CLI","guide d''installation de babysit-pr","configuration de Termux pour l''IA"],"de":["KI-Tools für Android","wie man Codex CLI verwendet","was ist OpenAI","Alternativen zu Codex CLI","Installationsanleitung für babysit-pr","Konfiguration von Termux für KI"],"pt":["como usar babysit-pr","o que é babysit-pr","babysit-pr vs codex-cli","instalar babysit-pr","guia de configuração do babysit-pr","desenvolvimento de aplicativos android","ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","codex-cli para termux"],"ru":["как использовать babysit-pr","что такое babysit-pr","babysit-pr vs codex-cli","установка babysit-pr","руководство по настройке babysit-pr","разработка приложений для android","инструменты ии для разработчиков","codex-cli для termux"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام babysit-pr","ما هو babysit-pr","babysit-pr مقابل codex-cli","تثبيت babysit-pr","دليل إعداد babysit-pr","تطوير تطبيقات أندرويد","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","codex-cli لبرنامج termux"]}},"owner":"Kbediako","repo":"codex-termux-pocket","repoPath":"Kbediako/codex-termux-pocket","stars":1,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T22:48:32Z","topics":["android","cli","codex","codex-cli","openai","termux"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"babysit-pr","description":"Babysit a GitHub pull request after creation by continuously polling CI checks/workflow runs, new review comments, and mergeability state until the PR is ready to merge (or merged/closed). Diagnose failures, retry likely flaky failures up to 3 times, auto-fix/push branch-related issues when appropriate, and stop only when user help is required (for example CI infrastructure issues, exhausted flaky retries, or ambiguous/blocking situations). Use when the user asks Codex to monitor a PR, watch CI, handle review comments, or keep an eye on failures and feedback on an open PR.","bodyPreview":"# PR Babysitter\n\n## Objective\nBabysit a PR persistently until one of these terminal outcomes occurs:\n\n- The PR is merged or closed.\n- CI is successful, there are no unaddressed review comments surfaced by the watcher, required review approval is not blocking merge, and there are no potential merge conflicts (PR is mergeable / not reporting conflict risk).\n- A situation requires user help (for example CI infrastructure issues, repeated flaky failures after retry budget is exhausted, permission pr","body":"# PR Babysitter\n\n## Objective\nBabysit a PR persistently until one of these terminal outcomes occurs:\n\n- The PR is merged or closed.\n- CI is successful, there are no unaddressed review comments surfaced by the watcher, required review approval is not blocking merge, and there are no potential merge conflicts (PR is mergeable / not reporting conflict risk).\n- A situation requires user help (for example CI infrastructure issues, repeated flaky failures after retry budget is exhausted, permission problems, or ambiguity that cannot be resolved safely).\n\nDo not stop merely because a single snapshot returns `idle` while checks are still pending.\n\n## Inputs\nAccept any of the following:\n\n- No PR argument: infer the PR from the current branch (`--pr auto`)\n- PR number\n- PR URL\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n1. When the user asks to \"monitor\"/\"watch\"/\"babysit\" a PR, start with the watcher''s continuous mode (`--watch`) unless you are intentionally doing a one-shot diagnostic snapshot.\n2. Run the watcher script to snapshot PR/CI/review state (or consume each streamed snapshot from `--watch`).\n3. Inspect the `actions` list in the JSON response.\n4. If `diagnose_ci_failure` is present, inspect failed run logs and classify the failure.\n5. If the failure is likely caused by the current branch, patch code locally, commit, and push.\n6. If `process_review_comment` is present, inspect surfaced review items and decide whether to address them.\n7. If a review item is actionable and correct, patch code locally, commit, and push.\n8. If the failure is likely flaky/unrelated and `retry_failed_checks` is present, rerun failed jobs with `--retry-failed-now`.\n9. If both actionable review feedback and `retry_failed_checks` are present, prioritize review feedback first; a new commit will retrigger CI, so avoid rerunning flaky checks on the old SHA unless you intentionally defer the review change.\n10. On every loop, verify mergeability / merge-conflict status (for example via `gh pr view`) in addition to CI and review state.\n11. After any push or rerun action, immediately return to step 1 and continue polling on the updated SHA/state.\n12. If you had been using `--watch` before pausing to patch/commit/push, relaunch `--watch` yourself in the same turn immediately after the push (do not wait for the user to re-invoke the skill).\n13. Repeat polling until the PR is green + review-clean + mergeable, `stop_pr_closed` appears, or a user-help-required blocker is reached.\n14. Maintain terminal/session ownership: while babysitting is active, keep consuming watcher output in the same turn; do not leave a detached `--watch` process running and then end the turn as if monitoring were complete.\n\n## Commands\n\n### One-shot snapshot\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr auto --once\n```\n\n### Continuous watch (JSONL)\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr auto --watch\n```\n\n### Trigger flaky retry cycle (only when watcher indicates)\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr auto --retry-failed-now\n```\n\n### Explicit PR target\n\n```bash\npython3 .codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/gh_pr_watch.py --pr <number-or-url> --once\n```\n\n## CI Failure Classification\nUse `gh` commands to inspect failed runs before deciding to rerun.\n\n- `gh run view <run-id> --json jobs,name,workflowName,conclusion,status,url,headSha`\n- `gh run view <run-id> --log-failed`\n\nPrefer treating failures as branch-related when logs point to changed code (compile/test/lint/typecheck/snapshots/static analysis in touched areas).\n\nPrefer treating failures as flaky/unrelated when logs show transient infra/external issues (timeouts, runner provisioning failures, registry/network outages, GitHub Actions infra errors).\n\nIf classification is ambiguous, perform one manual diagnosis attempt before choosing rerun.\n\nRead `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/references/heuristics.md` for a concise checklist.\n\n## Review Comment Handling\nThe watcher surfaces review items from:\n\n- PR issue comments\n- Inline review comments\n- Review submissions (COMMENT / APPROVED / CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nIt intentionally surfaces Codex reviewer bot feedback (for example comments/reviews from `chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]`) in addition to human reviewer feedback. Most unrelated bot noise should still be ignored.\nFor safety, the watcher only auto-surfaces trusted human review authors (for example repo OWNER/MEMBER/COLLABORATOR, plus the authenticated operator) and approved review bots such as Codex.\nOn a fresh watcher state file, existing pending review feedback may be surfaced immediately (not only comments that arrive after monitoring starts). This is intentional so already-open review comments are not missed.\n\nWhen you agree with a comment and it is actionable:\n\n1. Patch code locally.\n2. Commit with `codex: address PR review feedback (#<n>)`.\n3. Push to the PR head branch.\n4. Resume watching on the new SHA immediately (do not stop after reporting the push).\n5. If monitoring was running in `--watch` mode, restart `--watch` immediately after the push in the same turn; do not wait for the user to ask again.\n\nIf you disagree or the comment is non-actionable/already addressed, record it as handled by continuing the watcher loop (the script de-duplicates surfaced items via state after surfacing them).\nIf a code review comment/thread is already marked as resolved in GitHub, treat it as non-actionable and safely ignore it unless new unresolved follow-up feedback appears.\n\n## Git Safety Rules\n\n- Work only on the PR head branch.\n- Avoid destructive git commands.\n- Do not switch branches unless necessary to recover context.\n- Before editing, check for unrelated uncommitted changes. If present, stop and ask the user.\n- After each successful fix, commit and `git push`, then re-run the watcher.\n- If you interrupted a live `--watch` session to make the fix, restart `--watch` immediately after the push in the same turn.\n- Do not run multiple concurrent `--watch` processes for the same PR/state file; keep one watcher session active and reuse it until it stops or you intentionally restart it.\n- A push is not a terminal outcome; continue the monitoring loop unless a strict stop condition is met.\n\nCommit message defaults:\n\n- `codex: fix CI failure on PR #<n>`\n- `codex: address PR review feedback (#<n>)`\n\n## Monitoring Loop Pattern\nUse this loop in a live Codex session:\n\n1. Run `--once`.\n2. Read `actions`.\n3. First check whether the PR is now merged or otherwise closed; if so, report that terminal state and stop polling immediately.\n4. Check CI summary, new review items, and mergeability/conflict status.\n5. Diagnose CI failures and classify branch-related vs flaky/unrelated.\n6. Process actionable review comments before flaky reruns when both are present; if a review fix requires a commit, push it and skip rerunning failed checks on the old SHA.\n7. Retry failed checks only when `retry_failed_checks` is present and you are not about to replace the current SHA with a review/CI fix commit.\n8. If you pushed a commit or triggered a rerun, report the action briefly and continue polling (do not stop).\n9. After a review-fix push, proactively restart continuous monitoring (`--watch`) in the same turn unless a strict stop condition has already been reached.\n10. If everything is passing, mergeable, not blocked on required review approval, and there are no unaddressed review items, report success and stop.\n11. If blocked on a user-help-required issue (infra outage, exhausted flaky retries, unclear reviewer request, permissions), report the blocker and stop.\n12. Otherwise sleep according to the polling cadence below and repeat.\n\nWhen the user explicitly asks to monitor/watch/babysit a PR, prefer `--watch` so polling continues autonomously in one command. Use repeated `--once` snapshots only for debugging, local testing, or when the user explicitly asks for a one-shot check.\nDo not stop to ask the user whether to continue polling; continue autonomously until a strict stop condition is met or the user explicitly interrupts.\nDo not hand control back to the user after a review-fix push just because a new SHA was created; restarting the watcher and re-entering the poll loop is part of the same babysitting task.\nIf a `--watch` process is still running and no strict stop condition has been reached, the babysitting task is still in progress; keep streaming/consuming watcher output instead of ending the turn.\n\n## Polling Cadence\nUse adaptive polling and continue monitoring even after CI turns green:\n\n- While CI is not green (pending/running/queued or failing): poll every 1 minute.\n- After CI turns green: start at every 1 minute, then back off exponentially when there is no change (for example 1m, 2m, 4m, 8m, 16m, 32m), capping at every 1 hour.\n- Reset the green-state polling interval back to 1 minute whenever anything changes (new commit/SHA, check status changes, new review comments, mergeability changes, review decision changes).\n- If CI stops being green again (new commit, rerun, or regression): return to 1-minute polling.\n- If any poll shows the PR is merged or otherwise closed: stop polling immediately and report the terminal state.\n\n## Stop Conditions (Strict)\nStop only when one of the following is true:\n\n- PR merged or closed (stop as soon as a poll/snapshot confirms this).\n- PR is ready to merge: CI succeeded, no surfaced unaddressed review comments, not blocked on required review approval, and no merge conflict risk.\n- User intervention is required and Codex cannot safely proceed alone.\n\nKeep polling when:\n\n- `actions` contains only `idle` but checks are still pending.\n- CI is still running/queued.\n- Review state is quiet but CI is not terminal.\n- CI is green but mergeability is unknown/pending.\n- CI is green and mergeable, but the PR is still open and you are waiting for possible new review comments or merge-conflict changes per the green-state cadence.\n- The PR is green but blocked on review approval (`REVIEW_REQUIRED` / similar); continue polling on the green-state cadence and surface any new review comments without asking for confirmation to keep watching.\n\n## Output Expectations\nProvide concise progress updates while monitoring and a final summary that includes:\n\n- During long unchanged monitoring periods, avoid emitting a full update on every poll; summarize only status changes plus occasional heartbeat updates.\n- Treat push confirmations, intermediate CI snapshots, and review-action updates as progress updates only; do not emit the final summary or end the babysitting session unless a strict stop condition is met.\n- A user request to \"monitor\" is not satisfied by a couple of sample polls; remain in the loop until a strict stop condition or an explicit user interruption.\n- A review-fix commit + push is not a completion event; immediately resume live monitoring (`--watch`) in the same turn and continue reporting progress updates.\n- When CI first transitions to all green for the current SHA, emit a one-time celebratory progress update (do not repeat it on every green poll). Preferred style: `🚀 CI is all green! 33/33 passed. Still on watch for review approval.`\n- Do not send the final summary while a watcher terminal is still running unless the watcher has emitted/confirmed a strict stop condition; otherwise continue with progress updates.\n\n- Final PR SHA\n- CI status summary\n- Mergeability / conflict status\n- Fixes pushed\n- Flaky retry cycles used\n- Remaining unresolved failures or review comments\n\n## References\n\n- Heuristics and decision tree: `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/references/heuristics.md`\n- GitHub CLI/API details used by the watcher: `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/references/github-api-notes.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T01:59:45.232Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for GitHub Agents needing persistent PR monitoring and automation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要持续PR监控和自动化能力的GitHub代理。","ja":"GitHubエージェントが持続的なPRモニタリングと自動化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"지속적인 PR 모니터링 및 자동화 기능이 필요한 GitHub 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de GitHub que necesitan un monitoreo y capacidades de automatización de PR persistentes.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents GitHub ayant besoin d''un suivi et de capacités d''automatisation de PR persistants.","de":"Perfekt für GitHub-Agents, die ein persistentes PR-Monitoring und Automatisierungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes do GitHub que precisam de monitoramento e capacidades de automação de PR persistentes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов GitHub, требующих постоянного мониторинга и автоматизации возможностей PR.","ar":"مثالي لعميل GitHub الذين يحتاجون إلى مراقبة وآليّة مستمرة لمراجعة الطلبات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to persistently babysit PRs until merge or closure, leveraging CI success, review comment resolution, and merge conflict avoidance using Termux and Codex CLI tweaks for Android.","zh":"赋予代理持续监控PR直到合并或关闭的能力，利用CI成功、审查评论解决和合并冲突避免使用Termux和Codex CLI调整 для Android。","ja":"エージェントに、CIの成功、レビューコメントの解決、MergeConflictの回避を使用して、PRをマージまたはクローズするまで持続的に監視する能力を与えます。TermuxとCodex CLIの調整を使用してAndroidで実行します。","ko":"에이전트가 PR을 병합 또는 닫힐 때까지 지속적으로 모니터링 할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. CI 성공, 리뷰评论 해결 및 병합 충돌 방지를 위해 Termux 및 Codex CLI 조정을 사용하여 Android에서 실행합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a vigilar persistentemente las PR hasta la fusión o cierre, aprovechando el éxito de CI, la resolución de comentarios de revisión y la evitación de conflictos de fusión utilizando ajustes de Termux y Codex CLI para Android.","fr":"Permet aux agents de surveiller en permanence les PR jusqu''à la fusion ou la fermeture, en exploitant la réussite de CI, la résolution des commentaires d''examen et l''évitement des conflits de fusion en utilisant des ajustements de Termux et de Codex CLI pour Android.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, PRs bis zum Merge oder zur Schließung persistent zu überwachen, indem es den CI-Erfolg, die Auflösung von Überprüfungskommentaren und die Vermeidung von Merge-Konflikten unter Verwendung von Termux- und Codex-CLI-Anpassungen für Android nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a supervisionar persistentemente as PRs até a mesclagem ou fechamento, aproveitando o sucesso do CI, a resolução de comentários de revisão e a evasão de conflitos de mesclagem usando ajustes do Termux e do Codex CLI para Android.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью постоянно следить за PR до слияния или закрытия, используя успех CI, разрешение комментариев к обзору и избежание конфликтов слияния с помощью настроек Termux и Codex CLI для Android.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على مراقبة استمرارية طلبات المراجعة حتى الاندماج أو الإغلاق، واستخدام نجاح CI وحل التعليقات المراجعة وتجنب صراعات الاندماج باستخدام تعديلات Termux و Codex CLI لمنصة Android."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating PR monitoring for merge readiness","Debugging CI infrastructure issues and flaky failures","Resolving potential merge conflicts and permission issues"],"zh":["自动化PR监控以准备合并","调试CI基础架构问题和不稳定故障","解决潜在的合并冲突和权限问题"],"ja":["マージの準備のためにPRモニタリングを自動化する","CIインフラストラクチャの問題とフレイクィーフェイルをデバッグする","潜在的なマージコンフリクトとパーミッションの問題を解決する"],"ko":["병합 준비를 위한 PR 모니터링 자동화","CI 인프라스트럭처 문제 및 가변 실패 디버깅","潜在的な 병합 충돌 및 권한 문제 해결"],"es":["Automatización del monitoreo de PR para la preparación para la fusión","Depuración de problemas de infraestructura de CI y fallos poco fiables","Resolución de conflictos de fusión y problemas de permisos potenciales"],"fr":["Automatisation du suivi des PR pour la préparation à la fusion","Débogage des problèmes d''infrastructure de CI et des défaillances peu fiables","Résolution des conflits de fusion et des problèmes de permissions potentiels"],"de":["Automatisierung der PR-Überwachung für die Merge-Bereitschaft","Fehlerbehebung bei CI-Infrastrukturproblemen und fehlerhaften Fehlern","Auflösung von Merge-Konflikten und potenziellen Berechtigungsproblemen"],"pt":["Automatizar a monitoração de PR para prontidão de mesclagem","Depurar problemas de infraestrutura de CI e falhas intermitentes","Resolver possíveis conflitos de mesclagem e problemas de permissão"],"ru":["Автоматизировать мониторинг PR для готовности к слиянию","Отладить проблемы инфраструктуры CI и промежуточные сбои","Разрешить потенциальные конфликты слияния и проблемы с разрешениями"],"ar":["آليّة مراقبة طلبات المراجعة لجاهزیة الدمج","تصحيح مشكلات بنية CI والفشل المتقطع","حل النزاعات المحتملة للاندماج ومشاكل الصلاحيات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub API access","Limited to PRs with accessible CI infrastructure","Dependent on Termux and Codex CLI compatibility"],"zh":["需要GitHub API访问","仅限于具有可访问CI基础架构的PR","依赖Termux和Codex CLI兼容性"],"ja":["GitHub APIへのアクセスが必要","アクセス可能なCIインフラストラクチャを持つPRのみ","TermuxとCodex CLIの互換性に依存"],"ko":["GitHub API 액세스가 필요함","액세스 가능한 CI 인프라스트럭처를 갖춘 PR에만 제한됨","Termux 및 Codex CLI 호환성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la API de GitHub","Limitado a PR con infraestructura de CI accesible","Dependiente de la compatibilidad de Termux y Codex CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''API GitHub","Limité aux PR avec une infrastructure de CI accessible","Dépend de la compatibilité de Termux et de Codex CLI"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die GitHub-API","Begrenzt auf PR mit zugänglicher CI-Infrastruktur","Abhängig von der Kompatibilität von Termux und Codex CLI"],"pt":["Requer acesso à API do GitHub","Limitado a PRs com infraestrutura de CI acessível","Dependente da compatibilidade do Termux e do Codex CLI"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к API GitHub","Ограничен до PR с доступной инфраструктурой CI","Зависит от совместимости Termux и Codex CLI"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات GitHub","محدود لطلبات المراجعة ببنية CI قابلة للوصول","اعتماد على توافق Termux و Codex CLI"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"165e7c05a4d5a7d1ba58afca15c3539f48b2b0cf0c3c251a0e644b2a1434ecf5","qualityScore":55}');
