+のクローン版、クロスプラットフォームのメモ機能を提供","ko":"Rust 크로스 플랫폼 메모장은 Notepad++의 클론 버전으로, 크로스 플랫폼의 메모 기능을 제공","es":"Rust es una herramienta de notas de código abierto inspirada en Notepad++, diseñada para proporcionar una experiencia de escritura eficiente en múltiples pla...","fr":"Rust est un outil de notes open source inspiré de Notepad++, conçu pour offrir une expérience d''écriture efficace sur plusieurs plateformes","de":"Rust ist ein Open-Source-Notiztool inspiriert von Notepad++, entwickelt für eine effiziente Schreibweise auf mehreren Plattformen","pt":"A ferramenta Rust é um notepad de código aberto inspirado no Notepad++, com funcionalidades de edição de texto avançadas","ru":"ИИ Агент Rust - кроссплатформенный блокнот, вдохновленный Notepad++, с расширенными функциями редактирования текста","ar":"أداة الرست هي محرر نصوص مفتوح المصدر مستوحى من برنامج Notepad++، مع ميزات تحرير متقدمة","en":"Cross-platform Notepad inspired by Notepad++"},"definition":{"en":"Cross-platform Notepad inspired by Notepad++"},"features":{"zh":["跨平台支持","灵感来自Notepad++","提供便捷的笔记功能","基于Rust开发","支持多种操作系统"],"ja":["クロスプラットフォーム対応","Notepad++からインスピレーションを得た","便利なメモ機能を提供","Rustで開発された","複数のオペレーティングシステムをサポート"],"ko":["크로스 플랫폼 지원","Notepad++에서 영감을 받은","편리한 메모 기능을 제공","Rust로 개발된","다중 운영 체제 지원"],"es":["Interfaz gráfica de usuario intuitiva","Compatibilidad con múltiples plataformas","Edición de texto avanzada","Soporte para notas y organización","Personalización de la interfaz"],"fr":["Interface graphique utilisateur intuitive","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes","Édition de texte avancée","Prise en charge des notes et de l''organisation","Personnalisation de l''interface"],"de":["Intuitive Benutzeroberfläche","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen","Erweiterte Textbearbeitung","Unterstützung für Notizen und Organisation","Anpassung der Oberfläche"],"pt":["Edição de texto avançada","Compatibilidade com múltiplas plataformas","Inspiração no Notepad++","Código aberto","Ferramenta de notas eficaz"],"ru":["Расширенное редактирование текста","Кроссплатформенность","Вдохновлен Notepad++","Открытый код","Эффективный инструмент для заметок"],"ar":["تحرير نص متقدم","توافق مع الأنظمة المختلفة","مستوحى من برنامج Notepad++","مفتوح المصدر","أداة ملاحظات فعالة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust跨平台记事本","Notepad++替代品","如何使用Rust记事本","Rust记事本安装","Rust记事本设置指南","跨平台笔记工具","Rust开发工具","笔记软件比较"],"ja":["Rustクロスプラットフォームメモ帳","Notepad++の代替","Rustメモ帳の使い方","Rustメモ帳のインストール","Rustメモ帳の設定ガイド","クロスプラットフォームのメモツール","Rust開発ツール","メモソフトの比較"],"ko":["Rust 크로스 플랫폼 메모장","Notepad++ 대체","Rust 메모장 사용법","Rust 메모장 설치","Rust 메모장 설정 가이드","크로스 플랫폼 메모 도구","Rust 개발 도구","메모 소프트웨어 비교"],"es":["herramientas de AI","Rust vs Notepad++","cómo usar Rust","guía de instalación de Rust","alternativas a Notepad++","Rust para desarrolladores","gui de Rust","notas en Rust","configuración de Rust"],"fr":["outils d''IA","Rust vs Notepad++","comment utiliser Rust","guide d''installation de Rust","alternatives à Notepad++","Rust pour les développeurs","interface graphique de Rust","notes dans Rust","configuration de Rust"],"de":["KI-Tools","Rust vs Notepad++","wie man Rust verwendet","Rust-Installationsanleitung","Alternativen zu Notepad++","Rust für Entwickler","Rust-Oberfläche","Notizen in Rust","Rust-Konfiguration"],"pt":["como usar a ferramenta Rust","o que é a ferramenta Rust","Rust vs Notepad++","alternativa ao Notepad++","instalar a ferramenta Rust","guia de configuração da ferramenta Rust","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агент Rust","что такое ИИ Агент Rust","Rust vs Notepad++","альтернатива Notepad++","установка ИИ Агента Rust","руководство по настройке ИИ Агента Rust","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة الرست","ما هي أداة الرست","الرست مقابل برنامج Notepad++","بديل لبرنامج Notepad++","تثبيت أداة الرست","دليل إعداد أداة الرست","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"brenordv","repo":"rust-pad","repoPath":"brenordv/rust-pad","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T06:29:36Z","topics":["gui","notebook","notepad","notepad-plus-plus","notes","tools"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust","description":"Write production-quality Rust code following industry best practices and idiomatic patterns. Use for any Rust coding task including applications, libraries, refactoring, debugging, or code review — with particular expertise in cross-platform GUI development.","bodyPreview":"## Instructions\n\n### 1. Planning & Analysis\n\n**Before writing any code:**\n- Understand the full requirements and constraints\n- Review the existing codebase for conventions, utilities, and patterns already in use\n- Check for shared/common modules before creating new utilities\n- Consider edge cases within reason unless the user specifically asks for more\n- For GUI work: identify which platforms are targeted and any platform-specific constraints\n\n### 2. Design Principles\n\n**Rust-Specific:**\n- Prefe","body":"## Instructions\n\n### 1. Planning & Analysis\n\n**Before writing any code:**\n- Understand the full requirements and constraints\n- Review the existing codebase for conventions, utilities, and patterns already in use\n- Check for shared/common modules before creating new utilities\n- Consider edge cases within reason unless the user specifically asks for more\n- For GUI work: identify which platforms are targeted and any platform-specific constraints\n\n### 2. Design Principles\n\n**Rust-Specific:**\n- Prefer borrowing over cloning; pass `&str` not `&String`, `&Path` not `&PathBuf`, `&[T]` not `&Vec<T>`\n- Use enums, newtypes, and the type system to make illegal states unrepresentable\n- Parse raw input into well-typed structures at the boundary, then pass typed data inward\n- Leverage `impl Into<T>`, `AsRef<T>`, and other conversion traits for ergonomic public APIs\n\n**General:**\n- **YAGNI**: Implement only what is required; add complexity as the need arises\n- **KISS**: Favor simplicity and clarity over cleverness\n- **DRY**: Extract shared logic into common modules or helper functions\n- Follow the repo''s existing conventions over personal preference\n\n### 3. Error Handling (anyhow required)\n\n**Use `anyhow` as the primary error-handling crate.** Do not introduce `thiserror`, `eyre`, or other error libraries unless explicitly approved.\n\n- All fallible functions return `anyhow::Result<T>`\n- Attach context at every level with `.context(\"message\")` or `.with_context(|| format!(...))`\n- Propagate errors with `?`; never use `unwrap()` or `expect()` outside test code\n- Use `anyhow::anyhow!(\"message\")` or `anyhow::bail!(\"message\")` for ad-hoc errors\n- At the entrypoint: handle errors gracefully — print to `stderr` and exit with appropriate code\n\n### 4. Project Structure\n\nFollow the structure established by the project. For new projects, use idiomatic Rust conventions:\n\n**Workspace projects:**\n- Place crates under a `crates/` directory; list them in root `Cargo.toml` `[workspace.members]`\n- Shared utilities go in a common crate (e.g., `crates/common/` or `crates/shared/`)\n- Each crate has a focused responsibility\n\n**Single-crate projects:**\n- `src/main.rs` — thin entrypoint: init, parse args/config, call into app logic, handle exit\n- `src/lib.rs` — public API surface; re-exports from submodules\n- `src/models.rs` — domain types, config structs, enums\n- `src/app.rs` (or domain-named module) — core logic\n\n**General guidelines:**\n- Keep `main.rs` thin — it orchestrates; logic lives in library code\n- One module per concern; split files when they exceed ~300 lines\n- Additional modules are fine when they keep things tidy and well-scoped\n- `#[derive(Debug, Clone)]` on config/model structs; add `Copy`, `PartialEq`, `Eq` where appropriate\n- Enums for discrete modes/states; `Option<T>` for optional fields\n\n### 5. Cross-Platform GUI Development\n\nWhen building GUI applications, apply these practices:\n\nBefore doing any visual changes, check the `ui-guidelines.md` at the root of the repo for general guidelines and best \npractices for UI/UX development.\n\n**Architecture:**\n- Separate core logic from UI: business logic in a library crate, UI in the binary crate\n- Use a message/command pattern to communicate between UI and logic layers\n- Keep platform-specific code isolated behind trait abstractions or `#[cfg(target_os)]` gates\n- Design for the event loop: avoid blocking the main/UI thread\n\n**Framework guidance (choose based on project needs):**\n- **iced** — Elm-inspired, pure Rust, good for data-driven UIs. Strengths: type-safe message passing, no unsafe, cross-platform. Use `iced::Application` or `iced::Sandbox` traits.\n- **egui / eframe** — immediate-mode, excellent for tools, dashboards, debug UIs. Strengths: very fast iteration, minimal boilerplate, easy embedding. Use `eframe::App` trait.\n- **Tauri** — web-tech frontend with Rust backend. Strengths: small binary size, leverage web ecosystem, strong IPC. Use for apps where web UI is preferred.\n- **Slint** — declarative UI with `.slint` markup language. Strengths: designer-friendly, embedded-capable, good accessibility.\n- **gtk4-rs / relm4** — GTK4 bindings. Strengths: mature widget set, strong Linux integration. Use `relm4` for Elm-style architecture on top of GTK4.\n- **Dioxus** — React-like with RSX syntax. Strengths: familiar to web devs, cross-platform (desktop, web, mobile).\n\n**Cross-platform considerations:**\n- Test on all target platforms early and regularly (Windows, macOS, Linux at minimum)\n- Use `dirs` or `directories` crate for platform-appropriate config/data/cache paths\n- Handle HiDPI/scaling — use logical pixels, not physical pixels\n- Respect platform conventions for keyboard shortcuts (Cmd vs Ctrl), file paths, and native look-and-feel\n- Use `cfg(target_os)` sparingly and only when truly needed; prefer cross-platform abstractions\n- For file dialogs, system notifications, and other OS integration, use `rfd`, `notify-rust`, or similar cross-platform crates\n\n**State management:**\n- Treat application state as a single source of truth; UI renders from state\n- Use message/event enums to describe state transitions\n- Keep state serializable where practical (enables save/restore, undo/redo)\n- For complex state, consider a reducer pattern or `Arc<Mutex<State>>` for thread-safe sharing\n\n**Async and threading in GUI apps:**\n- Never block the UI thread — offload heavy work to background threads or async tasks\n- Use channels (`std::sync::mpsc`, `crossbeam-channel`, `tokio::sync::mpsc`) to send results back to the UI\n- For async runtimes alongside GUI event loops, use the framework''s built-in async support or run `tokio` on a separate thread\n- Debounce expensive operations triggered by rapid UI events (typing, resizing)\n\n### 6. Code Style\n\n- Use the repo''s `rustfmt` and `clippy` configuration; never change them; fix all warnings\n- `snake_case` for functions/variables/modules/files; `PascalCase` for types; `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants\n- Group imports: `crate::`, external crates, `std::`; no glob imports in production code\n- Doc comments (`///`) on all public items with `# Errors` / `# Panics` sections where applicable\n- Comments explain \"why\", not \"what\"; no commented-out code\n- Functions ~50 lines max; extract helpers when they grow\n- `match` over `if let` chains for multiple variants; guard clauses for early returns\n\n### 7. Dependencies\n\n- Check the existing `Cargo.toml` before adding new dependencies\n- Prefer well-maintained, widely used crates (check download counts, recent activity, `unsafe` usage)\n- Pin major versions; use `cargo update` for patch updates\n- Feature-gate optional functionality to keep compile times and binary size down\n- For cross-platform apps, verify that dependencies support all target platforms\n- Dependencies should be always kept up-to-date with the latest stable versions\n\n**Commonly useful crates:**\n- CLI: `clap` (derive), `indicatif` (progress bars)\n- Serialization: `serde` + `serde_json` / `toml` / `ron`\n- Async: `tokio` (only when genuinely needed)\n- Logging: `tracing` or `log` + `env_logger`\n- File I/O: `tempfile` (tests), `walkdir` (traversal)\n- Cross-platform paths: `dirs`, `directories`\n\n### 8. Performance\n\n- Use `BufReader`/`BufWriter` for file I/O\n- Pre-allocate `Vec` capacity when size is known; use `Cow<''_, str>` to avoid unnecessary allocations\n- Use `std::sync::LazyLock` (or `once_cell::sync::Lazy`) for expensive one-time inits like compiled regexes\n- Profile before optimizing — use `cargo flamegraph`, `criterion` for benchmarks\n- For GUI: keep frame budgets in mind (~16ms for 60fps); avoid allocations in hot render paths\n\n### 9. Testing\n\n- Unit tests: `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` at the bottom of each file; `use super::*`\n- File-based tests: `tempfile::tempdir()` for temporary directories\n- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert; use helper functions to build test fixtures\n- Use `assert!(matches!(...))` for enum variant checks\n- Test happy paths, error conditions, and meaningful boundary values\n- Add tests where it makes sense; don''t add them purely for coverage numbers\n- For GUI: test logic and state management independently from rendering; use snapshot/golden tests for UI if the framework supports it\n\n### 10. Forbidden\n\n- `unsafe` code unless explicitly approved by the user\n- `unwrap()` / `expect()` in non-test code\n- Error libraries other than `anyhow` (no `thiserror`, `eyre`, etc.) unless explicitly approved\n- Changing `rustfmt` or `clippy` settings without explicit approval\n- Blocking the UI/main thread in GUI applications\n\n### 11. Quality Validation\n\nRun before completion (adjust package name to match the project):\n```bash\ncargo build -p <package-name>\ncargo clippy -p <package-name> -- -D warnings\ncargo test -p <package-name>\ncargo fmt -p <package-name> -- --check\n```\n\nFor workspace-wide checks:\n```bash\ncargo build --workspace\ncargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings\ncargo test --workspace\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\n```\n\nNever run git commit. Summarize changes to the user alongside any problems and caveats.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing new Rust applications, libraries, or tools\n- Building cross-platform GUI applications in Rust\n- Adding functionality to existing crates\n- Refactoring, debugging, or reviewing Rust code\n- Any Rust task where production-quality, idiomatic code is expected"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T14:52:30.929Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for systems programming agents requiring memory-safe and concurrent code execution with Rust.","zh":"适用于需要内存安全和并发代码执行的系统编程代理，使用Rust。","ja":"Rustを使用してメモリ安全でコンカレントなコード実行を必要とするシステムプログラミングエージェントに最適。","ko":"메모리 안전 및 동시 코드 실행이 필요한 시스템 프로그래밍 에이전트에 적합하며 Rust를 사용합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de programación de sistemas que requieren ejecución de código concurrente y seguro en memoria con Rust.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de programmation de systèmes nécessitant une exécution de code sécurisée en mémoire et concurrente avec Rust.","de":"Ideal für Systemprogrammierungsagenten, die eine Speicher-sichere und konkurrierende Codeausführung mit Rust erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de programação de sistemas que exigem execução de código concorrente e seguro em memória com Rust.","ru":"Идеально подходит для системных программных агентов, требующих безопасного и одновременного выполнения кода с помощью Rust.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات برمجة النظام التي تتطلب تنفيذ код متزامن وأمن للمتغيرات مع Rust."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build cross-platform applications with Rust''s ownership model and borrow checker, ensuring reliable and efficient code. It provides a robust foundation for developing Notepad-inspired GUI applications, leveraging Rust''s standard library and ecosystem.","zh":"赋予代理构建跨平台应用的能力，使用Rust的所有权模型和借用检查器，确保可靠和高效的代码。它为开发记事本风格的GUI应用程序提供了坚实的基础，利用Rust的标准库和生态系统。","ja":"Rustの所有権モデルと借用チェッカーを使用して、クロスプラットフォームアプリケーションを構築するエージェントの能力を提供し、信頼性が高く効率的なコードを保証します。Rustの標準ライブラリとエコシステムを利用して、メモ帳風のGUIアプリケーションを開発するための堅実な基盤を提供します。","ko":"Rust의 소유권 모델과 빌림 검사기를 사용하여 신뢰할 수 있고 효율적인 코드를 보장하는 크로스 플랫폼 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 제공합니다. Rust의 표준 라이브러리와 생태계를 활용하여 메모장과 같은 GUI 애플리케이션을 개발하기 위한 견고한基础를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir aplicaciones multiplataforma con el modelo de propiedad y el verificador de préstamos de Rust, garantizando un código confiable y eficiente. Proporciona una base sólida para desarrollar aplicaciones de GUI inspiradas en Notepad, aprovechando la biblioteca y el ecosistema estándar de Rust.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des applications multiplateformes avec le modèle de propriété et le vérificateur d''emprunt de Rust, garantissant un code fiable et efficace. Fournit une base solide pour développer des applications GUI inspirées de Notepad, en exploitant la bibliothèque et l''écosystème standard de Rust.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, plattformübergreifende Anwendungen mit Rusts Besitzmodell und Borrow-Checker zu erstellen, um zuverlässigen und effizienten Code zu gewährleisten. Bietet eine solide Grundlage für die Entwicklung von GUI-Anwendungen im Stil von Notepad, indem es die Standardbibliothek und das Ökosystem von Rust nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir aplicativos cross-platform com o modelo de propriedade e verificador de empréstimo do Rust, garantindo um código confiável e eficiente. Ele fornece uma base sólida para o desenvolvimento de aplicações GUI inspiradas no Notepad, aproveitando a biblioteca padrão e o ecossistema do Rust.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать кроссплатформенные приложения с помощью модели владения и заемщика Rust, обеспечивая надежный и эффективный код. Он обеспечивает прочную основу для разработки GUI-приложений, вдохновленных Notepad, используя стандартную библиотеку и экосистему Rust.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء بناء تطبيقات متعددة المنصات باستخدام نموذج ملكية Rust و فحص الإقراض، مما يضمن كودًا موثوقًا وفعّالًا. يوفر أساسًا قويًا لتطوير تطبيقات واجهة المستخدم الرسومية التي تتخذ من Notepad نموذجًا، مستفيدًا من المكتبة القياسية وبيئة Rust."},"useCases":{"en":["Building cross-platform Notepad-like applications","Creating system tools with memory safety guarantees","Developing concurrent and parallel systems with Rust''s async/await support"],"zh":["构建跨平台的记事本类应用程序","创建具有内存安全保证的系统工具","使用Rust的异步/等待支持开发并发和并行系统"],"ja":["クロスプラットフォームのメモ帳風アプリケーションを構築する","メモリ安全性保証のあるシステムツールを作成する","Rustのasync/awaitサポートを使用してコンカレントおよび並列システムを開発する"],"ko":["크로스 플랫폼 메모장과 같은 애플리케이션 구축","메모리 안전 보장 시스템 도구 생성","Rust의 async/await 지원을 사용한 동시 및 병렬 시스템 개발"],"es":["Construir aplicaciones multiplataforma similares a Notepad","Crear herramientas de sistema con garantías de seguridad de memoria","Desarrollar sistemas concurrentes y paralelos con el soporte async/await de Rust"],"fr":["Créer des applications multiplateformes similaires à Notepad","Créer des outils système avec des garanties de sécurité de la mémoire","Développer des systèmes concurrents et parallèles avec le support async/await de Rust"],"de":["Erstellen von plattformübergreifenden Anwendungen im Stil von Notepad","Erstellen von Systemtools mit Speicher-Sicherheitsgarantien","Entwicklung von konkurrierenden und parallelen Systemen mit Rusts async/await-Unterstützung"],"pt":["Construir aplicações cross-platform semelhantes ao Notepad","Criar ferramentas de sistema com garantias de segurança de memória","Desenvolver sistemas concorrentes e paralelos com o suporte async/await do Rust"],"ru":["Создание кроссплатформенных приложений, похожих на Notepad","Разработка системных инструментов с гарантиями безопасности памяти","Разработка конкрутных и параллельных систем с помощью поддержки async/await в Rust"],"ar":["بناء تطبيقات متعددة المنصات مشابهة ل Notepad","إنشاء أدوات نظام مع ضمانات أمان المتغيرات","تطوير أنظمة متزامنة ومتوازية باستخدام دعم async/await في Rust"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust compiler and toolchain installation","Platform-specific constraints for GUI development"],"zh":["需要Rust编译器和工具链安装","GUI开发的平台特定约束"],"ja":["Rustコンパイラとツールチェーンのインストールが必要","GUI開発のプラットフォーム固有の制約"],"ko":["Rust 컴파일러 및 툴체인 설치가 필요","GUI 개발을 위한 플랫폼 특정 제약"],"es":["Requiere instalación del compilador y la cadena de herramientas de Rust","Restricciones específicas de la plataforma para el desarrollo de GUI"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation du compilateur et de la chaîne d''outils de Rust","Contraintes spécifiques à la plateforme pour le développement de GUI"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation des Rust-Compilers und der Werkzeugkette","Plattform-spezifische Einschränkungen für die GUI-Entwicklung"],"pt":["Exige instalação do compilador e da cadeia de ferramentas do Rust","Restrições específicas de plataforma para desenvolvimento de GUI"],"ru":["Требует установки компилятора и инструментария Rust","Платформенно-специфические ограничения для разработки GUI"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت مترجم و سلسلة أدوات Rust","قيود محددة بالمنصة لتطوير واجهة المستخدم الرسومية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"41978aba0c2aee8024cd61d0e035bc0f4ff7f661a0f966772d154428608b04cb","qualityScore":55}');
