et à configurer","Compatibilité avec plusieurs versions de Git"],"de":["Integration in Visual Studio","Detaillierte Zusammenfassung der vorgenommenen Änderungen","Leichtes Tool für Git","Einfach zu installieren und zu konfigurieren","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Git-Versionen"],"pt":["Integração com o Visual Studio","Visão geral das alterações feitas no código","Ferramenta leve e de fácil instalação","Melhoria da produtividade dos desenvolvedores","Compatibilidade com diferentes versões do Git"],"ru":["Интеграция с Visual Studio","Обзор изменений, внесенных в код","Легкая установка и использование","Повышение производительности разработчиков","Совместимость с разными версиями Git"],"ar":["التكامل مع فيجوال ستوديو","نظرة عامة على التعديلات التي تم إجراؤها على الكود","أداة خفيفة الوزن وسهلة التثبيت","تحسين إنتاجية المطورين","التوافق مع إصدارات مختلفة من الغيت"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用Git Blame","什么是轻量级Git Blame","Visual Studio插件","Git Blame Visual Studio","代码审查工具","AI智能工具","代码可视化工具"],"ja":["Git Blameの使い方","軽量Git Blameとは","Visual Studioプラグイン","Git Blame Visual Studio","コードレビューツール","AIエージェント","コード可視化ツール"],"ko":["Git Blame 사용법","가벼운 Git Blame","Visual Studio 플러그인","Git Blame Visual Studio","코드 리뷰 도구","AI 에이전트","코드 시각화 도구"],"es":["herramientas de desarrollo","resumen de características","plugin de Visual Studio","Git","cómo instalar el plugin de resumen de características","alternativas al plugin de resumen de características","guía de configuración del plugin de resumen de características"],"fr":["outils de développement","résumé de fonctionnalités","plugin de Visual Studio","Git","comment installer le plugin de résumé de fonctionnalités","alternatives au plugin de résumé de fonctionnalités","guide de configuration du plugin de résumé de fonctionnalités"],"de":["Entwicklungstools","Feature-Summary","Visual Studio-Plugin","Git","wie man das Feature-Summary-Plugin installiert","Alternativen zum Feature-Summary-Plugin","Konfigurationsanleitung für das Feature-Summary-Plugin"],"pt":["como usar o Git Blame","o que é o Git Blame","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","plug-in para Visual Studio","alternativas para o Git Blame","Guia de instalação do plug-in","configuração do plug-in","diferenças entre o Git Blame e o Git Diff"],"ru":["как использовать Git Blame","что такое Git Blame","инструменты для разработчиков","плагин для Visual Studio","альтернативы для Git Blame","Руководство по установке плагина","настройка плагина","различия между Git Blame и Git Diff"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام الغيت بلايم","ما هو الغيت بلايم","أدوات المطورين","إضافة إلى فيجوال ستوديو","بديلات للغيت بلايم","دليل تثبيت الإضافة","ضبط الإضافة","الفرق بين الغيت بلايم والغيت ديف"]}},"owner":"prulloac","repo":"git-blame-vsc","repoPath":"prulloac/git-blame-vsc","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T00:33:08Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"feature-summary","description":"Create comprehensive feature documentation summaries that describe current and future capabilities. Use after feature-breakdown to document what a feature does, its business value, technical implementation, and roadmap. Ideal for creating user-facing documentation and feature catalogs in `docs/features/<feature-name>/` format.","bodyPreview":"# Feature Summary Skill\n\n**Answers the question: How do we DOCUMENT and COMMUNICATE a feature to stakeholders, users, and developers?**\n\nThis skill focuses on **feature documentation and communication**, transforming detailed breakdowns into accessible, comprehensive summaries that serve multiple audiences.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when you have a **completed feature** (or a detailed feature breakdown) and need to:\n- Create comprehensive user-facing documentation\n- Build a feature catalog","body":"# Feature Summary Skill\n\n**Answers the question: How do we DOCUMENT and COMMUNICATE a feature to stakeholders, users, and developers?**\n\nThis skill focuses on **feature documentation and communication**, transforming detailed breakdowns into accessible, comprehensive summaries that serve multiple audiences.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when you have a **completed feature** (or a detailed feature breakdown) and need to:\n- Create comprehensive user-facing documentation\n- Build a feature catalog or knowledge base\n- Document business features for stakeholder communication\n- Explain technical implementation to developers\n- Create feature roadmaps and status tracking\n- Document current and future capabilities\n- Classify features by type (core, customization, performance, accessibility, UX)\n\n**Key indicator**: You''re asking \"How do we document and communicate this feature?\" or \"What should users know about this capability?\"\n\n**Works best with**: This skill complements `feature-breakdown` (provides the detailed task list) and `feature-planning` (provides the execution sequence)\n\n## When NOT to Use\n\n- You only have a feature idea/spec without breakdown details → Use `feature-breakdown` first\n- You need to determine task execution order → Use `feature-planning` instead\n- You need to track real-time implementation progress → Use `execution-tracking` instead\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nRecommended (but not strictly required):\n\n1. **Feature breakdown** (`docs/features/[feature-name]/breakdown.md`)\n   - Provides detailed task list and component architecture\n   - Helps identify all feature aspects to document\n   \n2. **Feature implementation** (completed or well-understood)\n   - Access to working code or specifications\n   - Understanding of current status\n\n3. **Audience understanding**\n   - Who will read this documentation?\n   - What do they need to know?\n\n## Inputs\n\n- **Feature specification or implemented feature** (required)\n- **Feature breakdown document** (recommended): `docs/features/[feature-name]/breakdown.md`\n- **Source code access** (optional but helpful): For accurate implementation details\n- **Usage examples** (optional): For user documentation\n\n## Directory Structure\n\nAll feature-summary output must follow this structure:\n\n```\ndocs/features/[feature-name]/\n├── breakdown.md              (created by feature-breakdown skill)\n├── summary.md                (created by this skill - PRIMARY OUTPUT)\n├── configuration.md          (optional - created by this skill)\n├── reference.md              (optional - created by this skill)\n└── implementation-progress.md (created by execution-tracking skill during implementation)\n```\n\n## Outputs\n\n**MANDATORY FILE ORGANIZATION**: All feature documentation must be in `docs/features/<feature-name>/` subdirectory.\n\nWhen this skill completes, it creates:\n\n1. **Primary Output: Feature Summary** (`docs/features/[feature-name]/summary.md`)\n   - Comprehensive feature documentation\n   - 150-250 lines covering all major aspects\n   - Serves multiple audiences (users, developers, stakeholders)\n   - Includes feature type classification\n   - **Example**: `docs/features/git-blame-overlay/summary.md`\n\n2. **Optional: Configuration Reference** (`docs/features/[feature-name]/configuration.md`)\n   - Detailed configuration options and examples\n   - For features with significant customization\n   \n3. **Optional: Reference Guide** (`docs/features/[feature-name]/reference.md`)\n   - Technical implementation details for developers\n   - Architecture decisions and patterns\n   \n4. **Supporting Structure**:\n   - `docs/features/[feature-name]/breakdown.md` - Implementation tasks (created by feature-breakdown skill)\n   - `docs/features/[feature-name]/implementation-progress.md` - Tracking file (created by execution-tracking skill)\n\n## Workflow Overview\n\nThe feature summary process transforms a feature concept into comprehensive documentation:\n\n```\nFeature Input (Breakdown or Implementation)\n    ↓\nAnalyze Feature Aspects\n    ↓\nIdentify Audiences & Use Cases\n    ↓\nClassify Feature Type\n    ↓\nCreate Executive Summary\n    ↓\nDocument Configuration & Options\n    ↓\nExplain Technical Implementation\n    ↓\nDefine Status & Version Info\n    ↓\nIdentify Limitations & Future Enhancements\n    ↓\nWrite Output Files\n    ↓\nComprehensive Feature Documentation\n```\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Analyze Feature Scope\n\n**Input**: Feature specification, breakdown, or implementation\n\n1. **Identify feature aspects**:\n   - What does it do? (Core functionality)\n   - Why is it valuable? (Business value)\n   - How do users interact with it? (User experience)\n   - What are the key capabilities? (Feature list)\n   - What are the limitations? (Edge cases and constraints)\n\n2. **Extract technical details**:\n   - How is it implemented? (Architecture, components)\n   - What are the technical requirements? (Dependencies, prerequisites)\n   - Where is the code located? (Source file references)\n   - What patterns or technologies are used?\n\n3. **Understand current state**:\n   - Version number and release status\n   - When was it introduced?\n   - What improvements or fixes have been made?\n   - Is it production-ready?\n\n### Phase 2: Classify Feature Type\n\nAssign the feature to one or more categories:\n\n| Category | Description | Examples |\n|----------|-------------|----------|\n| **Core Functionality** | Essential feature defining the product''s primary purpose | Git blame overlay, authentication system |\n| **Customization** | Allows users to personalize behavior and appearance | Output patterns, color customization |\n| **User Experience** | Improves usability, visual integration, and workflow | Theme adaptation, command palette |\n| **Accessibility** | Supports users with different abilities and needs | Color options, keyboard shortcuts, ARIA labels |\n| **Performance** | Optimizes speed and resource usage | Caching, lazy loading, pagination |\n| **Extended Functionality** | Non-essential features that enhance core capability | Advanced filtering, export options |\n| **Developer Experience** | Improves developer productivity and experience | Debugging tools, API documentation |\n\n## Output Format\n\nFeature summaries include these key sections (in order):\n\n1. **Feature Header** - Name, overview, status, version, feature type\n2. **Business Value** - Why it matters, specific benefits\n3. **What It Does** - Core functionality with user experience and examples\n4. **Key Features** - Capabilities and extended functionality\n5. **Configuration** (if applicable) - Options and examples\n6. **Technical Implementation** - Code references and architecture\n7. **User Interactions** - Workflows and commands\n8. **Status and Roadmap** - Current status, limitations, future enhancements\n9. **Related Features** - Cross-references to related features\n\n**For a complete template with examples and detailed guidelines**, see:\n- [`assets/documentation-template.md`](assets/documentation-template.md) - Blank template for creating new features\n- [`examples/example-feature-summary-core.md`](examples/example-feature-summary-core.md) - Core functionality example\n- [`examples/example-feature-summary-customization.md`](examples/example-feature-summary-customization.md) - Customization example\n- [`examples/example-feature-summary-performance.md`](examples/example-feature-summary-performance.md) - Performance example\n\n## Feature Type Classification\n\nEvery feature should be classified with a primary type and optional secondary types. This helps users understand:\n- **What is this feature?** (Its purpose)\n- **Is it essential?** (Core vs. optional)\n- **How does it relate to other features?** (Ecosystem awareness)\n\n### Quick Reference\n\n| Type | Icon | Purpose | Example |\n|------|------|---------|---------|\n| **Core Functionality** | ⭐ | Essential, defines product purpose | Git blame overlay |\n| **Customization** | 🎨 | Personalization & preferences | Output patterns |\n| **User Experience** | 👥 | Usability & visual integration | Theme-aware styling |\n| **Accessibility** | ♿ | Support for diverse users | Color options |\n| **Performance** | 🚀 | Speed & resource optimization | Caching system |\n| **Extended Functionality** | ➕ | Optional enhancements | Export options |\n| **Developer Experience** | 🛠️ | Developer productivity | API docs |\n\n**For detailed guidance on each type**, see [`references/feature-type-reference.md`](references/feature-type-reference.md)\n\n## Guidelines\n\n### Writing for Multiple Audiences\n\n**For Users**:\n- Use clear, non-technical language\n- Explain benefits and use cases\n- Provide concrete examples\n- Include configuration examples\n\n**For Developers**:\n- Include code references and file paths\n- Explain architecture and design decisions\n- Document patterns and conventions\n- Link to technical documentation\n\n**For Stakeholders**:\n- Lead with business value\n- Emphasize impact and ROI\n- Focus on status and roadmap\n- Quantify benefits where possible\n\n### Feature Classification\n\nWhen assigning feature types:\n\n1. **Identify primary category**: What is this feature''s main purpose?\n2. **Note secondary categories**: Can it serve multiple purposes?\n3. **Explain classification**: Why does this categorization make sense?\n4. **Consider user perception**: How do users think about this feature?\n\n### Technical Accuracy\n\n- Reference actual source code paths\n- Include line numbers for specific implementations\n- Verify all code examples work correctly\n- Document technical constraints accurately\n\n### Keeping Documentation Current\n\n- Update status section when feature versions change\n- Add to limitations if new constraints are discovered\n- Move items from \"Future Enhancements\" when implemented\n- Update configuration examples if options change\n\n## Common Pitfalls to Avoid\n\n❌ **Too technical for users**: Remember non-technical readers; explain technical concepts\n❌ **Too vague for developers**: Provide specific code references and implementation details\n❌ **Incomplete feature classification**: Always explain why a feature fits its category\n❌ **Missing examples**: Concrete examples are crucial for understanding\n❌ **Outdated information**: Keep status and version info current\n❌ **Poor cross-linking**: Reference related features; help readers understand relationships\n❌ **Missing technical details**: Developers need code references and architecture info\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\nThe feature-summary skill works as part of a larger feature documentation ecosystem. For detailed integration workflows and examples:\n\n- **Overview of the skill ecosystem**: [`references/ecosystem-diagram.md`](references/ecosystem-diagram.md)\n- **Practical integration workflows**: [`references/workflow-integration-guide.md`](references/workflow-integration-guide.md)\n- **Quick navigation**: [`references/integration-guide.md`](references/integration-guide.md)\n\n### Recommended Skill Sequence\n\n1. **feature-breakdown** (1-2 hrs) - Decompose feature into tasks and acceptance criteria\n2. **feature-summary** (1-2 hrs) - Create user-facing documentation\n3. **feature-planning** (1-2 hrs) - Sequence tasks for execution\n4. **execution-tracking** (ongoing) - Monitor implementation progress\n\n### Key Concepts\n\n**feature-breakdown creates** (`docs/features/[name]/breakdown.md`):\n- Internal task list\n- Component architecture\n- Acceptance criteria\n- Validation plan\n\n**feature-summary creates** (`docs/features/[name]/summary.md`):\n- User-facing documentation\n- Business value explanation\n- Configuration examples\n- Roadmap and future enhancements\n\n## Quality Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing feature documentation:\n\n- [ ] Feature type classification is clear and explained\n- [ ] Business value section explains \"why\" not just \"what\"\n- [ ] Examples show real-world usage\n- [ ] Technical details are accurate with code references\n- [ ] Configuration options are clearly documented\n- [ ] Status and version info are current\n- [ ] Known limitations are honestly documented\n- [ ] Future enhancements are realistic and categorized\n- [ ] Cross-references to related features are accurate\n- [ ] Documentation is accessible to intended audiences\n- [ ] Language is clear and concise\n- [ ] All file paths and code references are accurate\n\n## Example Output\n\nFor a real example of how feature documentation should look, see the example feature summaries:\n\n- Reference: `examples/example-feature-summary-core.md` (Core functionality example)\n- Reference: `examples/example-feature-summary-customization.md` (Customization example)\n- Reference: `examples/example-feature-summary-performance.md` (Performance feature example)\n\n## See Also\n\n- `feature-breakdown` - Decompose features into tasks\n- `feature-planning` - Sequence tasks for execution\n- `execution-tracking` - Monitor feature implementation progress\n- `readme-updater` - Keep project README in sync with features\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T07:14:13.570Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Writing Agents needing to create comprehensive feature documentation for stakeholders and users.","zh":"适用于需要为利益相关者和用户创建全面特性文档的技术写作代理。","ja":"ステークホルダーとユーザーに配布するための包括的な機能ドキュメントを作成する必要があるテクニカルライティングエージェントに適しています。","ko":"이익 관련자와 사용자에게 배포할 수 있는 포괄적인 기능 문서를 작성해야 하는 기술 작가 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Escritura Técnica que necesitan crear documentación de características comprehensiva para partes interesadas y usuarios.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de rédaction technique ayant besoin de créer une documentation de fonctionnalités complète pour les parties prenantes et les utilisateurs.","de":"Ideal für technische Schreibagenten, die umfassende Funktionsdokumentationen für Stakeholder und Benutzer erstellen müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Redação Técnica que precisam criar documentação de recursos abrangente para partes interessadas e usuários.","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов написания, которым необходимо создавать комплексную документацию функций для заинтересованных сторон и пользователей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الكتابة الفنية الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء توثيق ميزات شاملة للمستخدمين وأصحاب المصلحة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform detailed feature breakdowns into accessible summaries using lightweight markup formats, facilitating effective communication through feature catalogs and user-facing documentation, leveraging git blame and Visual Studio plugins for streamlined collaboration.","zh":"赋予代理人使用轻量级标记格式将详细的功能细分转化为易于访问的摘要的能力，通过功能目录和用户面向的文档实现有效的沟通，并利用git blame和Visual Studio插件实现流畅的协作。","ja":"エージェントが詳細な機能の細分化をアクセス可能な概要に変換する軽量マークアップ形式を使用する能力を付与し、機能カタログやユーザー向けのドキュメントを通じて効果的なコミュニケーションを実現し、git blameやVisual Studioプラグインを使用したスムーズなコラボレーションを可能にします。","ko":"세부적인 기능의 세부를 가벼운 마크업 형식으로 사용하여 접근 가능한 요약으로 변환하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하고 기능 카탈로그 및 사용자 친화적인 문서를 통해 효과적인 의사 소통을 달성하며 git blame 및 Visual Studio 플러그인을 사용하여 원활한 협력을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar desgloses detallados de características en resúmenes accesibles utilizando formatos de marcado ligero, facilitando la comunicación efectiva a través de catálogos de características y documentación orientada al usuario, aprovechando git blame y plugins de Visual Studio para una colaboración optimizada.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer les décompositions détaillées de fonctions en résumés accessibles en utilisant des formats de balisage légers, facilitant une communication efficace à travers des catalogues de fonctions et une documentation orientée utilisateur, en exploitant git blame et les plugins Visual Studio pour une collaboration optimisée.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, detaillierte Funktionszerlegungen in zugängliche Zusammenfassungen umzuwandeln, indem sie leichte Markup-Formate verwenden, und ermöglicht so eine effektive Kommunikation durch Funktionskataloge und benutzerorientierte Dokumentation, indem git blame und Visual Studio-Plugins für eine optimierte Zusammenarbeit genutzt werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes transformem quebras detalhadas de recursos em resumos acessíveis usando formatos de marcação leves, facilitando a comunicação eficaz por meio de catálogos de recursos e documentação voltada para o usuário, aproveitando plugins git blame e Visual Studio para colaboração simplificada.","ru":"Позволяет агентам превратить подробный разбор функций в доступные сводки, используя легкие форматы разметки, облегчая эффективную коммуникацию через каталоги функций и документацию, ориентированную на пользователя, используя плагины git blame и Visual Studio для упрощенного сотрудничества.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تحويل كسر مفصل للميزات إلى ملخصات يمكن الوصول إليها باستخدام تنسيقات تحرير خفيفة، وتسهيل الاتصال الفعال من خلال فهرس الميزات وتوضيح موجه للمستخدم، والاستفادة من ملحقات git blame و Visual Studio للتعاون المبسّط."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating user manuals for newly released features","Creating feature catalogs for product showcases","Automating documentation updates using git blame integration"],"zh":["为新发布的功能生成用户手册","为产品展示创建功能目录","使用git blame集成自动化文档更新"],"ja":["新しくリリースされた機能のユーザーマニュアルを生成する","製品の展示用に機能カタログを作成する","git blameの統合を使用してドキュメントの更新を自動化する"],"ko":["새로发布된 기능의 사용자 설명서 생성","제품展示를 위한 기능 카탈로그 생성","git blame 통합을 사용하여 문서 업데이트 자동화"],"es":["Generar manuales de usuario para características recién lanzadas","Crear catálogos de características para exhibiciones de productos","Automatizar las actualizaciones de documentación mediante la integración de git blame"],"fr":["Générer des manuels d''utilisateur pour les fonctions récemment lancées","Créer des catalogues de fonctions pour les expositions de produits","Automatiser les mises à jour de documentation à l''aide de l''intégration de git blame"],"de":["Benutzerhandbücher für neu veröffentlichte Funktionen generieren","Funktionskataloge für Produktpräsentationen erstellen","Dokumentationsupdates mithilfe der git blame-Integration automatisieren"],"pt":["Gerar manuais do usuário para recursos lançados recentemente","Criar catálogos de recursos para mostras de produtos","Automatizar atualizações de documentação usando integração git blame"],"ru":["Генерировать руководства пользователя для недавно выпущенных функций","Создавать каталоги функций для демонстраций продукта","Автоматизировать обновления документации с помощью интеграции git blame"],"ar":["генерировать دليلاً للمستخدم لملحقات صدرت حديثًا","إنشاء فهرس الميزات لأجهزة العرض للمنتجات","تأتمتة تحديثات التوثيق باستخدام دمج git blame"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires completed feature or detailed breakdown","Primarily suited for technical writing and documentation purposes"],"zh":["需要完成的功能或详细的细分","主要适用于技术写作和文档目的"],"ja":["完了した機能または詳細な細分化が必要","主にテクニカルライティングとドキュメントの目的で使用する"],"ko":["완료된 기능 또는 세부적인 세분화가 필요","주로 기술 작문 및 문서 목적으로 적합"],"es":["Requiere una característica completada o una descomposición detallada","Primariamente diseñado para fines de escritura y documentación técnicas"],"fr":["Nécessite une fonctionnalité complétée ou une décomposition détaillée","Principalement conçu pour des fins de rédaction et de documentation techniques"],"de":["Erfordert eine abgeschlossene Funktion oder eine detaillierte Zerlegung","In erster Linie für technische Schreib- und Dokumentationszwecke geeignet"],"pt":["Exige recurso concluído ou quebra detalhada","Primariamente adequado para fins de redação técnica e documentação"],"ru":["Требует завершенного функционала или подробного разбора","В основном подходит для целей технического написания и документации"],"ar":["يتطلب ميزة مكتملة أو كسر مفصل","في الغالب مناسب للأغراض الكتابية الفنية والتوثيق"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c62b6903f190733fbb871982f2629346d589fdf6e0cbaef916f75971d90e8b1e","qualityScore":55}');
