de la productividad y la eficiencia en el desarrollo"],"fr":["Développement basé sur des spécifications","Intégration avec des technologies comme React et Node.js","Création de projets de manière efficace et efficiente","Support pour CLI et Agent","Amélioration de la productivité et de l''efficacité dans le développement"],"de":["Spezifikationsbasierte Entwicklung","Integration mit Technologien wie React und Node.js","Erstellung von Projekten in effizienter und effektiver Weise","Unterstützung für CLI und Agent","Verbesserung der Produktivität und Effizienz in der Entwicklung"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento baseado em especificações","Integração com Ferramentas de AI Agents","Simplificação do processo de desenvolvimento de projetos","Melhoria da colaboração em equipe","Aumento da eficiência no desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Разработка на основе спецификации","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами","Упрощение процесса разработки проектов","Улучшение командной работы","Повышение эффективности разработки программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التطوير القائم على المواصفات","التكامل مع أدوات الإيجاد الذكي","تبسيط عملية تطوير المشاريع","تحسين التعاون الفريق","زيادة كفاءة تطوير البرمجيات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","项目域","规格驱动开发","如何使用项目域","项目域安装","项目域设置指南","项目域与其他开发工具比较","React项目域","Python项目域"],"ja":["AIエージェント","プロジェクトドメイン","仕様駆動開発","プロジェクトドメインの使い方","プロジェクトドメインのインストール","プロジェクトドメインの設定ガイド","プロジェクトドメインと他の開発ツールの比較","Reactプロジェクトドメイン","Pythonプロジェクトドメイン"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","프로젝트 도메인","명세 기반 개발","프로젝트 도메인 사용법","프로젝트 도메인 설치","프로젝트 도메인 설정 가이드","프로젝트 도메인과 다른 개발 도구 비교","React 프로젝트 도메인","Python 프로젝트 도메인"],"es":["herramientas de proyecto de dominio","metodología de desarrollo basada en especificaciones","cómo usar proyecto de dominio","proyecto de dominio vs otras herramientas","instalación de proyecto de dominio","guía de configuración de proyecto de dominio","desarrollo de proyectos con React y Node.js"],"fr":["outils de projet de domaine","méthodologie de développement basée sur des spécifications","comment utiliser le projet de domaine","projet de domaine vs autres outils","installation du projet de domaine","guide de configuration du projet de domaine","développement de projets avec React et Node.js"],"de":["Projekt-Domain-Tools","spezifikationsbasierte Entwicklungsmethode","wie man Projekt-Domain verwendet","Projekt-Domain vs andere Tools","Installation von Projekt-Domain","Konfigurationsanleitung für Projekt-Domain","Entwicklung von Projekten mit React und Node.js"],"pt":["como usar Ferramentas de AI Agents","o que é project-domain","Ferramentas de AI Agents alternative","project-domain vs outras metodologias","instalar project-domain","guia de configuração do project-domain","desenvolvimento de software com project-domain","Ferramentas de AI Agents para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое project-domain","ИИ Агенты alternative","project-domain vs другие методологии","установить project-domain","руководство по настройке project-domain","разработка программного обеспечения с project-domain","ИИ Агенты для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الإيجاد الذكي","ما هي منهجية مشروع project-domain","أدوات الإيجاد الذكي بديلة","منهجية مشروع project-domain مقابل منهجيات أخرى","تثبيت منهجية مشروع project-domain","دليل إعداد منهجية مشروع project-domain","تطوير البرمجيات مع منهجية مشروع project-domain","أدوات الإيجاد الذكي للمطورين"]}},"owner":"telum-ai","repo":"speck","repoPath":"telum-ai/speck","stars":2,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T14:49:13Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"project-domain","description":"Capture subject matter expertise and domain knowledge that will inform all product decisions - the ubiquitous language, domain rules, and principles from the field","bodyPreview":"---\ndescription: Capture subject matter expertise and domain knowledge that will inform all product decisions - the ubiquitous language, domain rules, and principles from the field.\n---\n\nThe user input to you can be provided directly by the agent or as a command argument - you **MUST** consider it before proceeding with the prompt (if not empty).\n\nUser input:\n\n$ARGUMENTS\n\nCreate or update the domain model that captures subject matter expertise for this project.\n\n## Why Domain Knowledge Matters","body":"---\ndescription: Capture subject matter expertise and domain knowledge that will inform all product decisions - the ubiquitous language, domain rules, and principles from the field.\n---\n\nThe user input to you can be provided directly by the agent or as a command argument - you **MUST** consider it before proceeding with the prompt (if not empty).\n\nUser input:\n\n$ARGUMENTS\n\nCreate or update the domain model that captures subject matter expertise for this project.\n\n## Why Domain Knowledge Matters\n\nMany products operate in specialized domains (fitness, healthcare, finance, education, etc.) where:\n- **Terminology matters**: Using wrong terms confuses users and violates industry norms\n- **Domain rules exist**: Physical, scientific, or regulatory constraints that can''t be ignored\n- **Expertise is required**: Decisions must be informed by domain knowledge, not guesses\n- **User trust depends on accuracy**: Getting domain details wrong destroys credibility\n\nThis command captures that knowledge **early** so it informs all downstream decisions.\n\n## Project Identification\n\nFirst, determine the project:\n- Parse arguments for project identifier\n- If not provided, ask: \"Which project should I create/update domain model for?\"\n- List available projects in `specs/projects/`\n\nSet `PROJECT_DIR` = `specs/projects/[PROJECT_ID]`\n\n## Context Loading\n\nLoad existing project artifacts:\n```\nREQUIRED:\n- {PROJECT_DIR}/project.md → Project vision, domain type, users\n\nOPTIONAL (if exist):\n- {PROJECT_DIR}/domain-model.md → Existing domain model (update mode)\n- {PROJECT_DIR}/project-import.md → Brownfield import notes\n- {PROJECT_DIR}/project-landscape-overview.md → Brownfield code scan\n```\n\n**Detect mode**:\n- If `domain-model.md` exists: **UPDATE mode** - enhance existing model\n- If not: **CREATE mode** - build from scratch\n\n## Just-In-Time Research\n\n**Reference**: Follow the just-in-time research pattern (`.cursor/skills/just-in-time-research/SKILL.md`)\n\n### Research Strategy\n\nFor domain model creation, research is **critical**. Identify knowledge gaps and conduct research:\n\n**1. Domain Terminology**:\n- Decision: What are the canonical terms in [domain]?\n- Web Search: \"[domain] glossary\", \"[domain] terminology standards\"\n- Deep Research (if specialized): Industry-specific ontologies, taxonomies\n\n**2. Domain Principles**:\n- Decision: What scientific/industry principles govern [domain]?\n- Web Search: \"[domain] best practices\", \"[domain] principles\", \"[field] science\"\n- Deep Research (if needed): Academic research, industry standards\n\n**3. Domain Rules & Constraints**:\n- Decision: What rules must always hold true in [domain]?\n- Web Search: \"[domain] safety guidelines\", \"[domain] regulations\"\n- Deep Research (if safety-critical): Regulatory requirements, certification standards\n\n**4. Domain Entities**:\n- Decision: What are the core concepts/entities in [domain]?\n- Web Search: \"[domain] data model\", \"[domain] ontology\"\n- Context7 (if applicable): Domain-specific libraries with established models\n\n### Research Execution\n\nUse available MCP tools in this priority order:\n1. **Perplexity MCP** (preferred): `perplexity_search`, `perplexity_ask`, `perplexity_research`\n2. **Web Search** (fallback): `web_search` tool\n3. **User Input**: Ask user for SME knowledge they have\n\n**Embed all findings** directly into the domain model sections with source citations.\n\n## Interactive Domain Elicitation\n\n### Step 1: Domain Identification\n\nAsk the user:\n\n> \"Let''s capture the domain expertise for your project. I''ll ask you questions to understand the specialized knowledge that should inform this product.\n>\n> **What domain/field does this product operate in?**\n> (e.g., Exercise Science, Healthcare, Financial Services, Education, Agriculture, etc.)\n>\n> **What makes this domain specialized?** Why does someone need expertise to build this correctly?\"\n\nWait for response. Use the domain identification to guide research.\n\n### Step 2: Terminology Elicitation\n\n> \"Now let''s establish the **canonical terminology** for this domain.\n>\n> **What are the most important terms/concepts users and the product must use?**\n> For each term, provide:\n> - The precise definition\n> - Any synonyms we should AVOID (to maintain consistency)\n>\n> I''ll also research standard terminology in [domain] to ensure we''re aligned with industry norms.\"\n\nConduct terminology research and merge with user input.\n\n### Step 3: Core Concepts & Entities\n\n> \"What are the **core concepts or entities** in this domain?\n>\n> Think about:\n> - What ''things'' does the user work with? (e.g., Workouts, Exercises, Muscle Groups)\n> - How do these relate to each other?\n> - What attributes define each concept?\n>\n> I''ll help structure these into a domain model.\"\n\nBuild entity definitions and relationships.\n\n### Step 4: Domain Rules & Invariants\n\n> \"What **rules must always be true** in this domain?\n>\n> Examples:\n> - ''A workout cannot have zero exercises''\n> - ''Rest periods must be positive numbers''\n> - ''A muscle group cannot be trained on consecutive days'' (if that''s a principle you follow)\n>\n> These become validation rules and system invariants.\"\n\n### Step 5: Domain Principles\n\n> \"What **scientific or industry principles** should guide this product?\n>\n> For a fitness app, this might include:\n> - Progressive overload principle\n> - Muscle recovery requirements\n> - Volume-intensity relationship\n>\n> For each principle, I''ll research the evidence base and document how it applies to our product.\"\n\nConduct principle research and document with sources.\n\n### Step 6: Constraints & Safety\n\n> \"What is **impossible, unsafe, or inadvisable** in this domain?\n>\n> - Physical constraints (can''t do negative reps)\n> - Safety constraints (max heart rate limits)\n> - Regulatory constraints (medical advice disclaimers)\n>\n> These become hard boundaries the product must respect.\"\n\n## Domain Model Generation\n\nAfter elicitation and research, generate `{PROJECT_DIR}/domain-model.md` using:\n- Template: `.speck/templates/project/domain-model-template.md`\n- User-provided domain expertise\n- Research findings with citations\n- Structured entity relationships\n\n### Quality Checks\n\nBefore finalizing, verify:\n\n**Completeness**:\n- [ ] All user-provided terms captured in glossary\n- [ ] Core entities have attributes and relationships\n- [ ] Key invariants documented\n- [ ] At least 2-3 foundational principles with sources\n- [ ] Constraints clearly stated\n\n**Consistency**:\n- [ ] Terminology matches project.md and other artifacts\n- [ ] No conflicting rules\n- [ ] Entity relationships are bidirectional\n\n**Actionability**:\n- [ ] Glossary terms can be used in code (valid identifiers)\n- [ ] Rules are specific enough to validate\n- [ ] Principles provide clear guidance\n\n## Output\n\nCreate/update: `{PROJECT_DIR}/domain-model.md`\n\n**Summary to user**:\n```\n✅ Domain model created/updated for [PROJECT_NAME]\n\nCaptured:\n- [X] terms in glossary\n- [X] core entities with relationships\n- [X] domain invariants\n- [X] foundational principles\n- [X] constraints\n\nResearch sources:\n- [List key sources used]\n\nThis domain model will be referenced by:\n- /project-plan (epic structure informed by domain)\n- /epic-specify (feature scope uses domain terms)\n- /story-specify (user stories use glossary)\n- /story-plan (data model validates against domain)\n- /story-validate (checks domain invariants)\n\nNext steps:\n1. Review domain-model.md for accuracy\n2. Add any missing domain expertise\n3. Continue with /project-context or /project-plan\n```\n\n## Integration Notes\n\n**For brownfield projects**:\n- Extract domain terminology from existing codebase (variable names, comments, UI text)\n- Identify implicit domain rules in existing validation logic\n- Document the \"as-is\" domain model before proposing changes\n\n**For recipe-based projects**:\n- Some recipes may have domain considerations (e.g., SaaS billing → subscription domain)\n- Layer product-specific domain on top of recipe patterns\n\n## When to Run This Command\n\n**Recommended position in flow**:\n```\n/project-specify → /project-clarify → /project-domain → /project-context → /project-architecture → /project-plan\n```\n\n**Why here?**\n- After specify/clarify: We know what we''re building\n- Before context: Domain constraints inform technical constraints\n- Before architecture: Domain entities inform data architecture\n- Before plan: Domain structure informs epic organization\n\n**Can skip if**:\n- Product has no specialized domain (generic CRUD app)\n- Domain is purely technical (developer tools)\n- Team already has domain documented elsewhere (link to it)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T02:00:13.045Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing comprehensive content analysis for informed product decisions","zh":"非常适合需要全面内容分析以做出明智产品决策的开发代理","ja":"開発エージェントが包括的なコンテンツ分析によって情報に基づいた製品の決定を下す必要がある場合に最適","ko":"전면적인 콘텐츠 분석을 통해 정보에 기반한 제품 결정을 내릴 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan un análisis de contenido integral para tomar decisiones informadas de productos","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement qui ont besoin d''une analyse de contenu complète pour prendre des décisions éclairées sur les produits","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine umfassende Inhaltsanalyse für fundierte Produktentscheidungen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de análise de conteúdo abrangente para tomar decisões informadas de produto","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходим комплексный анализ контента для принятия обоснованных решений о продукте","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل محتوى شامل لاتخاذ قرارات منتج مدروسة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to capture subject matter expertise and domain knowledge, informing product decisions with ubiquitous language, domain rules, and principles from the field, utilizing spec-driven development methodologies","zh":"赋予代理捕获主题专业知识和领域知识的能力，利用普遍的语言、领域规则和原则来告知产品决策，并采用基于规格的开发方法","ja":"エージェントが主題の専門知識とドメイン知識を取得し、普遍的な言語、ドメインルール、分野の原則を使用して製品の決定を下し、仕様駆動開発メソッドを採用することを可能に","ko":"에이전트가 주제 전문 지식과 도메인 지식을 획득하여 보편적인 언어, 도메인 규칙 및 분야의 원칙을 사용하여 제품 결정을 내리고 규格 기반 개발 방법론을 적용할 수 있도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a capturar la experiencia en la materia y el conocimiento del dominio, informando decisiones de productos con un lenguaje ubicuo, reglas de dominio y principios del campo, utilizando metodologías de desarrollo impulsadas por especificaciones","fr":"Permet aux agents de capturer l''expertise dans le domaine et les connaissances du domaine, informant les décisions de produits avec un langage ubiquitaire, des règles de domaine et des principes du domaine, en utilisant des méthodologies de développement basées sur des spécifications","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Fachwissen und Domänenwissen zu erfassen und Produktentscheidungen mit ubiquitärem Sprachgebrauch, Domänenregeln und Prinzipien aus dem Feld zu treffen, indem spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklungsmethoden eingesetzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a capturar a expertise em matéria e o conhecimento de domínio, informando decisões de produto com linguagem onipresente, regras de domínio e princípios do campo, utilizando metodologias de desenvolvimento baseadas em especificações","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью захватить экспертизу в предметной области и знания домена, информируя решения о продукте с помощью повсеместного языка, правил домена и принципов отр