: git-commit-push für torchtune YAML-Dateien","pt":"Ferramenta AI Agent git-commit-push para TorchTune","ru":"ИИ Агент git-commit-push для генерации YAML","ar":"أداة الإيجنت الذكية git-commit-push للأكواد البرمجية","en":"git-commit-push"},"description":{"zh":"git-commit-push是一个Python工具，用于生成TorchTune YAML配置文件，简化开发流程","ja":"git-commit-pushは、TorchTune YAML設定ファイルを生成するためのPythonツールです","ko":"git-commit-push는 토치튜너 YAML 구성 파일을 생성하는 파이썬 툴입니다","es":"Git-commit-push es una herramienta de Python para generar archivos YAML de torchtune de forma programática. Ideal para desarrolladores que buscan automatizar...","fr":"Git-commit-push est un outil Python pour générer des fichiers YAML torchtune de manière programmée. Idéal pour les développeurs qui cherchent à automatiser d...","de":"Git-commit-push ist ein Python-Tool zum programmatischen Erstellen von torchtune-YAML-Dateien. Perfekt für Entwickler, die Aufgaben automatisieren möchten","pt":"A ferramenta git-commit-push é uma solução Python para gerar arquivos de configuração YAML do TorchTune de forma programática.","ru":"ИИ Агент git-commit-push - это инструмент на Python для генерации файлов конфигурации YAML TorchTune.","ar":"أداة الإيجنت الذكية git-commit-push هي أداة بايثون لتوليد ملفات YAML لأكواد البرمجية TorchTune ببرمجة","en":"Python tool for generating torchtune YAML configuration files programmatically"},"definition":{"en":"Python tool for generating torchtune YAML configuration files programmatically"},"features":{"zh":["支持TorchTune YAML配置文件生成","使用Python编写","简化开发流程","提高开发效率","支持多种配置文件格式"],"ja":["TorchTune YAML設定ファイル生成をサポート","Pythonで書かれています","開発プロセスを簡素化","開発効率を向上させる","複数の設定ファイル形式をサポート"],"ko":["토치튜너 YAML 구성 파일 생성 지원","파이썬으로 작성됨","개발 프로세스 단순화","개발 효율성 향상","다중 구성 파일 형식 지원"],"es":["Generación programática de archivos YAML de torchtune","Automatización de tareas para desarrolladores","Integración con herramientas de Python","Configuración flexible y personalizable","Compatibilidad con diferentes versiones de torchtune"],"fr":["Génération programmée de fichiers YAML torchtune","Automatisation de tâches pour les développeurs","Intégration avec des outils Python","Configuration flexible et personnalisable","Compatibilité avec différentes versions de torchtune"],"de":["Programmatische Erstellung von torchtune-YAML-Dateien","Automatisierung von Aufgaben für Entwickler","Integration mit Python-Tools","Flexibles und anpassbares Konfigurationsmenü","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen torchtune-Versionen"],"pt":["Geração de arquivos YAML do TorchTune","Integração com o Python","Configuração programática","Suporte ao TorchTune","Fácil de usar"],"ru":["Генерация файлов конфигурации YAML TorchTune","Интеграция с Python","Программная настройка","Поддержка TorchTune","Легко использовать"],"ar":["إنشاء ملفات YAML لأكواد البرمجية TorchTune","التكامل مع لغة بايثون","التكوين البرمجي","دعم TorchTune","سهل الاستخدام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用git-commit-push","TorchTune YAML配置文件","Python工具","AI工具","git-commit-push安装","TorchTune YAML设置","git-commit-push教程","AI开发工具"],"ja":["git-commit-pushの使い方","TorchTune YAML設定ファイル","Pythonツール","AIエージェント","git-commit-pushのインストール","TorchTune YAML設定","git-commit-pushのチュートリアル","AI開発ツール"],"ko":["git-commit-push 사용법","토치튜너 YAML 구성 파일","파이썬 툴","AI 에이전트","git-commit-push 설치","토치튜너 YAML 설정","git-commit-push 튜토리얼","AI 개발 툴"],"es":["herramienta AI para YAML","git-commit-push tutorial","torchtune configuración","automatización de tareas en Python","alternativas a git-commit-push","instalación de git-commit-push","guía de configuración de git-commit-push","torchtune vs otros frameworks","uso de git-commit-push en proyectos de machine learning"],"fr":["outil IA pour YAML","tutoriel git-commit-push","configuration de torchtune","automatisation de tâches en Python","alternatives à git-commit-push","installation de git-commit-push","guide de configuration de git-commit-push","torchtune vs autres frameworks","utilisation de git-commit-push dans les projets de machine learning"],"de":["KI-Tool für YAML","git-commit-push-Tutorial","torchtune-Konfiguration","Automatisierung von Aufgaben in Python","Alternativen zu git-commit-push","Installation von git-commit-push","Konfigurationshandbuch für git-commit-push","torchtune im Vergleich zu anderen Frameworks","Verwendung von git-commit-push in Machine-Learning-Projekten"],"pt":["como usar git-commit-push","o que é git-commit-push","git-commit-push vs outras ferramentas","instalar git-commit-push","guia de configuração do git-commit-push","ferramentas de desenvolvimento Python","TorchTune YAML","gerar arquivos YAML"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агент git-commit-push","что такое ИИ Агент git-commit-push","ИИ Агент git-commit-push vs другие инструменты","установить ИИ Агент git-commit-push","руководство по настройке ИИ Агента git-commit-push","инструменты разработки на Python","TorchTune YAML","генерация файлов конфигурации YAML"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة الإيجنت الذكية git-commit-push","ما هي أداة الإيجنت الذكية git-commit-push","أداة الإيجنت الذكية git-commit-push مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت أداة الإيجنت الذكية git-commit-push","دليل إعداد أداة الإيجنت الذكية git-commit-push","أدوات تطوير بايثون","TorchTune YAML","إنشاء ملفات YAML"]}},"owner":"msalganik","repo":"torchtune_config_writer","repoPath":"msalganik/torchtune_config_writer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.732Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"git-commit-push","description":"This skill should be used when the user wants to commit their work to git and push to GitHub. It guides through reviewing changes, crafting meaningful commit messages following project conventions (including Conventional Commits when detected), creating commits with security checks, and pushing to remote repositories.","bodyPreview":"# Git Commit and Push\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides a structured workflow for committing changes to git and pushing to GitHub. It ensures changes are reviewed, commit messages are meaningful and follow conventions, secrets are not committed, and commits are properly pushed to remote repositories. The skill adapts to project conventions, supporting both Conventional Commits and custom formats.\n\n**Execution Philosophy**: This skill uses **contextual autonomy** - it executes immediately for saf","body":"# Git Commit and Push\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides a structured workflow for committing changes to git and pushing to GitHub. It ensures changes are reviewed, commit messages are meaningful and follow conventions, secrets are not committed, and commits are properly pushed to remote repositories. The skill adapts to project conventions, supporting both Conventional Commits and custom formats.\n\n**Execution Philosophy**: This skill uses **contextual autonomy** - it executes immediately for safe, straightforward commits, but asks for confirmation when changes are large, complex, or potentially risky. This balances speed with safety.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n- Explicitly requests to \"commit my work\" or \"push to GitHub\"\n- Says they want to save/commit/push their changes\n- Asks to create a commit or push code\n- Wants to share their work on GitHub\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Review Changes\n\nBefore committing, review what has changed:\n\n1. **Check git status** to see modified, new, and deleted files:\n   ```bash\n   git status\n   ```\n\n2. **Analyze diff systematically**:\n   ```bash\n   git diff --stat  # Overview of changes\n   git diff         # Detailed line-by-line changes\n   ```\n\n3. **Categorize changes** to inform commit message:\n   - **New features**: New files, new functions, new capabilities\n   - **Bug fixes**: Modified logic, error handling improvements\n   - **Refactoring**: Structure changes with no behavior change\n   - **Documentation**: *.md files, code comments, docstrings\n   - **Tests**: Test files, test additions/modifications\n   - **Configuration**: Build files, dependencies, settings\n   - **Styling**: Formatting, whitespace, code style only\n\n4. **Check recent commits** to understand commit message style:\n   ```bash\n   git log --oneline -20\n   ```\n\n5. **Present summary** to the user:\n   - List all modified, new, and deleted files\n   - Highlight key changes by category\n   - Note total lines added/removed\n   - Flag any unusual patterns (large files, many deletions, etc.)\n\n### Step 2: Detect Project Convention\n\nDetermine if project uses Conventional Commits or custom format:\n\n1. **Check for Conventional Commits pattern**:\n   ```bash\n   # Look for type(scope): format in recent commits\n   git log --oneline -20 | grep -E \"^[a-f0-9]+ (feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|test|chore|perf|ci|build|revert)(\\(.+\\))?:\"\n   ```\n\n2. **Analyze result**:\n   - If ≥50% of commits match pattern → Project uses Conventional Commits\n   - Otherwise → Project uses custom format\n\n3. **Note the convention** for commit message crafting\n\n### Step 3: Craft Commit Message\n\nCreate a meaningful commit message following detected convention:\n\n#### If Conventional Commits Detected\n\nUse format: `type(scope): description`\n\n**Common types**:\n- `feat`: New feature or capability\n- `fix`: Bug fix\n- `docs`: Documentation changes only\n- `style`: Code style/formatting (no logic change)\n- `refactor`: Code restructuring (no behavior change)\n- `test`: Adding or modifying tests\n- `chore`: Maintenance, dependencies, build\n- `perf`: Performance improvements\n- `ci`: CI/CD pipeline changes\n- `build`: Build system or external dependencies\n\n**Optional scope**: Component or module affected (e.g., `auth`, `api`, `ui`)\n\n**Format**:\n```\ntype(scope): imperative summary (max 50 chars)\n\nOptional body explaining the change in detail.\nExplain WHY, not WHAT (the diff shows what).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n```\n\n**Example**:\n```\nfeat(evaluation): add Inspect AI integration to experiment framework\n\nImplements Phase 4 evaluation support with:\n- User-written evaluation tasks workflow\n- Adapter-only checkpointing (200x storage reduction)\n- Complete working examples and documentation\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n```\n\n#### If Custom Format Detected\n\nMatch the project''s existing style:\n\n1. **Summarize changes** in 1-2 sentences (imperative, present tense)\n2. **Focus on \"why\"** rather than \"what\" (diff shows what changed)\n3. **Follow observed conventions** (capitalization, punctuation, length)\n4. **Keep concise** but informative\n\n**Format**:\n```\nSummary line (imperative mood, present tense)\n\nOptional detailed explanation of the changes.\nFocus on motivation and context.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n```\n\n**Example**:\n```\nAdd evaluation configuration to experiment definition framework\n\nImplements Inspect AI integration, adapter-only checkpointing support,\nand complete working examples for Phase 4 implementation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n```\n\n### Step 4: Assess Commit Risk\n\nDetermine whether this commit is \"safe\" (autonomous) or \"risky\" (requires confirmation):\n\n**Safe commits** (execute autonomously):\n- ≤ 5 files changed\n- ≤ 500 total lines changed\n- Not committing to main/master branch\n- All changes are related (same category from Step 1)\n- No unusual patterns (massive deletions, binary files, etc.)\n- User specified which files to commit\n\n**Risky commits** (require confirmation):\n- > 5 files changed\n- > 500 total lines changed\n- Committing to main/master branch\n- Mixed change types (features + fixes + refactoring)\n- Many untracked files (unclear what to commit)\n- Large files (> 100KB)\n- Unusual patterns detected\n\n**If risky**, show summary and ask user:\n```\n⚠️ Large/complex commit detected\n\nFiles: 15 files changed (+2,500 lines, -300 lines)\nTypes: Features (8 files), Documentation (5 files), Tests (2 files)\nBranch: main\nMessage: \"Add evaluation configuration and examples\"\n\nThis appears to contain multiple logical changes.\nOptions:\n  [Y] Proceed with single commit\n  [n] Cancel (I''ll help you split it)\n  [s] Show detailed file list\n```\n\n**If safe**, proceed autonomously to Step 5.\n\n### Step 5: Check for Secrets\n\nBefore staging, scan for sensitive information:\n\n1. **Check unstaged changes for secret patterns**:\n   ```bash\n   git diff | grep -E \"(api[_-]?key|api[_-]?secret|password|token|secret[_-]?key|private[_-]?key|aws[_-]?access)\" -i\n   ```\n\n2. **Check for specific patterns**:\n   - AWS Access Keys: `AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}`\n   - Generic API keys: `[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{32,}`\n   - Private keys: `-----BEGIN.*PRIVATE KEY-----`\n   - GitHub tokens: `ghp_`, `gho_`, `ghs_`, `ghr_`\n   - Bearer tokens: `Bearer [a-zA-Z0-9._-]+`\n   - Passwords in configs: `password\\s*[:=]\\s*[\"'']?[^\"''\\s]+`\n\n3. **Check for sensitive files**:\n   ```bash\n   git status --short | grep -E \"\\.env|credentials|secrets|\\.pem|\\.key|\\.p12\"\n   ```\n\n4. **If secrets detected**:\n   - ❌ **STOP immediately**\n   - Show user the matched patterns (without revealing full values)\n   - Explain the risk\n   - Ask user to:\n     - Remove secrets from code\n     - Use environment variables or secret management\n     - Add file to `.gitignore` if appropriate\n   - **Do not proceed** until secrets are removed\n\n5. **If no secrets detected**:\n   - ✅ Proceed to staging\n\n### Step 6: Stage and Commit Changes\n\n1. **Stage relevant files**:\n   ```bash\n   git add <file1> <file2> ...\n   ```\n\n   **Staging guidelines**:\n   - Stage files related to this logical change\n   - Do NOT stage unrelated changes (save for separate commit)\n   - Determine files to stage based on change analysis from Step 1\n   - **If autonomous**: Announce which files are being staged\n   - **If confirmed**: User already saw file list in confirmation\n\n2. **Verify staged changes**:\n   ```bash\n   git diff --staged --stat\n   ```\n\n3. **Announce or show commit message**:\n   - **If autonomous**: Announce message briefly (\"Committing: ''Add feature X''\")\n   - **If confirmed**: User already saw message in confirmation\n\n4. **Create commit** with formatted message:\n   ```bash\n   git commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n   <commit message here>\n\n   🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n   Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n   EOF\n   )\"\n   ```\n\n5. **Verify commit** was created:\n   ```bash\n   git log -1 --stat\n   ```\n\n### Step 7: Push to Remote\n\n1. **Check remote status**:\n   ```bash\n   git status  # Check if branch tracks remote\n   ```\n\n2. **Push to GitHub**:\n   ```bash\n   # If branch already tracks remote\n   git push\n\n   # If new branch (first push)\n   git push -u origin <branch-name>\n   ```\n\n3. **Confirm success**:\n   - Report push result to user\n   - Show number of commits pushed\n   - Provide remote URL if available\n   - Note any warnings or issues\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n### Safety Rules\n\n- **Never push force** to main/master without explicit user confirmation\n- **Never skip hooks** (--no-verify) unless explicitly requested by user\n- **Never commit secrets** - stop and warn user if detected\n- **Check authorship** before amending commits (don''t amend others'' work)\n- **Check for large files** - warn if files > 100KB (may need Git LFS)\n- **Always verify** what''s being committed before executing\n\n### Best Practices\n\n1. **Review before committing** - show user what will be committed\n2. **Meaningful messages** - explain why changes were made, not just what\n3. **Atomic commits** - each commit should be a single logical change\n4. **Follow conventions** - detect and match project''s commit style\n5. **Add co-author attribution** - include Claude Code footer\n6. **Keep commits focused** - don''t mix refactoring with features\n\n### Commit Scope Guidelines\n\n**Good commit scope**:\n- ✅ One logical change per commit\n- ✅ Related files together (e.g., code + corresponding test)\n- ✅ Can be described in one sentence\n- ✅ Typically < 500 lines (unless it''s a rename/refactor)\n- ✅ All changes serve the same purpose\n\n**Signs to split commits**:\n- ❌ Using \"and\" more than once in commit message\n- ❌ Changes span multiple unrelated features\n- ❌ Mix of bug fixes and new features\n- ❌ Experimental changes alongside production code\n- ❌ \"WIP\", \"misc fixes\", or \"various updates\" messages\n\n**When to split**:\n```bash\n# If you have unrelated changes, stage selectively:\ngit add -p  # Interactively choose hunks to stage\n\n# Or stage specific files:\ngit add file1.py file1_test.py  # First commit: feature A\ngit commit -m \"feat: add feature A\"\n\ngit add file2.py file2_test.py  # Second commit: feature B\ngit commit -m \"feat: add feature B\"\n```\n\n### Error Handling\n\n**If commit fails**:\n- Check for pre-commit hooks modifying files\n- Review error message carefully\n- May need to stage hook-modified files and amend\n- Only amend if: (1) user requested it OR (2) fixing pre-commit hook changes AND it''s safe (check authorship, not pushed)\n\n**If secrets detected**:\n- Stop immediately, do not commit\n- Explain which patterns matched\n- Guide user to remove secrets\n- Suggest using environment variables or secret management\n- Consider adding `.gitignore` entries\n\n**If push fails**:\n- Check remote branch status (might need pull first)\n- Check for merge conflicts\n- Verify remote URL is correct\n- Check authentication/permissions\n- Report error to user with suggested fixes\n\n**If large files detected**:\n- Warn user about file sizes\n- Suggest Git LFS for files > 100KB\n- Ask if files should be committed or added to `.gitignore`\n\n## Example Interaction\n\n### Example 1: Conventional Commits Project\n\n**User**: \"I''d like to commit my work and push to GitHub\"\n\n**Assistant**:\n1. Runs `git status` and `git diff --stat`\n2. Analyzes: \"2 files changed (+1,269 lines)\"\n3. Categorizes: \"New feature (eval config), documentation\"\n4. Risk assessment: ✅ Safe (2 files, 1,269 lines, feature branch)\n5. Checks convention: Detects Conventional Commits (15/20 matches)\n6. Scans for secrets: ✅ None detected\n7. Announces: \"Committing: `feat(evaluation): add Inspect AI integration`\"\n8. Executes: `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`\n9. Reports: \"✓ Committed 795efaf and pushed to GitHub\"\n\n### Example 2: Large Commit Requiring Confirmation\n\n**User**: \"commit my changes\"\n\n**Assistant**:\n1. Analyzes: \"15 files changed (+2,847 lines, -156 lines)\"\n2. Categorizes: \"Features (8 files), docs (5 files), tests (2 files)\"\n3. Risk assessment: ⚠️ **Risky** (>5 files, >500 lines, mixed types)\n4. Scans for secrets: ✅ None detected\n5. Shows confirmation:\n   ```\n   ⚠️ Large commit with mixed changes detected\n\n   Files: 15 (+2,847 lines, -156 lines)\n   Categories: Features (8), Documentation (5), Tests (2)\n   Message: \"Add evaluation framework with examples and tests\"\n\n   Consider splitting into:\n   - Commit 1: Core evaluation framework (8 files)\n   - Commit 2: Documentation (5 files)\n   - Commit 3: Tests (2 files)\n\n   Proceed with single commit? [Y/n/split]\n   ```\n6. **Waits** for user response\n\n### Example 3: Secrets Detected (Always Blocks)\n\n**User**: \"commit my changes\"\n\n**Assistant**:\n1. Reviews changes: Modified config.py (+10 lines)\n2. Scans for secrets: ❌ **FOUND** pattern matching API key\n3. **STOPS**: \"⚠️ Security Warning: Detected potential API key in config.py\"\n4. Shows matched line: `api_key = \"sk_live_...\"`\n5. Advises: \"Please use environment variables instead: `api_key = os.getenv(''API_KEY'')`\"\n6. **Does not proceed** until user confirms secrets are removed\n\n## Notes\n\n- This skill follows the git safety protocol from the Bash tool documentation\n- Commit message format includes Claude Code attribution as per project conventions\n- Always run commands sequentially (staging, committing, pushing) not in parallel\n- Adapts to project conventions rather than enforcing a single standard\n- Uses **contextual autonomy**: executes immediately for safe commits, confirms for risky ones\n- Security checks are non-negotiable - always blocks on secrets\n- Thresholds: Safe ≤ 5 files, ≤ 500 lines, not main/master, single change type\n\n## References\n\n- [Conventional Commits Specification](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)\n- [Git Commit Best Practices](https://cbea.ms/git-commit/)\n- [Pre-commit Framework](https://pre-commit.com/)\n- [Git Hooks Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/githooks)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:00:57.105Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring automated git workflow management and Conventional Commits support","zh":"适用于需要自动化git工作流管理和Conventional Commits支持的开发代理","ja":"開発エージェントが自動化されたgitワークフロー管理とConventional Commitsのサポートを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"자동화된 git 워크플로 관리 및 Conventional Commits 지원이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo que requieren una gestión de flujo de trabajo de git automatizada y soporte para Commits Convencionales","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Développement nécessitant une gestion de workflow de git automatisée et un support pour les Commits Conventionnels","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine automatisierte git-Workflow-Verwaltung und Unterstützung für Conventional Commits erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que exigem gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho git automatizado e suporte a Commits Convencionais","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих автоматизированного управления рабочим процессом git и поддержки Конвенциональных Коммитов","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يتطلب إدارة تدفق العمل التلقائي git ودعم Commits التقليدية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce meaningful commit messages, prevent secret leaks, and adhere to project conventions using torchtune YAML configurations and GitHub protocol integration, ensuring seamless git commit and push operations","zh":"赋予代理人使用torchune YAML配置和GitHub协议集成执行有意义的提交消息、防止秘密泄露和遵守项目约定，确保无缝的git提交和推送操作","ja":"torchune YAML構成とGitHubプロトコル統合を使用して、エージェントが意味のあるコミットメッセージを適用し、秘密漏洩を防ぎ、プロジェクトの規約に従うことを可能にし、無停止のgitコミットとプッシュ操作を保証する","ko":"토르튠 YAML 구성과 깃허브 프로토콜 통합을 사용하여 에이전트가 의미 있는 커밋 메시지를 적용하고, 비밀 유출을 방지하며, 프로젝트 규약을 준수하도록 하여, 무중단의 깃 커밋 및 푸시 작업을 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar mensajes de confirmación significativos, prevenir fugas de secretos y adherirse a las convenciones del proyecto utilizando configuraciones de YAML de torchtune y la integración del protocolo de GitHub, garantizando operaciones de confirmación y envío de git sin problemas","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des messages de validation significatifs, de prévenir les fuites de secrets et de se conformer aux conventions du projet en utilisant les configurations YAML de torchtune et l''intégration du protocole GitHub, garantissant des opérations de validation et d''envoi de git sans problème","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, sinnvolle Commit-Nachrichten durchzusetzen, Geheimnisverluste zu verhindern und den Projekt konventionen zu entsprechen, indem sie torchtune-YAML-Konfigurationen und GitHub-Protokollintegration verwenden, um nahtlose git-Commit- und Push-Vorgänge sicherzustellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor mensagens de commit significativas, prevenir vazamentos de segredos e aderir às convenções do projeto usando configurações YAML do torchtune e integração do protocolo GitHub, garantindo operações de commit e push git sem problemas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать значимые сообщения коммитов, предотвращать утечки секретов и соблюдать проектные конвенции с помощью конфигураций YAML torchtune и интеграции протокола GitHub, обеспечивая бесперебойные операции коммита и пуша git","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على فرض رسائل التزام ذات معنى ومنع تسرب الأسرار والامتثال لاتفاقيات المشروع باستخدام تكوينات YAML لبرنامج torchtune وتكامل بروتوكول GitHub ، مما يضمن عمليات التزام و دفع git دون مشاكل"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit message validation","Generating Conventional Commits compliant messages","Pushing changes to remote GitHub repositories"],"zh":["自动化提交消息验证","生成符合Conventional Commits的消息","推送更改到远程GitHub仓库"],"ja":["コミットメッセージの検証の自動化","Conventional Commitsに準拠したメッセージの生成","リモートGitHubリポジトリへの変更のプッシュ"],"ko":["커밋 메시지 검증 자동화","Conventional Commits 규약에 맞는 메시지 생성","원격 깃허브 저장소에 변경 사항 푸시"],"es":["Automatización de la validación de mensajes de confirmación","Generación de mensajes compatibles con Conventional Commits","Envío de cambios a repositorios remotos de GitHub"],"fr":["Automatisation de la validation des messages de validation","Génération de messages compatibles avec les Commits Conventionnels","Envoi de modifications vers des dépôts GitHub distants"],"de":["Automatisierung der Validierung von Commit-Nachrichten","Erzeugung von Conventional-Commits-konformen Nachrichten","Übertragung von Änderungen an Remote-GitHub-Repositorys"],"pt":["Automação de validação de mensagens de commit","Geração de mensagens conformes com os Commits Convencionais","Envio de alterações para repositórios remotos do GitHub"],"ru":["Автоматизация валидации сообщений коммита","Генерация сообщений, соответствующих Конвенциональным Коммитам","Отправка изменений в удаленные репозитории GitHub"],"ar":["أتمتة التحقق من صحة رسائل الالتزام","إنتاج رسائل متوافقة مع Commits التقليدية","نشر التغييرات على مستودعات GitHub عن بعد"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git installation and configuration","Supports Conventional Commits and custom formats only"],"zh":["需要git安装和配置","仅支持Conventional Commits和自定义格式"],"ja":["gitのインストールと設定が必要","Conventional Commitsとカスタム形式のみをサポート"],"ko":["깃 설치 및 구성이 필요","Conventional Commits 및 사용자 정의 형식만 지원"],"es":["Requiere la instalación y configuración de git","Soporta solo formatos personalizados y Conventional Commits"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de git","Prend en charge uniquement les formats personnalisés et les Commits Conventionnels"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation und Konfiguration von git","Unterstützt nur benutzerdefinierte Formate und Conventional Commits"],"pt":["Exige instalação e configuração do git","Suporta apenas formatos personalizados e Commits Convencionais"],"ru":["Требует установки и конфигурации git","Поддерживает только Конвенциональные Коммиты и пользовательские форматы"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين git","يدعم فقط تنسيقات Commits التقليدية والمخصصة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"282f102bee5158a3205231ff7763863f94b1eff2d813bba0290a5bff8959baae","qualityScore":55}');
