:["Автоматическая индексация Dojo","Повышение эффективности разработки","Интеграция с инструментами ИИ","Поддержка разработки приложений","Оптимизация процесса разработки"],"ar":["تحديد فهرس أوتوماتيكي ل Dojo","تحسين كفاءة التطوير","التكامل مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","دعم تطوير التطبيقات","تحسين عملية التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用AI工具创建计划","什么是自动索引器","create-a-plan的替代方案","Dojo开发工具","AI工具安装","create-a-plan设置指南","Dojo自动索引器","开发效率优化"],"ja":["AIエージェントを使用してcreate-a-planを作成する方法","自動索引器とは","create-a-planの代替ソリューション","Dojo開発ツール","AIエージェントのインストール","create-a-planの設定ガイド","Dojo自動索引器","開発効率の最適化"],"ko":["AI 에이전트를 사용하여 create-a-plan을 생성하는 방법","자동 색인器란","create-a-plan의 대체 솔루션","Dojo 개발 도구","AI 에이전트 설치","create-a-plan 설정 가이드","Dojo 자동 색인기","개발 효율성 최적화"],"es":["herramientas de AI","indexador automático","Dojo","desarrollo de aplicaciones","cómo usar herramientas de AI","mejora de la productividad","alternativas a Dojo","instalación de herramientas de AI"],"fr":["outils d''IA","indexeur automatique","Dojo","développement d''applications","comment utiliser des outils d''IA","amélioration de la productivité","alternatives à Dojo","installation d''outils d''IA"],"de":["KI-Tools","automatischer Indexierer","Dojo","Anwendungsentwicklung","wie man KI-Tools verwendet","Steigerung der Produktivität","Alternativen zu Dojo","Installation von KI-Tools"],"pt":["ferramentas de IA","indexador automático Dojo","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","otimização do desenvolvimento","create-a-plan alternative","como usar create-a-plan","guia de instalação create-a-plan","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","автоматический индексатор Dojo","разработка приложений","оптимизация разработки","create-a-plan альтернатива","как использовать create-a-plan","руководство по установке create-a-plan","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","محدد فهرس أوتوماتيكي Dojo","تطوير التطبيقات","تحسين التطوير","بديل create-a-plan","كيفية استخدام create-a-plan","دليل تثبيت create-a-plan","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"dojoengine","repo":"torii","repoPath":"dojoengine/torii","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.734Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"create-a-plan","description":"Conduct a focused technical planning interview to produce an implementable, parallelizable plan or spec with clear dependencies, risks, and open questions.","bodyPreview":"# Create a Plan Skill\n\nThis skill runs a structured technical interview to turn a rough idea or an existing spec into a detailed, implementable plan. The output is organized for parallel execution: foundations first, then independent workstreams, then merge and integration.\n\n## Invocation\n\nThe user will provide one of:\n- A path to a spec or plan file (for example: `SPEC.md`, `PLAN.md`, `RFC.md`)\n- A rough description of what they want to build\n- A feature request or problem statement\n\nOutput is","body":"# Create a Plan Skill\n\nThis skill runs a structured technical interview to turn a rough idea or an existing spec into a detailed, implementable plan. The output is organized for parallel execution: foundations first, then independent workstreams, then merge and integration.\n\n## Invocation\n\nThe user will provide one of:\n- A path to a spec or plan file (for example: `SPEC.md`, `PLAN.md`, `RFC.md`)\n- A rough description of what they want to build\n- A feature request or problem statement\n\nOutput is always written to `PLAN.md` in the repo root.\n\n## Process\n\n### Phase 0: Preflight\n\n1. If a file path is provided, read it first and note goals, non-goals, constraints, and gaps.\n2. Confirm you will produce `PLAN.md` as the output in the repo root. If `PLAN.md` already exists, update it rather than creating a new file.\n\n### Phase 1: Discovery\n\nSummarize what is known, then identify missing details. Focus on:\n- Goals and non-goals\n- Constraints (time, budget, platform, dependencies)\n- Success metrics and acceptance criteria\n\n### Phase 2: Deep Interview\n\nUse the `AskUserQuestion` (Claude) and/or `request_user_input` (Codex) tools in rounds. Ask 1-3 questions per round. Each round should go deeper and avoid repeating what is already known.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n1. Never ask obvious questions. If the codebase or spec already answers it, do not ask it again.\n2. Ask about edge cases and failure modes.\n3. Probe for hidden complexity (state transitions, migrations, concurrency).\n4. Challenge assumptions when they create risk or ambiguity.\n5. Identify parallelization boundaries and serial dependencies.\n6. If the user is unsure, propose a default and ask for confirmation.\n\nQuestion categories to cover as relevant:\n- Technical architecture and data flow\n- Data model and state management\n- API contracts and versioning\n- Caching and invalidation\n- Background jobs, retries, and idempotency\n- Error handling and recovery\n- Observability and debugging\n- Performance, scale, and SLAs\n- Security, privacy, and compliance\n- Integrations and external dependencies\n- UX flows, accessibility, and responsiveness\n- Rollout, migration, and rollback\n- Testing strategy and validation\n\n### Phase 3: Dependency Analysis\n\nIdentify:\n1. Serial dependencies that must complete first\n2. Parallel workstreams that can run independently\n3. Merge points where work reconvenes\n\n### Phase 4: Plan Generation\n\nWrite the final plan to `PLAN.md`. Ensure the plan includes concrete verification steps the agent can run end to end. If the user only wants a plan in chat, provide it inline and mention that it would be written to `PLAN.md`.\n\n## Output Format\n\nThe generated plan MUST follow this structure:\n\n```markdown\n# [Feature Name] Implementation Plan\n\n## Overview\n[2-3 sentence summary of what this implements and why]\n\n## Goals\n- [Explicit goal 1]\n- [Explicit goal 2]\n\n## Non-Goals\n- [What this explicitly does NOT do]\n\n## Assumptions and Constraints\n- [Known constraints or assumptions]\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- [Requirement]\n\n### Non-Functional\n- [Performance, reliability, security, compliance]\n\n## Technical Design\n\n### Data Model\n[Schema changes, new entities, relationships]\n\n### API Design\n[New endpoints, request/response shapes, versioning]\n\n### Architecture\n[System diagram in text or mermaid, component interactions]\n\n### UX Flow (if applicable)\n[Key screens, loading states, error recovery]\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### Serial Dependencies (Must Complete First)\n\nThese tasks create foundations that other work depends on. Complete in order.\n\n#### Phase 0: [Foundation Name]\n**Prerequisite for:** All subsequent phases\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| 0.1 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n| 0.2 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n---\n\n### Parallel Workstreams\n\nThese workstreams can be executed independently after Phase 0.\n\n#### Workstream A: [Name]\n**Dependencies:** Phase 0\n**Can parallelize with:** Workstreams B, C\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| A.1 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n| A.2 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n#### Workstream B: [Name]\n**Dependencies:** Phase 0\n**Can parallelize with:** Workstreams A, C\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| B.1 | [Task description] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n---\n\n### Merge Phase\n\nAfter parallel workstreams complete, these tasks integrate the work.\n\n#### Phase N: Integration\n**Dependencies:** Workstreams A, B, C\n\n| Task | Description | Output |\n|------|-------------|--------|\n| N.1 | [Integration task] | [Concrete deliverable] |\n\n---\n\n## Testing and Validation\n\n- [Unit, integration, end-to-end coverage]\n- [Manual test plan if needed]\n\n## Rollout and Migration\n\n- [Feature flags, staged rollout, migration steps]\n- [Rollback plan]\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n- [Exact commands or manual steps the agent can run to verify correctness]\n- [Expected outputs or success criteria]\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------------|--------|------------|\n| [Risk description] | Low/Med/High | Low/Med/High | [Strategy] |\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- [ ] [Question that still needs resolution]\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| Decision | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----------|-----------|------------------------|\n| [Decision made] | [Why] | [What else was considered] |\n```\n\n## Interview Flow Example\n\nRound 1: High-Level Architecture\n- \"The spec mentions a sync engine. Is this push-based (webhooks), pull-based (polling), or event-driven (queue)?\"\n- \"What is the expected data volume and throughput?\"\n\nRound 2: Edge Cases\n- \"If a batch fails mid-run, do we retry the whole batch or resume from a checkpoint?\"\n- \"What happens when source data is deleted but still referenced downstream?\"\n\nRound 3: Parallelization\n- \"Can we process different categories independently, or are there cross-category dependencies?\"\n- \"Is there a natural partition key that allows sharding?\"\n\nRound 4: Operational\n- \"What is the acceptable latency for sync or processing?\"\n- \"How will operators debug failures and what visibility do they need?\"\n\n## Key Behaviors\n\n1. Persist until the plan is implementable and verifiable by the agent, but avoid user fatigue by batching questions.\n2. Challenge vague answers when they affect design decisions.\n3. Identify hidden work and operational overhead.\n4. Think about the merge and integration steps early.\n5. Summarize understanding and confirm before writing the final plan.\n\n## Completing the Interview\n\nAfter sufficient rounds of questions:\n1. Summarize your understanding back to the user\n2. Confirm the parallelization strategy\n3. Write the complete plan to the target file\n4. Ask if any sections need refinement\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:02:54.235Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Writing Agents and Project Management AI needing structured plan generation from rough ideas or specs.","zh":"适合技术写作代理和项目管理AI，需要从粗略想法或规格生成结构化计划。","ja":"技術文章作成エージェントやプロジェクト管理AIに適しており、粗いアイデアや仕様から構造化された計画を生成する必要があります。","ko":"기술 문서 작성을 위한 에이전트와 프로젝트 관리 AI에 적합하며, 粗略한 아이디어나 사양에서 구조화된 계획을 생성하는 것이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Escritura Técnica y Gestión de Proyectos de IA que necesitan generación de planes estructurados a partir de ideas o especificaciones rudimentarias.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''écriture technique et la gestion de projet d''IA nécessitant une génération de plans structurés à partir d''idées ou de spécifications rudimentaires.","de":"Ideal für technische Schreibagenten und Projektmanagement-KI, die eine strukturierte Planerstellung aus groben Ideen oder Spezifikationen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Escrita Técnica e Gerenciamento de Projetos de IA que necessitam de geração de planos estruturados a partir de ideias ou especificações rudimentares.","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов написания и агентов ИИ по управлению проектами, которым необходима генерация структурированных планов из грубых идей или спецификаций.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النصيين الفنيين وإدارة المشاريع الإصطناعية التي تحتاج إلى توليد خطط منظم من الأفكار أو المواصفات الخشنة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform rough descriptions or existing specs into detailed, implementable plans with organized parallel execution, leveraging foundations, independent workstreams, and merge and integration strategies, supporting file formats like Markdown (.md) for spec and plan files.","zh":"赋予代理能力，将粗略的描述或现有的规格转换为详细的、可实施的计划，具有组织化的并行执行，利用基础、独立的工作流和合并和集成策略，支持Markdown (.md)等文件格式的规格和计划文件。","ja":"エージェントに、粗い説明や既存の仕様を詳細で実行可能な計画に変換する能力を与え、基盤、独立したワークフロー、統合戦略を活用し、Markdown (.md) などのファイル形式をサポートする仕様および計画ファイルを生成します。","ko":"에이전트에게 粗略한 설명이나 기존의 사양을 상세하고实施 가능한 계획으로 변환하는 능력을 부여하며, 기초, 독립적인 작업 흐름, 병합 및 통합 전략을 활용하여 Markdown (.md)와 같은 파일 형식의 사양 및 계획 파일을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar descripciones rudimentarias o especificaciones existentes en planes detallados e implementables con ejecución paralela organizada, aprovechando fundamentos, flujos de trabajo independientes y estrategias de fusión e integración, y admitiendo formatos de archivo como Markdown (.md) para archivos de especificaciones y planes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des descriptions rudimentaires ou des spécifications existantes en plans détaillés et réalisables avec une exécution parallèle organisée, en exploitant les fondements, les flux de travail indépendants et les stratégies de fusion et d''intégration, et en prenant en charge des formats de fichiers tels que Markdown (.md) pour les fichiers de spécifications et de plans.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, grobe Beschreibungen oder bestehende Spezifikationen in detaillierte und umsetzbare Pläne mit organisierter paralleler Ausführung umzuwandeln, indem sie Grundlagen, unabhängige Arbeitsabläufe und Merge- und Integrationsstrategien nutzen und Dateiformate wie Markdown (.md) für Spezifikations- und Plan-Dateien unterstützen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar descrições rudimentares ou especificações existentes em planos detalhados e implementáveis com execução paralela organizada, aproveitando fundamentos, fluxos de trabalho independentes e estratégias de mesclagem e integração, suportando formatos de arquivo como Markdown (.md) para arquivos de especificação e plano.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовывать грубые описания или существующие спецификации в подробные и реализуемые планы с организованной параллельной выполнением, используя основы, независимые потоки работы и стратегии слияния и интеграции, поддерживая форматы файлов, такие как Markdown (.md) для файлов спецификаций и планов.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحويل الوصف الخشن أو المواصفات الحالية إلى خطط مفصلة وقابلة للتطبيق مع تنفيذ موازٍ منظمة، مستفيدة من الأسس والتدفقات العمل المستقلة واستراتيجيات الدمج والتكامل، ودعم صيغ الملفات مثل Markdown (.md) لملفات المواصفات والخطط."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating detailed project plans from feature requests","Organizing specs into actionable workstreams","Creating implementable plans from problem statements"],"zh":["从功能请求生成详细的项目计划","将规格组织成可执行的工作流","从问题陈述创建可实施的计划"],"ja":["機能要求から詳細なプロジェクト計画を生成する","仕様を実行可能なワークフローに組織する","問題文から実行可能な計画を作成する"],"ko":["기능 요청에서 상세한 프로젝트 계획을 생성하는 것","사양을 실행 가능한 작업 흐름으로 조직하는 것","문제 문장에서 실행 가능한 계획을 생성하는 것"],"es":["Generación de planes de proyecto detallados a partir de solicitudes de características","Organización de especificaciones en flujos de trabajo realizables","Creación de planes implementables a partir de declaraciones de problemas"],"fr":["Génération de plans de projet détaillés à partir de demandes de fonctionnalités","Organisation de spécifications en flux de travail réalisables","Création de plans réalisables à partir de déclarations de problèmes"],"de":["Erstellung detaillierter Projektpläne aus Funktionsanforderungen","Organisation von Spezifikationen in umsetzbare Arbeitsabläufe","Erstellung umsetzbarer Pläne aus Problembeschreibungen"],"pt":["Geração de planos de projeto detalhados a partir de solicitações de recursos","Organização de especificações em fluxos de trabalho realizáveis","Criação de planos implementáveis a partir de declarações de problemas"],"ru":["Генерация подробных планов проекта из запросов функций","Организация спецификаций в реализуемые потоки работы","Создание реализуемых планов из заявлений о проблемах"],"ar":["توليد خطط مشروع مفصلة من طلبات الميزات","تنظيم المواصفات في تدفقات عمل قابلة للتنفيذ","إنشاء خطط قابلة للتطبيق من بيانات المشاكل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires input in the form of a spec or plan file (e.g., SPEC.md, PLAN.md, RFC.md) or a rough description of the project"],"zh":["需要以规格或计划文件（例如 SPEC.md、PLAN.md、RFC.md）的形式输入或粗略的项目描述"],"ja":["仕様または計画ファイル（例： SPEC.md、PLAN.md、RFC.md）の形式で入力する必要があります、またはプロジェクトの粗い説明"],"ko":["사양이나 계획 파일(예: SPEC.md, PLAN.md, RFC.md)의 형식으로 입력이 필요하거나, 프로젝트에 대한 粗略한 설명"],"es":["Requiere una entrada en forma de archivo de especificación o plan (por ejemplo, SPEC.md, PLAN.md, RFC.md) o una descripción rudimentaria del proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée sous la forme d''un fichier de spécification ou de plan (par exemple, SPEC.md, PLAN.md, RFC.md) ou d''une description rudimentaire du projet"],"de":["Benötigt eine Eingabe in Form einer Spezifikations- oder Plan-Datei (z. B. SPEC.md, PLAN.md, RFC.md) oder einer groben Beschreibung des Projekts"],"pt":["Exige entrada na forma de um arquivo de especificação ou plano (por exemplo, SPEC.md, PLAN.md, RFC.md) ou uma descrição rudimentar do projeto"],"ru":["Требует ввода в форме файла спецификации или плана (например, SPEC.md, PLAN.md, RFC.md) или грубого описания проекта"],"ar":["يتطلب الإدخال في شكل ملف مواصفات أو خطة (على سبيل المثال، SPEC.md، PLAN.md، RFC.md) أو وصف مشروع خشن"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"76755dca1a8ade8c8e895de1efdf62f805b008bf3c8a9c427ad3a6c8bb1c1ddd","qualityScore":55}');
