ür CLI und andere Entwicklungsumgebungen","Code-Analyse und Optimierungs-Empfehlungen","Integration mit AI-Coding-Assistenten"],"pt":["Melhoria da produtividade dos desenvolvedores","Assistentes de codificação de IA avançados","Integração com React, Python e Node.js","Suporte a CLI e Agent","Otimização de código e depuração"],"ru":["Повышение производительности разработчиков","Продвинутые ИИ-ассистенты кодирования","Интеграция с React, Python и Node.js","Поддержка CLI и Agent","Оптимизация кода и отладка"],"ar":["تحسين إنتاجية المطورين","مساعدي الترميز الذكي المتقدمة","التكامل مع React و Python و Node.js","دعم CLI و Agent","تحسين الكود و تصحيح الأخطاء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用pSEO技能","什么是pSEO技术","pSEO技能替代方案","pSEO技能与其他工具比较","pSEO技能安装指南","pSEO技能设置教程","AI编码助手pSEO技能","pSEO技能开发框架","pSEO技能搜索引擎优化"],"ja":["pSEOスキルの使用方法","pSEOスキルとは","pSEOスキル代替","pSEOスキルと他のツールの比較","pSEOスキルのインストールガイド","pSEOスキルの設定チュートリアル","AIエージェントpSEOスキル","pSEOスキル開発フレームワーク","pSEOスキル検索エンジン最適化"],"ko":["pSEO 기술 사용 방법","pSEO 기술이란","pSEO 기술 대체","pSEO 기술과 다른 도구 비교","pSEO 기술 설치 가이드","pSEO 기술 설정 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트 pSEO 기술","pSEO 기술 개발 프레임워크","pSEO 기술 검색 엔진 최적화"],"es":["cómo usar pSEO","qué es pSEO","herramientas de pSEO","pSEO vs SEO","instalar pSEO","guía de configuración de pSEO","asistentes de codificación de IA","optimización de motores de búsqueda para desarrolladores"],"fr":["comment utiliser pSEO","qu''est-ce que pSEO","outils de pSEO","pSEO vs SEO","installer pSEO","guide de configuration de pSEO","assistants de codage de l''IA","optimisation de moteurs de recherche pour développeurs"],"de":["wie man pSEO verwendet","was ist pSEO","pSEO-Tools","pSEO vs SEO","pSEO installieren","pSEO-Konfigurationsanleitung","AI-Coding-Assistenten","Suchmaschinen-Optimierung für Entwickler"],"pt":["como usar pseo-discovery","o que é pseo-discovery","pseo-discovery vs alternativas","instalar pseo-discovery","guia de configuração pseo-discovery","pseo-discovery para desenvolvedores","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvimento","melhorias de produtividade para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать pseo-discovery","что такое pseo-discovery","pseo-discovery vs альтернативы","установить pseo-discovery","руководство по настройке pseo-discovery","pseo-discovery для разработчиков","инструменты ИИ для разработки","повышение производительности для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام pseo-discovery","ما هي pseo-discovery","pseo-discovery vs البدائل","تثبيت pseo-discovery","دليل إعداد pseo-discovery","pseo-discovery للمطورين","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للتطوير","تحسين إنتاجية المطورين"]}},"owner":"lisbeth718","repo":"pseo-skills","repoPath":"lisbeth718/pseo-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.763Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"pseo-discovery","description":"Analyze a codebase and business context to discover programmatic SEO opportunities, identifying what page types to generate, what data assets exist, and what search intent can be matched at scale. Use when starting a new pSEO project, when the user isnt sure what to build programmatically, or when exploring what structured data exists in the codebase or business that could power scalable pages.","bodyPreview":"# pSEO Discovery\n\nAnalyze the codebase, business context, and market to determine what programmatic SEO pages can and should be built. This skill answers the question: **\"What should we generate, and do we have the data to do it?\"**\n\nThis skill runs BEFORE pseo-audit. The audit checks if the codebase is ready; this skill figures out what to build.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Data-first**: Only propose page types backed by structured data that exists or can be sourced\n2. **Intent-matched**: Every p","body":"# pSEO Discovery\n\nAnalyze the codebase, business context, and market to determine what programmatic SEO pages can and should be built. This skill answers the question: **\"What should we generate, and do we have the data to do it?\"**\n\nThis skill runs BEFORE pseo-audit. The audit checks if the codebase is ready; this skill figures out what to build.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Data-first**: Only propose page types backed by structured data that exists or can be sourced\n2. **Intent-matched**: Every proposed page type must target a real search intent with volume\n3. **Differentiated**: Each page must be able to produce genuinely unique content — not just variable swaps\n4. **Feasible**: Proposals must be realistic given the current data, codebase, and team capacity\n5. **Business-aligned**: pSEO pages should serve the business''s actual audience and goals\n\n## Discovery Procedure\n\n### 1. Explore the Codebase for Data Assets\n\nSearch the codebase for existing structured data that could power pages:\n\n**Database/ORM models:**\n- Search for schema definitions (Prisma, Drizzle, TypeORM, Mongoose, SQL migrations)\n- Identify entities with many records (products, locations, services, users, listings, articles)\n- Note which entities have rich attributes (descriptions, categories, images, metadata)\n\n**CMS content types:**\n- Check for headless CMS configs (Contentful, Sanity, Strapi, etc.)\n- Identify content types and their field schemas\n- Count records per content type\n\n**API endpoints:**\n- Map all API routes and their response shapes\n- Identify list endpoints that return collections of entities\n- Check for paginated endpoints (signals large datasets)\n\n**Static data files:**\n- Search for JSON, CSV, YAML, MDX files in `data/`, `content/`, `src/data/` directories\n- Count records and inspect field richness\n- Check for categorization or taxonomy structures\n\n**What to extract per data source:**\n- Entity name and count (e.g., \"2,500 products\", \"150 cities\", \"80 services\")\n- Available fields (especially: name, description, category, attributes, images)\n- Relationships between entities (product → category, service → location)\n- Data freshness (how often updated, is there a lastModified field)\n\n### 2. Map Business Entities to Page Types\n\nFor each data asset found, evaluate whether it can power a pSEO page type:\n\n| Question | Must answer \"yes\" |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| Are there 50+ unique records? | Minimum for pSEO to make sense |\n| Does each record have enough data for a full page? | Title, description, 3+ unique attributes |\n| Would someone search for this? | Real search intent exists |\n| Can each page be meaningfully different? | Not just variable swaps |\n| Does this serve the business? | Drives traffic the business can convert |\n\n**Common pSEO page patterns by business type:**\n\n- **E-commerce**: Product pages, category pages, brand pages, `[product] vs [product]` comparisons, `best [category] for [use-case]`\n- **SaaS**: Feature pages, integration pages, `[tool] alternative`, `[tool] vs [competitor]`, use-case pages\n- **Marketplace**: Listing pages, location pages, `[service] in [city]`, category + location combinations\n- **Content/Media**: Topic pages, tag pages, author pages, `[topic] guide`, glossary/definition pages\n- **Local business**: Service + location pages, `[service] in [neighborhood]`, FAQ pages per service\n- **Directory**: Profile pages, category pages, comparison pages, `top [category] in [location]`\n\n### 3. Identify Keyword Patterns and Search Intent\n\nFor each proposed page type, validate that search demand exists:\n\n**Keyword pattern analysis:**\n- Identify the base keyword pattern (e.g., `[service] in [city]`, `best [product] for [use-case]`)\n- Estimate volume per pattern using keyword research tools or inferred demand\n- Check for long-tail variations that indicate intent depth\n- Verify that existing top results are not exclusively high-authority domains\n\n**Intent classification per page type:**\n- **Informational**: User wants to learn (guides, definitions, how-tos)\n- **Commercial investigation**: User is comparing options (comparisons, reviews, \"best X\")\n- **Transactional**: User wants to buy/sign up (product pages, pricing, service pages)\n- **Navigational**: User wants a specific entity (brand pages, location pages)\n\nEach pSEO page type should clearly map to one intent category.\n\n### 4. Evaluate Data Sufficiency for Content Uniqueness\n\nFor each proposed page type, assess whether the data produces genuinely unique pages:\n\n**The Content Differentiation Test:**\nTake 5 random records. For each, write out what the page would contain:\n- Title\n- H1\n- Intro paragraph\n- Main content sections\n- FAQ questions\n\nIf 3+ of these elements are essentially the same text with different proper nouns, the data is insufficient. Either:\n- Enrich the data (add more attributes, descriptions, FAQs per record)\n- Combine data sources (e.g., product data + user reviews + competitor data)\n- Narrow the page type to records with richer data\n- Abandon the page type as a pSEO candidate\n\n**Minimum data requirements per page:**\n- 2+ unique text fields beyond title and description (for body content)\n- 3+ structured attributes (for data tables, stat highlights)\n- Category or taxonomy data (for hub-spoke linking)\n- Ideally: 3-5 FAQ pairs per record (for FAQ schema and content depth)\n\n### 5. Assess URL Structure and Taxonomy\n\nPropose a URL hierarchy for the pSEO pages:\n\n```\n/{category}/{slug}                     # standard\n/{location}/{service}                  # location-based\n/{product-type}/{product-slug}         # e-commerce\n/{topic}/{subtopic}                    # content-based\n```\n\nCheck:\n- Will all slugs be unique within their URL namespace?\n- Does the hierarchy create natural hub-spoke relationships?\n- Is the URL structure human-readable and keyword-inclusive?\n- How deep is the hierarchy? (Maximum 3 levels recommended)\n\n### 6. Competitive Landscape Check\n\nIdentify whether competitors are already doing pSEO for the same patterns:\n\n- Search for the target keyword patterns and see what ranks\n- Check if competitors have programmatic pages (signs: similar URL patterns, templated content, large indexed page counts)\n- Assess competitor content quality — can you do meaningfully better?\n- Look for gaps they haven''t covered (long-tail variations, underserved locations, new categories)\n\n### 7. Propose a pSEO Strategy\n\nCompile findings into a ranked list of pSEO opportunities.\n\n## Output Format\n\n```\n## pSEO Discovery Report\n\n### Data Assets Found\n| Entity | Record Count | Key Fields | Source |\n|--------|-------------|------------|--------|\n| [entity] | [count] | [fields] | [DB/CMS/API/files] |\n\n### Proposed Page Types (ranked by opportunity)\n\n#### 1. [Page Type Name]\n- **Pattern**: [URL pattern, e.g., /services/[service]-in-[city]]\n- **Record count**: [number of pages this would generate]\n- **Search intent**: [informational / commercial / transactional]\n- **Keyword pattern**: [e.g., \"[service] in [city]\"]\n- **Data source**: [where the data comes from]\n- **Content uniqueness**: [High / Medium / Low — with justification]\n- **Data gaps**: [what fields are missing or need enrichment]\n- **Feasibility**: [Ready / Needs data enrichment / Needs new data source]\n\n#### 2. [Next page type...]\n\n### Rejected Candidates\n| Entity | Reason Rejected |\n|--------|----------------|\n| [entity] | [too few records / insufficient data / no search intent / ...] |\n\n### Recommended URL Structure\n[Proposed hierarchy with examples]\n\n### Data Enrichment Needed\n[List of data fields that need to be added to unlock page types]\n\n### Next Steps\n1. [Confirm page types with stakeholder]\n2. [Enrich data where needed]\n3. [Run pseo-audit on the codebase]\n4. [Begin implementation with pseo-data]\n```\n\n## Scope Parameter\n\nIf `$ARGUMENTS` specifies a focus:\n- `all` (default): Full discovery\n- `codebase`: Only analyze existing data assets in the code (steps 1-2)\n- `business`: Focus on business entity mapping and page type proposals (steps 2-4)\n- `keywords`: Focus on keyword patterns and competitive landscape (steps 3, 6)\n\n## YMYL Risk Assessment\n\nGoogle''s September 2025 Quality Rater Guidelines expanded YMYL (Your Money or Your Life) to include civic information alongside health, finance, and legal content. pSEO in YMYL verticals carries elevated risk.\n\n**YMYL categories (as of September 2025):**\n- Health and medical information\n- Financial information (investing, taxes, loans, insurance)\n- Legal information\n- Civic information (voting, government, public trust)\n- Safety information (product safety, emergency procedures)\n- News about major events\n\n**If the proposed page types fall into ANY YMYL category:**\n\n1. **Flag the risk explicitly** in the discovery report\n2. **Elevate content quality requirements**: Every page needs cited authoritative sources, expert attribution, and review processes\n3. **Evaluate if pSEO is appropriate at all**: YMYL content often requires human expert review per page, which conflicts with the \"programmatic\" approach. Be honest about this tension.\n4. **Recommend stricter quality guard thresholds**: Higher minimum word counts, stricter uniqueness requirements, mandatory E-E-A-T fields\n5. **Consider hybrid approach**: Programmatic data structure + human-reviewed content per page\n\n**Discovery output should include a YMYL assessment:**\n```\n### YMYL Assessment\n- YMYL category: [None | Health | Finance | Legal | Civic | Safety]\n- Risk level: [Low | Medium | High]\n- Recommendation: [Standard pSEO OK | Needs elevated quality standards | Human review per page required | pSEO not recommended for this vertical]\n```\n\n## Output Artifact\n\nSave the discovery report to `.pseo/discovery-report.md` in the project root. This file is consumed by pseo-audit and pseo-orchestrate to inform subsequent phases. The file must include at minimum:\n\n- Confirmed page types with their URL patterns\n- Data source locations (file paths, API endpoints, CMS content types)\n- YMYL assessment (if applicable)\n- Data gaps that need enrichment before implementation\n\nIf running within a single Claude Code session, the report can also be kept in conversation context. The file serves as a persistent artifact for multi-session workflows.\n\n## Important Constraints\n\n- This is a research-only skill. Do NOT modify code or create files.\n- Be honest about data gaps. Don''t propose page types the data can''t support.\n- Quantity of pages is not the goal. 200 genuinely unique pages beats 5,000 thin pages.\n- If the codebase has no usable structured data, say so. The answer may be \"build the data layer first\" or \"this business isn''t a good fit for pSEO.\"\n- If a page type would produce thin or near-identical pages, flag it as rejected with a clear reason.\n\n## Relationship to Other Skills\n\n- **Runs before**: All other pseo-* skills\n- **Feeds into**: pseo-audit (what to look for), pseo-data (what models to build)\n- **Independent of**: All implementation skills — this is pure research\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:16:02.027Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for SEO-focused AI Coding Assistants needing advanced programmatic page analysis and generation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级程序化页面分析和生成功能的SEO专注AI编码助手。","ja":"SEOに特化したAIコーディングアシスタントが、高度なプログラムによるページ分析および生成機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 프로그램화된 페이지 분석 및 생성 기능이 필요한 SEO 중심의 AI 코딩 어시스턴트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para asistentes de codificación de AI enfocados en SEO que necesitan capacidades de análisis y generación de páginas programáticas avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les assistants de codage IA axés sur le SEO nécessitant des capacités d''analyse et de génération de pages programmatiques avancées.","de":"Perfekt für SEO-fokussierte AI-Coding-Assistenten, die erweiterte programmatische Seitenanalyse- und Generierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Assistente de Codificação de IA focado em SEO que necessita de capacidades avançadas de análise e geração de páginas programáticas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для SEO-ориентированных помощников кодирования ИИ, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности программной аналитики и генерации страниц.","ar":"مثالي لمرافق كتابة الشفرة الإصطناعية التي تركز على تحسين محركات البحث وتحتاج إلى قدرات تحليل وإنشاء صفحات متقدمة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to determine optimal programmatic SEO page types using data-first and intent-matched principles, backed by structured data analysis and market research, leveraging protocols like data sourcing and business context evaluation.","zh":"赋予代理人使用数据优先和意图匹配原则确定最佳程序化SEO页面类型的能力，依靠结构化数据分析和市场研究，并利用数据来源和业务背景评估等协议。","ja":"データ優先と意図の一致の原則を使用して、構造化データ分析と市場調査をバックアップし、データソーシングやビジネスコンテキスト評価などのプロトコルを利用して、最適なプログラムによるSEOページタイプを決定するエージェントの能力を提供します。","ko":"데이터 우선 및 의도 일치 원칙을 사용하여 구조화된 데이터 분석 및 시장 연구를 백업하고 데이터 소싱 및 비즈니스 컨텍스트 평가와 같은 프로토콜을 활용하여 최적의 프로그램화된 SEO 페이지 유형을 결정하는 에이전트의 능력을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a determinar los tipos de páginas de SEO programáticos óptimos utilizando principios de datos y coincidencia de intención, respaldados por análisis de datos estructurados e investigación de mercado, aprovechando protocolos como la obtención de datos y la evaluación del contexto empresarial.","fr":"Permet aux agents de déterminer les types de pages SEO programmatiques optimaux en utilisant des principes de données et de correspondance d''intention, étayés par l''analyse de données structurées et la recherche de marché, en exploitant des protocoles tels que la fourniture de données et l''évaluation du contexte commercial.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die optimalen programmtischen SEO-Seitentypen unter Verwendung von datenbasierten und intent-gesicherten Prinzipien zu bestimmen, die durch strukturierte Datenanalyse und Marktforschung unterstützt werden und Protokolle wie Datenquellen und Geschäftskontextbewertung nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a determinarem os tipos de página de SEO programático ótimos, usando princípios baseados em dados e correspondência de intenção, apoiados por análise de dados estruturados e pesquisa de mercado, aproveitando protocolos como obtenção de dados e avaliação de contexto empresarial.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью определять оптимальные типы страниц для программного SEO, используя принципы, основанные на данных и соответствующие намерениям, подтвержденные анализом структурированных данных и рыночными исследованиями, используя протоколы, такие как получение данных и оценка делового контекста.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تحديد أنواع الصفحات المثلى لتحسين محركات البحث البرمجي باستخدام مبادئ الأولى للبيانات والتوافق في القصد، مدعومة بتحليل البيانات المنظمة وأبحاث السوق، واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل حصول على البيانات وتقييم السياق التجاري"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating page type discovery for improved search engine rankings","Generating programmatic SEO page recommendations based on existing data","Evaluating market demand for specific page types to inform development"],"zh":["自动化页面类型发现以提高搜索引擎排名","根据现有数据生成程序化SEO页面推荐","评估特定页面类型的市场需求以指导开发"],"ja":["検索エンジンランキングの向上のためのページタイプの自動発見","既存のデータに基づいてプログラムによるSEOページの推奨を生成する","開発の参考となる特定のページタイプの市場需要の評価"],"ko":["검색 엔진 순위 개선을 위한 페이지 유형 자동 발견","기존 데이터에 기반한 프로그램화된 SEO 페이지 추천 생성","개발을 위한 특정 페이지 유형의 시장 수요 평가"],"es":["Automatizar el descubrimiento de tipos de páginas para mejorar los rankings de los motores de búsqueda","Generar recomendaciones de páginas SEO programáticas basadas en datos existentes","Evaluar la demanda del mercado para tipos de páginas específicas para informar el desarrollo"],"fr":["Automatiser la découverte de types de pages pour améliorer les classements des moteurs de recherche","Générer des recommandations de pages SEO programmatiques basées sur des données existantes","Évaluer la demande du marché pour des types de pages spécifiques pour éclairer le développement"],"de":["Automatisieren der Seitentypen-Erkennung für verbesserte Suchmaschinen-Rankings","Generieren von programmatischen SEO-Seiten-Empfehlungen basierend auf vorhandenen Daten","Bewertung der Marktnachfrage für bestimmte Seitentypen, um die Entwicklung zu unterstützen"],"pt":["Automatizar a descoberta de tipos de páginas para melhorar os rankings de motores de busca","Gerar recomendações de páginas de SEO programático com base em dados existentes","Avaliar a demanda de mercado para tipos de páginas específicos para informar o desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обнаружение типов страниц для улучшения рейтинга поисковых систем","Генерировать рекомендации по страницам программного SEO на основе существующих данных","Оценить спрос на рынке на определенные типы страниц для информирования разработки"],"ar":["تحسين اكتشاف أنواع الصفحات لتحسين تصنيف محركات البحث","توليد توصيات لصفحات تحسين محركات البحث البرمجي بناءً على البيانات الحالية","تقييم الطلب السوقي لأنواع صفحات محددة لإبلاغ التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to structured data and business context information","Must be used in conjunction with pseo-audit for comprehensive SEO analysis"],"zh":["需要访问结构化数据和业务背景信息","必须与pseo-audit一起使用以进行全面SEO分析"],"ja":["構造化データとビジネスコンテキスト情報へのアクセスが必要","包括的なSEO分析を行うために、pseo-auditと併用する必要がある"],"ko":["구조화된 데이터 및 비즈니스 컨텍스트 정보에 대한 액세스가 필요","전체 SEO 분석을 수행하기 위해 pseo-audit와 함께 사용해야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a datos estructurados y información de contexto empresarial","Debe utilizarse en conjunción con pseo-audit para un análisis SEO completo"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à des données structurées et à des informations de contexte commercial","Doit être utilisé en conjonction avec pseo-audit pour une analyse SEO complète"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf strukturierte Daten und Geschäftskontextinformationen","Muss in Verbindung mit pseo-audit für eine umfassende SEO-Analyse verwendet werden"],"pt":["Exige acesso a dados estruturados e informações de contexto empresarial","Deve ser usado em conjunto com o pseo-audit para análise abrangente de SEO"],"ru":["Требует доступа к структурированным данным и информации о деловом контексте","Должно использоваться в сочетании с pseo-audit для всестороннего анализа SEO"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى البيانات المنظمة ومعلومات السياق التجاري","يجب استخدامه بالاشتراك مع pseo-audit للتحليل الشامل لتحسين محركات البحث"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c8f5e10b74b2d7159306fe6d22e006b1a52ee8a4dccc9e1315e15aab560a3203","qualityScore":55}');
