e für komplexe Anwendungen","Effizientes Entwicklung mit KI","Solide Basis für Anwendungen","Integration mit aktuellen Technologien","Flexibilität und Anpassung"],"pt":["Boiler plate para aplicações complexas","Integração com AI Agents","Criação de soluções personalizadas","Desenvolvimento de aplicações escaláveis","Suporte a tecnologias de ponta"],"ru":["Инструмент для создания сложных приложений","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами","Создание индивидуальных решений","Разработка масштабируемых приложений","Поддержка передовых технологий"],"ar":["أداة للتعامل مع المتطلبات المعقدة","التكامل مع وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","إنشاء حلول مخصصة","تطوير تطبيقات قابلة للتوسعة","دعم التقنيات الحديثة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Elysia.js教程","AIエージェント是什么","如何使用Elysia.js","Elysia.js替代品","Elysia.js安装","Elysia.js设置指南","复杂应用开发","AIエージェント开发"],"ja":["Elysia.jsチュートリアル","AIエージェントとは","Elysia.jsの使い方","Elysia.jsの代替","Elysia.jsのインストール","Elysia.jsの設定ガイド","複雑なアプリケーションの開発","AIエージェントの開発"],"ko":["Elysia.js 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트란","Elysia.js 사용법","Elysia.js 대체","Elysia.js 설치","Elysia.js 설정 가이드","복잡한 애플리케이션 개발","AI 에이전트 개발"],"es":["herramientas de AI","desarrollo de aplicaciones","elysia.js","plantilla para aplicaciones complejas","cómo usar elysia.js","alternativas a elysia.js","elysia.js vs otros frameworks","instalación de elysia.js","guía de configuración de elysia.js"],"fr":["outils IA","développement d''applications","elysia.js","modèle pour applications complexes","comment utiliser elysia.js","alternatives à elysia.js","elysia.js vs autres frameworks","installation d''elysia.js","guide de configuration d''elysia.js"],"de":["KI-Tools","Anwendungsentwicklung","elysia.js","Boilerplate für komplexe Anwendungen","wie man elysia.js verwendet","Alternativen zu elysia.js","elysia.js vs andere Frameworks","Installation von elysia.js","Konfigurationsanleitung für elysia.js"],"pt":["como usar elysia.js","o que é elysia.js","elysia.js alternative","elysia.js vs react","instalar elysia.js","guia de configuração elysia.js","desenvolvimento de aplicações com elysia.js"],"ru":["как использовать elysia.js","что такое elysia.js","elysia.js альтернатива","elysia.js vs react","установить elysia.js","руководство по настройке elysia.js","разработка приложений с elysia.js"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام elysia.js","ما هو elysia.js","بديل elysia.js","elysia.js مقابل react","تثبيت elysia.js","دليل إعداد elysia.js","تطوير التطبيقات مع elysia.js"]}},"owner":"yukikwi","repo":"elysia-boiler-plate","repoPath":"yukikwi/elysia-boiler-plate","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.872Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"elysiajs","description":"Create backend with ElysiaJS, a type-safe, high-performance framework.","bodyPreview":"# ElysiaJS Development Skill\n\nAlways consult [elysiajs.com/llms.txt](https://elysiajs.com/llms.txt) for code examples and latest API.\n\n## Overview\n\nElysiaJS is a TypeScript framework for building Bun-first (but not limited to Bun) type-safe, high-performance backend servers. This skill provides comprehensive guidance for developing with Elysia, including routing, validation, authentication, plugins, integrations, and deployment.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nTrigger this skill when the user asks t","body":"# ElysiaJS Development Skill\n\nAlways consult [elysiajs.com/llms.txt](https://elysiajs.com/llms.txt) for code examples and latest API.\n\n## Overview\n\nElysiaJS is a TypeScript framework for building Bun-first (but not limited to Bun) type-safe, high-performance backend servers. This skill provides comprehensive guidance for developing with Elysia, including routing, validation, authentication, plugins, integrations, and deployment.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nTrigger this skill when the user asks to:\n- Create or modify ElysiaJS routes, handlers, or servers\n- Setup validation with TypeBox or other schema libraries (Zod, Valibot)\n- Implement authentication (JWT, session-based, macros, guards)\n- Add plugins (CORS, OpenAPI, Static files, JWT)\n- Integrate with external services (Drizzle ORM, Better Auth, Next.js, Eden Treaty)\n- Setup WebSocket endpoints for real-time features\n- Create unit tests for Elysia instances\n- Deploy Elysia servers to production\n\n## Quick Start\nQuick scaffold:\n```bash\nbun create elysia app\n```\n\n### Basic Server\n```typescript\nimport { Elysia, t, status } from ''elysia''\n\nconst app = new Elysia()\n  \t.get(''/'', () => ''Hello World'')\n   \t.post(''/user'', ({ body }) => body, {\n    \tbody: t.Object({\n      \t\tname: t.String(),\n        \tage: t.Number()\n     \t})\n    })\n    .get(''/id/:id'', ({ params: { id } }) => {\n   \t\tif(id > 1_000_000) return status(404, ''Not Found'')\n     \n     \treturn id\n    }, {\n    \tparams: t.Object({\n     \t\tid: t.Number({\n       \t\t\tminimum: 1\n       \t\t})\n     \t}),\n     \tresponse: {\n      \t\t200: t.Number(),\n        \t404: t.Literal(''Not Found'')\n      \t}\n    })\n    .listen(3000)\n```\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n### HTTP Methods\n```typescript\nimport { Elysia } from ''elysia''\n\nnew Elysia()\n  .get(''/'', ''GET'')\n  .post(''/'', ''POST'')\n  .put(''/'', ''PUT'')\n  .patch(''/'', ''PATCH'')\n  .delete(''/'', ''DELETE'')\n  .options(''/'', ''OPTIONS'')\n  .head(''/'', ''HEAD'')\n```\n\n### Path Parameters\n```typescript\n.get(''/user/:id'', ({ params: { id } }) => id)\n.get(''/post/:id/:slug'', ({ params }) => params)\n```\n\n### Query Parameters\n```typescript\n.get(''/search'', ({ query }) => query.q)\n// GET /search?q=elysia → \"elysia\"\n```\n\n### Request Body\n```typescript\n.post(''/user'', ({ body }) => body)\n```\n\n### Headers\n```typescript\n.get(''/'', ({ headers }) => headers.authorization)\n```\n\n## TypeBox Validation\n\n### Basic Types\n```typescript\nimport { Elysia, t } from ''elysia''\n\n.post(''/user'', ({ body }) => body, {\n  body: t.Object({\n    name: t.String(),\n    age: t.Number(),\n    email: t.String({ format: ''email'' }),\n    website: t.Optional(t.String({ format: ''uri'' }))\n  })\n})\n```\n\n### Nested Objects\n```typescript\nbody: t.Object({\n  user: t.Object({\n    name: t.String(),\n    address: t.Object({\n      street: t.String(),\n      city: t.String()\n    })\n  })\n})\n```\n\n### Arrays\n```typescript\nbody: t.Object({\n  tags: t.Array(t.String()),\n  users: t.Array(t.Object({\n    id: t.String(),\n    name: t.String()\n  }))\n})\n```\n\n### File Upload\n```typescript\n.post(''/upload'', ({ body }) => body.file, {\n  body: t.Object({\n    file: t.File({\n      type: ''image'',              // image/* mime types\n      maxSize: ''5m''               // 5 megabytes\n    }),\n    files: t.Files({              // Multiple files\n      type: [''image/png'', ''image/jpeg'']\n    })\n  })\n})\n```\n\n### Response Validation\n```typescript\n.get(''/user/:id'', ({ params: { id } }) => ({\n  id,\n  name: ''John'',\n  email: ''john@example.com''\n}), {\n  params: t.Object({\n    id: t.Number()\n  }),\n  response: {\n    200: t.Object({\n      id: t.Number(),\n      name: t.String(),\n      email: t.String()\n    }),\n    404: t.String()\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## Standard Schema (Zod, Valibot, ArkType)\n\n### Zod\n```typescript\nimport { z } from ''zod''\n\n.post(''/user'', ({ body }) => body, {\n  body: z.object({\n    name: z.string(),\n    age: z.number().min(0),\n    email: z.string().email()\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\n.get(''/user/:id'', ({ params: { id }, status }) => {\n  const user = findUser(id)\n  \n  if (!user) {\n    return status(404, ''User not found'')\n  }\n  \n  return user\n})\n```\n\n## Guards (Apply to Multiple Routes)\n\n```typescript\n.guard({\n  params: t.Object({\n    id: t.Number()\n  })\n}, app => app\n  .get(''/user/:id'', ({ params: { id } }) => id)\n  .delete(''/user/:id'', ({ params: { id } }) => id)\n)\n```\n\n## Macro\n\n```typescript\n.macro({\n  hi: (word: string) => ({\n    beforeHandle() { console.log(word) }\n  })\n})\n.get(''/'', () => ''hi'', { hi: ''Elysia'' })\n```\n\n### Project Structure (Recommended)\nElysia takes an unopinionated approach but based on user request. But without any specific preference, we recommend a feature-based and domain driven folder structure where each feature has its own folder containing controllers, services, and models.\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── index.ts              # Main server entry\n├── modules/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   ├── index.ts      # Auth routes (Elysia instance)\n│   │   ├── service.ts    # Business logic\n│   │   └── model.ts      # TypeBox schemas/DTOs\n│   └── user/\n│       ├── index.ts\n│       ├── service.ts\n│       └── model.ts\n└── plugins/\n    └── custom.ts\n\npublic/                   # Static files (if using static plugin)\ntest/                     # Unit tests\n```\n\nEach file has its own responsibility as follows:\n- **Controller (index.ts)**: Handle HTTP routing, request validation, and cookie.\n- **Service (service.ts)**: Handle business logic, decoupled from Elysia controller if possible.\n- **Model (model.ts)**: Define the data structure and validation for the request and response.\n\n## Best Practice\nElysia is unopinionated on design pattern, but if not provided, we can relies on MVC pattern pair with feature based folder structure.\n\n- Controller:\n\t- Prefers Elysia as a controller for HTTP dependant controller\n\t- For non HTTP dependent, prefers service instead unless explicitly asked\n\t- Use `onError` to handle local custom errors\n\t- Register Model to Elysia instance via `Elysia.models({ ...models })` and prefix model by namespace `Elysia.prefix(''model'', ''Namespace.'')\n\t- Prefers Reference Model by name provided by Elysia instead of using an actual `Model.name`\n- Service:\n\t- Prefers class (or abstract class if possible)\n\t- Prefers interface/type derive from `Model`\n\t- Return `status` (`import { status } from ''elysia''`) for error\n\t- Prefers `return Error` instead of `throw Error`\n- Models:\n\t- Always export validation model and type of validation model\n\t- Custom Error should be in contains in Model\n\n## Elysia Key Concept\nElysia has a every important concepts/rules to understand before use.\n\n## Encapsulation - Isolates by Default\n\nLifecycles (hooks, middleware) **don''t leak** between instances unless scoped.\n\n**Scope levels:**\n- `local` (default) - current instance + descendants\n- `scoped` - parent + current + descendants  \n- `global` - all instances\n\n```ts\n.onBeforeHandle(() => {}) // only local instance\n.onBeforeHandle({ as: ''global'' }, () => {}) // exports to all\n```\n\n## Method Chaining - Required for Types\n\n**Must chain**. Each method returns new type reference.\n\n❌ Don''t:\n```ts\nconst app = new Elysia()\napp.state(''build'', 1) // loses type\napp.get(''/'', ({ store }) => store.build) // build doesn''t exists\n```\n\n✅ Do:\n```ts\nnew Elysia()\n  .state(''build'', 1)\n  .get(''/'', ({ store }) => store.build)\n```\n\n## Explicit Dependencies\n\nEach instance independent. **Declare what you use.**\n\n```ts\nconst auth = new Elysia()\n\t.decorate(''Auth'', Auth)\n\t.model(Auth.models)\n\nnew Elysia()\n  .get(''/'', ({ Auth }) => Auth.getProfile()) // Auth doesn''t exists\n\nnew Elysia()\n  .use(auth) // must declare\n  .get(''/'', ({ Auth }) => Auth.getProfile())\n```\n\n**Global scope when:**\n- No types added (cors, helmet)\n- Global lifecycle (logging, tracing)\n\n**Explicit when:**\n- Adds types (state, models)\n- Business logic (auth, db)\n\n## Deduplication\n\nPlugins re-execute unless named:\n\n```ts\nnew Elysia() // rerun on `.use`\nnew Elysia({ name: ''ip'' }) // runs once across all instances\n```\n\n## Order Matters\n\nEvents apply to routes **registered after** them.\n\n```ts\n.onBeforeHandle(() => console.log(''1''))\n.get(''/'', () => ''hi'') // has hook\n.onBeforeHandle(() => console.log(''2'')) // doesn''t affect ''/''\n```\n\n## Type Inference\n\n**Inline functions only** for accurate types.\n\nFor controllers, destructure in inline wrapper:\n\n```ts\n.post(''/'', ({ body }) => Controller.greet(body), {\n  body: t.Object({ name: t.String() })\n})\n```\n\nGet type from schema:\n```ts\ntype MyType = typeof MyType.static\n```\n\n## Reference Model\nModel can be reference by name, especially great for documenting an API\n```ts\nnew Elysia()\n\t.model({\n\t\tbook: t.Object({\n\t\t\tname: t.String()\n\t\t})\n\t})\n\t.post(''/'', ({ body }) => body.name, {\n\t\tbody: ''book''\n\t})\n```\n\nModel can be renamed by using `.prefix` / `.suffix`\n```ts\nnew Elysia()\n\t.model({\n\t\tbook: t.Object({\n\t\t\tname: t.String()\n\t\t})\n\t})\n\t.prefix(''model'', ''Namespace'')\n\t.post(''/'', ({ body }) => body.name, {\n\t\tbody: ''Namespace.Book''\n\t})\n```\n\nOnce `prefix`, model name will be capitalized by default.\n\n## Technical Terms\nThe following are technical terms that is use for Elysia:\n- `OpenAPI Type Gen` - function name `fromTypes` from `@elysiajs/openapi` for generating OpenAPI from types, see `plugins/openapi.md`\n- `Eden`, `Eden Treaty` - e2e type safe RPC client for share type from backend to frontend\n\n## Resources\nUse the following references as needed.\n\nIt''s recommended to checkout `route.md` for as it contains the most important foundation building blocks with examples.\n\n`plugin.md` and `validation.md` is important as well but can be check as needed.\n\n### references/\nDetailed documentation split by topic:\n- `bun-fullstack-dev-server.md` - Bun Fullstack Dev Server with HMR. React without bundler.\n- `cookie.md` - Detailed documentation on cookie\n- `deployment.md` - Production deployment guide / Docker\n- `eden.md` - e2e type safe RPC client for share type from backend to frontend\n- `guard.md` - Setting validation/lifecycle all at once\n- `macro.md` - Compose multiple schema/lifecycle as a reusable Elysia via key-value (recommended for complex setup, eg. authentication, authorization, Role-based Access Check)\n- `plugin.md` - Decouple part of Elysia into a standalone component\n- `route.md` - Elysia foundation building block: Routing, Handler and Context\n- `testing.md` - Unit tests with examples\n- `validation.md` - Setup input/output validation and list of all custom validation rules\n- `websocket.md` - Real-time features\n\n### plugins/ \nDetailed documentation, usage and configuration reference for official Elysia plugin:\n- `bearer.md` - Add bearer capability to Elysia (`@elysiajs/bearer`)\n- `cors.md` - Out of box configuration for CORS (`@elysiajs/cors`)\n- `cron.md` - Run cron job with access to Elysia context (`@elysiajs/cron`)\n- `graphql-apollo.md` - Integration GraphQL Apollo (`@elysiajs/graphql-apollo`)\n- `graphql-yoga.md` - Integration with GraphQL Yoga (`@elysiajs/graphql-yoga`)\n- `html.md` - HTML and JSX plugin setup and usage (`@elysiajs/html`)\n- `jwt.md` - JWT / JWK plugin (`@elysiajs/jwt`)\n- `openapi.md` - OpenAPI documentation and OpenAPI Type Gen / OpenAPI from types (`@elysiajs/openapi`)\n- `opentelemetry.md` - OpenTelemetry, instrumentation, and record span utilities (`@elysiajs/opentelemetry`)\n- `server-timing.md` - Server Timing metric for debug (`@elysiajs/server-timing`) \n- `static.md` - Serve static files/folders for Elysia Server (`@elysiajs/static`)\n\n### integrations/\nGuide to integrate Elysia with external library/runtime:\n- `ai-sdk.md` - Using Vercel AI SDK with Elysia\n- `astro.md` - Elysia in Astro API route\n- `better-auth.md` - Integrate Elysia with better-auth\n- `cloudflare-worker.md` - Elysia on Cloudflare Worker adapter\n- `deno.md` - Elysia on Deno\n- `drizzle.md` - Integrate Elysia with Drizzle ORM\n- `expo.md` - Elysia in Expo API route\n- `nextjs.md` - Elysia in Nextjs API route\n- `nodejs.md` - Run Elysia on Node.js\n- `nuxt.md` - Elysia on API route\n- `prisma.md` - Integrate Elysia with Prisma\n- `react-email.d` - Create and Send Email with React and Elysia\n- `sveltekit.md` - Run Elysia on Svelte Kit API route\n- `tanstack-start.md` - Run Elysia on Tanstack Start / React Query\n- `vercel.md` - Deploy Elysia to Vercel\n\n### examples/ (optional)\n- `basic.ts` - Basic Elysia example\n- `body-parser.ts` - Custom body parser example via `.onParse`\n- `complex.ts` - Comprehensive usage of Elysia server\n- `cookie.ts` - Setting cookie\n- `error.ts` - Error handling\n- `file.ts` - Returning local file from server\n- `guard.ts` - Setting mulitple validation schema and lifecycle\n- `map-response.ts` - Custom response mapper\n- `redirect.ts` - Redirect response\n- `rename.ts` - Rename context''s property \n- `schema.ts` - Setup validation\n- `state.ts` - Setup global state\n- `upload-file.ts` - File upload with validation\n- `websocket.ts` - Web Socket for realtime communication\n\n### patterns/ (optional)\n- `patterns/mvc.md` - Detail guideline for using Elysia with MVC patterns\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:51:34.276Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Backend Agents needing advanced TypeScript framework for building Bun-first type-safe, high-performance backend servers.","zh":"非常适合需要高级TypeScript框架来构建Bun-first类型安全、高性能后端服务器的后端代理。","ja":"バックエンドエージェントがTypeScriptフレームワークを使用してBun-firstタイプの安全で高性能なバックエンドサーバーを構築する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 TypeScript 프레임워크를 사용하여 Bun-first 형식의 안전하고 고성능 백엔드 서버를 구축하는 백엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Backend que necesitan un marco de trabajo avanzado de TypeScript para construir servidores de backend de tipo Bun-first, seguros y de alto rendimiento.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Backend qui ont besoin d''un framework TypeScript avancé pour construire des serveurs Backend de type Bun-first, sécurisés et à haute performance.","de":"Perfekt für Backend-Agents, die ein erweitertes TypeScript-Framework zum Aufbau von Bun-first-Typ, sicherer und hoher Leistung, Backend-Servern benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Backend que precisam de um framework TypeScript avançado para construir servidores de backend do tipo Bun-first, seguros e de alto desempenho.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Backend, которым требуется продвинутый фреймворк TypeScript для создания серверов backend первого типа Bun, безопасных и высокопроизводительных.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الخلفية الذين يحتاجون إلى إطار TypeScript متقدم لإنشاء خوادم خلفية من النوع الأول Bun، آمنة وذات أداء عالي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build with Elysia, including routing, validation, authentication, plugins, integrations, and deployment. It provides type-safe, high-performance backend servers using TypeScript framework.","zh":"赋予代理构建Elysia的能力，包括路由、验证、身份验证、插件、集成和部署。它提供使用TypeScript框架的类型安全、高性能后端服务器。","ja":"Elysiaを構築するエージェントを可能にし、ルーティング、バリデーション、認証、プラグイン、統合、デプロイなどを含みます。TypeScriptフレームワークを使用したタイプセーフで高性能なバックエンドサーバーを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 Elysia를 구축할 수 있도록 해주며, 라우팅, 검증, 인증, 플러그인, 통합, 배포 등을 포함합니다. TypeScript 프레임워크를 사용하여 형식이 안전하고 고성능인 백엔드 서버를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir con Elysia, incluyendo enrutamiento, validación, autenticación, plugins, integraciones y despliegue. Proporciona servidores de backend seguros y de alto rendimiento utilizando el framework de TypeScript.","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire avec Elysia, y compris le routage, la validation, l''authentification, les plugins, les intégrations et le déploiement. Il fournit des serveurs Backend sécurisés et à haute performance en utilisant le framework TypeScript.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, mit Elysia zu bauen, einschließlich Routing, Validierung, Authentifizierung, Plugins, Integrationen und Bereitstellung. Bietet sichere und hohe Leistung, Backend-Servern unter Verwendung des TypeScript-Frameworks.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir com Elysia, incluindo roteamento, validação, autenticação, plugins, integrações e implantação. Ele fornece servidores de backend seguros e de alto desempenho usando o framework TypeScript.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать с помощью Elysia, включая маршрутизацию, проверку, аутентификацию, плагины, интеграции и развертывание. Он обеспечивает безопасные и высокопроизводительные серверы backend, используя фреймворк TypeScript.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على بناء مع Elysia، بما في ذلك التوجيه والتحقق والتحقق من الصحة والبرامج الإضافية والتكامل والتشغيل. يوفر خوادم خلفية آمنة وذات أداء عالي باستخدام إطار TypeScript."},"useCases":{"en":["Building high-performance backend servers","Integrating plugins and integrations","Deploying Elysia applications"],"zh":["构建高性能后端服务器","集成插件和集成","部署Elysia应用"],"ja":["高性能バックエンドサーバーの構築","プラグインと統合の統合","Elysiaアプリケーションのデプロイ"],"ko":["고성능 백엔드 서버 구축","플러그인 및 통합 통합","Elysia 애플리케이션 배포"],"es":["Construir servidores de backend de alto rendimiento","Integrar plugins e integraciones","Desplegar aplicaciones Elysia"],"fr":["Construire des serveurs Backend à haute performance","Intégrer des plugins et des intégrations","Déployer des applications Elysia"],"de":["Aufbau von Backend-Servern mit hoher Leistung","Integration von Plugins und Integrationen","Bereitstellung von Elysia-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Construir servidores de backend de alto desempenho","Integrar plugins e integrações","Implantar aplicações Elysia"],"ru":["Создание высокопроизводительных серверов backend","Интеграция плагинов и интеграций","Развертывание приложений Elysia"],"ar":["بناء خوادم خلفية ذات أداء عالي","دمج البرامج الإضافية والتكامل","تشغيل تطبيقات Elysia"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires active database connection","Bun-first type of backend servers only"],"zh":["需要活动数据库连接","仅Bun-first类型的后端服务器"],"ja":["アクティブなデータベース接続が必要","Bun-firstタイプのバックエンドサーバーのみ"],"ko":["액티브 데이터베이스 연결이 필요","Bun-first 형식의 백엔드 서버만"],"es":["Requiere una conexión de base de datos activa","Solo servidores de backend de tipo Bun-first"],"fr":["Nécessite une connexion de base de données active","Seulement des serveurs Backend de type Bun-first"],"de":["Benötigt eine aktive Datenbankverbindung","Nur Backend-Server vom Typ Bun-first"],"pt":["Requer conexão de banco de dados ativa","Servidores de backend do tipo Bun-first apenas"],"ru":["Требуется активное подключение к базе данных","Только серверы backend первого типа Bun"],"ar":["يتطلب 